      </section>

      <!-- ==================================================================
           SUB-TOPIC 1.7 — LE FUTUR ANTÉRIEUR
           =================================================================== -->
      <section data-topic="verbes" data-topic-name="Les Verbes" data-sub="Le Futur Antérieur">

        <section data-slide-id="fa-1" data-step="Description">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">1</span> Description</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Le Futur Antérieur — "will have done"</h2>
            <p class="editable-field">This tense describes an action that <strong>will be finished before another future action</strong>. Two things lie ahead; this one finishes first.</p>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <p class="example-text">Quand tu <span class="highlight hl-aux">seras arrivé</span>, nous <span class="highlight hl-subject">dînerons</span>.</p>
              <p class="gloss">When you have arrived, we will have dinner.</p>
              <div class="formula-pipeline" style="margin-top:10px;">
                <div class="f-box" style="border-color:var(--green);"><span class="f-label">Maintenant</span><span class="f-value" style="color:var(--green);">on attend</span></div>
                <div class="f-op">→</div>
                <div class="f-box" style="border-color:var(--gold);"><span class="f-label">1<sup>er</sup> dans le futur</span><span class="f-value" style="color:var(--gold);">tu seras arrivé</span></div>
                <div class="f-op">→</div>
                <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">2<sup>e</sup> dans le futur</span><span class="f-value">nous dînerons</span></div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">It can also express a <strong>supposition about the past</strong>:
              <em>Il n'est pas là — il <span class="highlight hl-aux">aura oublié</span> le rendez-vous.</em>
              <span class="gloss">He isn't here — he must have forgotten the appointment.</span></p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="fa-2" data-step="Formation">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">2</span> Formation</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">La formule — auxiliaire au FUTUR SIMPLE</h2>
            <div class="formula-pipeline">
              <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Sujet</span><span class="f-value">J'</span></div>
              <div class="f-op">+</div>
              <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">avoir / être au futur</span><span class="f-value">aurai / serai</span></div>
              <div class="f-op">+</div>
              <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Participe passé</span><span class="f-value">fini</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Avec AVOIR — finir</h3>
                <table class="subj-table">
                  <tr><td>j'</td><td class="key-form">aurai fini</td><td>nous</td><td class="key-form">aurons fini</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>tu</td><td class="key-form">auras fini</td><td>vous</td><td class="key-form">aurez fini</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>il/elle</td><td class="key-form">aura fini</td><td>ils/elles</td><td class="key-form">auront fini</td></tr>
                </table>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Avec ÊTRE — partir</h3>
                <table class="subj-table">
                  <tr><td>je</td><td class="key-form">serai parti(e)</td><td>nous</td><td class="key-form">serons parti(e)s</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>tu</td><td class="key-form">seras parti(e)</td><td>vous</td><td class="key-form">serez parti(e)(s)</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>il/elle</td><td class="key-form">sera parti(e)</td><td>ils/elles</td><td class="key-form">seront parti(e)s</td></tr>
                </table>
              </div>
            </div>
            <p class="editable-field gloss">Pattern to notice: <strong>PC</strong> = auxiliary in présent · <strong>PQP</strong> = auxiliary in imparfait · <strong>Futur antérieur</strong> = auxiliary in futur. Same participle every time.</p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="fa-3" data-step="Exceptions">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">3</span> Exceptions</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Les exceptions — nothing new, but check the agreement</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Same ÊTRE list</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Elle <span class="highlight hl-aux">sera</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">rentrée</span> avant huit heures. <span class="gloss">She will have come home before eight.</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Ils <span class="highlight hl-aux">seront</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">descendus</span> au premier étage. <span class="gloss">They will have gone down to the first floor.</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Nous <span class="highlight hl-aux">nous serons</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">levés</span> tôt. <span class="gloss">We will have got up early.</span></p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Irregular auxiliary stems</h3>
                <p>Because the auxiliary is in the futur, it uses the irregular futur stems:</p>
                <p>avoir → <span class="key-form">aur-</span> : j'aurai vu</p>
                <p>être → <span class="key-form">ser-</span> : je serai venu</p>
                <p class="gloss">These two are the only stems you ever need for this tense.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field"><strong>Négation:</strong> around the auxiliary only —
              <em>Je <span class="highlight hl-neg">n'</span><span class="highlight hl-aux">aurai</span> <span class="highlight hl-neg">pas</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">terminé</span> avant midi.</em>
              <span class="gloss">I will not have finished before noon.</span></p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="fa-4" data-step="Pièges">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">4</span> Pièges</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">⚠️ Trap Alert — which clause gets which tense?</h2>
            <p class="editable-field">After <em>quand, dès que, lorsque, aussitôt que, après que</em>, the <strong>earlier</strong> action takes the futur antérieur and the <strong>later</strong> one takes the futur simple.</p>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box green content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--green);">✓ Correct</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Dès que j'<span class="highlight hl-aux">aurai fini</span>, je <span class="highlight hl-subject">sortirai</span>.</p>
                <p class="gloss">As soon as I have finished, I will go out.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Quand elle <span class="highlight hl-aux">sera partie</span>, nous <span class="highlight hl-subject">fermerons</span>.</p>
                <p class="gloss">When she has left, we will close.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box red content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--crimson);">✗ Common errors</h3>
                <p class="example-text">✗ Dès que je <span class="highlight hl-neg">finirai</span>, je sortirai. <span class="gloss">both simple future — the order is lost</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">✗ Dès que j'<span class="highlight hl-neg">ai fini</span>, je sortirai. <span class="gloss">passé composé cannot point to the future</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">✗ Quand elle <span class="highlight hl-neg">sera parti</span>… <span class="gloss">missing feminine agreement</span></p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">💡 <strong>Rule of thumb:</strong> the clause with <em>quand / dès que</em> holds the action that finishes <strong>first</strong> → futur antérieur. The other clause → futur simple.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="fa-5" data-step="Exemples">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">5</span> Exemples travaillés</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Worked examples</h2>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <p class="example-text">J'<span class="highlight hl-aux">aurai terminé</span> mes examens en mai.</p>
              <p class="gloss">I will have finished my exams in May.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Quand vous <span class="highlight hl-aux">aurez lu</span> ce livre, vous <span class="highlight hl-subject">comprendrez</span> mieux.</p>
              <p class="gloss">When you have read this book, you will understand better.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Elles <span class="highlight hl-aux">seront</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">arrivées</span> avant la nuit.</p>
              <p class="gloss">They will have arrived before nightfall. — être + feminine plural agreement</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text"><span class="q-tag">CBSE 2022</span>Dès que l'acteur <span class="highlight hl-aux">sera revenu</span>, le réalisateur <span class="highlight hl-subject">racontera</span> l'histoire.</p>
              <p class="gloss">As soon as the actor has returned, the director will tell the story. — <em>revenir</em> = être</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="fa-6" data-step="En contexte">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">6</span> En contexte</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">In context — Entre Jeunes themes</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">L.2 — Après le bac</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Dans trois ans, j'<span class="highlight hl-aux">aurai obtenu</span> mon diplôme.</p>
                <p class="gloss">In three years I will have obtained my degree.</p>
                <h3>L.3 — Chercher du travail</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Quand tu <span class="highlight hl-aux">auras envoyé</span> ton CV, tu attendras la réponse.</p>
                <p class="gloss">When you have sent your CV, you will wait for the reply.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">L.8 — L'environnement</h3>
                <p class="example-text">En 2050, la température <span class="highlight hl-aux">aura augmenté</span> de deux degrés.</p>
                <p class="gloss">By 2050 the temperature will have risen by two degrees.</p>
                <h3 style="color:var(--gold);">L.6 — Chacun ses goûts</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Dès qu'ils <span class="highlight hl-aux">auront choisi</span> le film, ils réserveront les places.</p>
                <p class="gloss">As soon as they have chosen the film, they will book the seats.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">💡 Notice the English pattern: "<strong>will have</strong> + past participle", or after <em>when/as soon as</em>, simply "<strong>have</strong> + participle". Both map onto the French futur antérieur.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="fa-7" data-step="Pratique QCM">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">7</span> Pratique — QCM</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Choose the correct future perfect</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="sera revenu">
                <p class="q-text">1. <span class="q-tag">CBSE 2022</span>Dès que l'acteur _____, le réalisateur racontera l'histoire. <span class="gloss">(revenir)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">reviendra</button><button class="option-btn">sera revenu</button><button class="option-btn">est revenu</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="aurai fini">
                <p class="q-text">2. Quand j'_____, je te téléphonerai. <span class="gloss">(finir)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">aurai fini</button><button class="option-btn">finirai</button><button class="option-btn">avais fini</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="seront arrivées">
                <p class="q-text">3. Elles _____ avant midi. <span class="gloss">(arriver)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">auront arrivé</button><button class="option-btn">seront arrivées</button><button class="option-btn">seront arrivés</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="aurons mangé">
                <p class="q-text">4. Nous _____ quand tu rentreras. <span class="gloss">(manger)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">aurons mangé</button><button class="option-btn">mangerons</button><button class="option-btn">serons mangés</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="n'aura pas terminé">
                <p class="q-text">5. Il _____ le travail avant ce soir. <span class="gloss">(ne pas terminer)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">n'aura pas terminé</button><button class="option-btn">n'aura terminé pas</button><button class="option-btn">ne sera pas terminé</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="fa-8" data-step="Pratique — à compléter">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">8</span> Pratique — à compléter</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Write the futur antérieur</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">1. Quand tu _____ (arriver), nous commencerons.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="seras arrivé|seras arrivée|seras arrivé(e)" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">2. J'_____ (écrire) la lettre avant ce soir.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="aurai écrit" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">3. Dès qu'ils _____ (partir), je rangerai la salle.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="seront partis" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">4. Vous _____ (comprendre) la règle après cet exercice.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="aurez compris" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">5. Elle _____ (se lever) avant le lever du soleil.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="se sera levée" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="accent-bar">
                <span class="ab-label">Accents :</span>
                <button class="accent-key">é</button><button class="accent-key">è</button><button class="accent-key">ê</button>
                <button class="accent-key">à</button><button class="accent-key">ç</button><button class="accent-key">ù</button>
                <button class="accent-key">û</button><button class="accent-key">î</button><button class="accent-key">ô</button>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn fib-check student-only">✓ Vérifier</button>
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </section>
      <!-- ==================================================================
           SUB-TOPIC 1.8 — LE CONDITIONNEL PRÉSENT
           =================================================================== -->
      <section data-topic="verbes" data-topic-name="Les Verbes" data-sub="Le Conditionnel Présent">

        <section data-slide-id="cond-1" data-step="Description">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">1</span> Description</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Le Conditionnel Présent — "would"</h2>
            <p class="editable-field">The conditionnel expresses what <strong>would</strong> happen — under a condition, as a wish, or simply to sound polite.</p>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Use it for…</h3>
                <p>① <strong>Politeness</strong> — <span class="example-text">Je <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">voudrais</span> un café, s'il vous plaît.</span> <span class="gloss">I would like a coffee, please.</span></p>
                <p>② <strong>Wishes</strong> — <span class="example-text">J'<span class="highlight hl-pronoun">aimerais</span> visiter la France.</span> <span class="gloss">I would like to visit France.</span></p>
                <p>③ <strong>Hypothesis</strong> — <span class="example-text">Si j'avais le temps, je <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">lirais</span> plus.</span> <span class="gloss">If I had time, I would read more.</span></p>
                <p>④ <strong>Advice</strong> — <span class="example-text">Tu <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">devrais</span> te reposer.</span> <span class="gloss">You should rest.</span></p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Why politeness matters in the exam</h3>
                <p>Compare the two registers:</p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-neg">Je veux</span> un stylo. <span class="gloss">I want a pen. — blunt, almost rude</span></p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-verb">Je voudrais</span> un stylo. <span class="gloss">I would like a pen. — polite</span></p>
                <p class="gloss">In dialogues and letters, the conditionnel is what makes you sound courteous. Examiners notice.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="cond-2" data-step="Formation">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">2</span> Formation</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">La formule — radical du FUTUR + terminaisons de l'IMPARFAIT</h2>
            <div class="formula-pipeline">
              <div class="f-box" style="border-color:var(--gold);"><span class="f-label">Radical du futur</span><span class="f-value" style="color:var(--gold);">parler-</span></div>
              <div class="f-op">+</div>
              <div class="f-box" style="border-color:var(--purple);"><span class="f-label">Terminaisons de l'imparfait</span><span class="f-value" style="color:var(--purple);">-ais -ais -ait -ions -iez -aient</span></div>
              <div class="f-op">=</div>
              <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Conditionnel</span><span class="f-value">je parlerais</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">parler</h3>
                <table class="subj-table">
                  <tr><td>je</td><td class="key-form">parlerais</td><td>nous</td><td class="key-form">parlerions</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>tu</td><td class="key-form">parlerais</td><td>vous</td><td class="key-form">parleriez</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>il/elle</td><td class="key-form">parlerait</td><td>ils/elles</td><td class="key-form">parleraient</td></tr>
                </table>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">The two halves you already know</h3>
                <p>You do not learn anything new here:</p>
                <p>✔ the <strong>stem</strong> is the futur simple stem</p>
                <p>✔ the <strong>endings</strong> are the imparfait endings</p>
                <p class="example-text">finir → finir<span class="highlight hl-pronoun">ais</span> · vendre → vendr<span class="highlight hl-pronoun">ais</span></p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="cond-3" data-step="Exceptions">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">3</span> Exceptions</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Les mêmes radicaux irréguliers que le futur</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <table class="subj-table">
                  <tr><th>Infinitif</th><th>Radical</th><th>Conditionnel</th></tr>
                  <tr><td>être</td><td>ser-</td><td class="key-form">je serais</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>avoir</td><td>aur-</td><td class="key-form">j'aurais</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>aller</td><td>ir-</td><td class="key-form">j'irais</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>faire</td><td>fer-</td><td class="key-form">je ferais</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>pouvoir</td><td>pourr-</td><td class="key-form">je pourrais</td></tr>
                </table>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <table class="subj-table">
                  <tr><th>Infinitif</th><th>Radical</th><th>Conditionnel</th></tr>
                  <tr><td>vouloir</td><td>voudr-</td><td class="key-form">je voudrais</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>devoir</td><td>devr-</td><td class="key-form">je devrais</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>savoir</td><td>saur-</td><td class="key-form">je saurais</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>venir</td><td>viendr-</td><td class="key-form">je viendrais</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>voir</td><td>verr-</td><td class="key-form">je verrais</td></tr>
                </table>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field"><strong>The three most useful polite forms</strong> — memorise them as fixed phrases:
                <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">je voudrais</span> <span class="gloss">I would like</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">pourriez-vous…?</span> <span class="gloss">could you…?</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">tu devrais</span> <span class="gloss">you should</span></p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="cond-4" data-step="Pièges">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">4</span> Pièges</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">⚠️ Trap Alert — the SI rule, and -ai vs -ais</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box green content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--green);">✓ Si + imparfait → conditionnel</h3>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-aux">Si</span> j'<span class="highlight hl-aux">avais</span> de l'argent, je <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">voyagerais</span>.</p>
                <p class="gloss">If I had money, I would travel.</p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-aux">Si</span> tu <span class="highlight hl-aux">venais</span>, nous <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">serions</span> contents.</p>
                <p class="gloss">If you came, we would be happy.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box red content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--crimson);">✗ Never conditionnel after SI</h3>
                <p class="example-text">✗ Si j'<span class="highlight hl-neg">aurais</span> de l'argent…</p>
                <p class="example-text">✗ Si tu <span class="highlight hl-neg">viendrais</span>…</p>
                <p class="gloss">The <em>si</em> clause never takes -rais. This is one of the most penalised errors in the paper.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">One letter changes the tense</h3>
              <table class="subj-table">
                <tr><th></th><th>Futur</th><th>Conditionnel</th></tr>
                <tr><td>je</td><td class="key-form">parlerai</td><td class="key-form">parlerais</td></tr>
                <tr><td>meaning</td><td>I will speak</td><td>I would speak</td></tr>
              </table>
              <p class="gloss">Futur <strong>-ai</strong> (one letter) · Conditionnel <strong>-ais</strong> (with s). Read the sentence: "will" or "would"?</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="cond-5" data-step="Exemples">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">5</span> Exemples travaillés</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Worked examples</h2>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <p class="example-text">Je <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">voudrais</span> réserver une table pour deux personnes.</p>
              <p class="gloss">I would like to book a table for two. — polite request</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-pronoun">Pourriez</span>-vous m'aider, s'il vous plaît ?</p>
              <p class="gloss">Could you help me, please? — pouvoir → pourr-</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Si nous avions plus de temps, nous <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">visiterions</span> le musée.</p>
              <p class="gloss">If we had more time, we would visit the museum. — si + imparfait, then conditionnel</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">À ta place, je <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">ferais</span> plus attention en classe.</p>
              <p class="gloss">In your place, I would pay more attention in class. — faire → fer-, giving advice</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="cond-6" data-step="En contexte">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">6</span> En contexte</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">In context — being polite and giving advice</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">L.3 — Chercher du travail</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Je <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">souhaiterais</span> poser ma candidature à ce poste.</p>
                <p class="gloss">I would like to apply for this position. — formal letter register</p>
                <h3>L.2 — Après le bac</h3>
                <p class="example-text">À ta place, je <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">choisirais</span> les sciences.</p>
                <p class="gloss">In your place, I would choose science.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">L.7 — En pleine forme</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Tu <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">devrais</span> manger moins de sucre.</p>
                <p class="gloss">You should eat less sugar.</p>
                <h3 style="color:var(--gold);">L.8 — L'environnement</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Si tout le monde recyclait, la ville <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">serait</span> plus propre.</p>
                <p class="gloss">If everyone recycled, the city would be cleaner.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">💡 <strong>Advice-letter formula:</strong> mix impératif and conditionnel —
              <em><span class="highlight hl-verb">Fais</span> du sport ! Et à ta place, je <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">dormirais</span> plus tôt.</em>
              The conditionnel softens the advice so it doesn't sound like an order.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="cond-7" data-step="Pratique QCM">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">7</span> Pratique — QCM</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Choose the correct conditional</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="voudrais">
                <p class="q-text">1. Je _____ un thé, s'il vous plaît. <span class="gloss">(vouloir)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">veux</button><button class="option-btn">voudrais</button><button class="option-btn">voudrai</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="avais">
                <p class="q-text">2. Si j'_____ le temps, je viendrais. <span class="gloss">(avoir)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">aurais</button><button class="option-btn">avais</button><button class="option-btn">aurai</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="serions">
                <p class="q-text">3. Nous _____ ravis de vous rencontrer. <span class="gloss">(être)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">serons</button><button class="option-btn">serions</button><button class="option-btn">étions</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="devrais">
                <p class="q-text">4. Tu _____ réviser avant l'examen. <span class="gloss">(devoir)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">devrais</button><button class="option-btn">devras</button><button class="option-btn">dois</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="irions">
                <p class="q-text">5. S'il faisait beau, nous _____ à la plage. <span class="gloss">(aller)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">irons</button><button class="option-btn">allions</button><button class="option-btn">irions</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="cond-8" data-step="Pratique — à compléter">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">8</span> Pratique — à compléter</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Write the conditionnel présent</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">1. _____ (pouvoir)-vous m'indiquer la gare ?</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="pourriez" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">2. Si tu travaillais plus, tu _____ (réussir).</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="réussirais" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">3. Ils _____ (aimer) partir en vacances en juillet.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="aimeraient" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">4. Elle _____ (savoir) répondre à cette question.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="saurait" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">5. Nous _____ (faire) le travail si c'était possible.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="ferions" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="accent-bar">
                <span class="ab-label">Accents :</span>
                <button class="accent-key">é</button><button class="accent-key">è</button><button class="accent-key">ê</button>
                <button class="accent-key">à</button><button class="accent-key">ç</button><button class="accent-key">ù</button>
                <button class="accent-key">û</button><button class="accent-key">î</button><button class="accent-key">ô</button>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn fib-check student-only">✓ Vérifier</button>
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </section>

      <!-- ==================================================================
           SUB-TOPIC 1.9 — LES VERBES PRONOMINAUX
           =================================================================== -->
      <section data-topic="verbes" data-topic-name="Les Verbes" data-sub="Les Verbes Pronominaux">

        <section data-slide-id="pron-1" data-step="Description">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">1</span> Description</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Les Verbes Pronominaux — the subject acts on itself</h2>
            <p class="editable-field">A pronominal verb always carries an extra pronoun that <strong>refers back to the subject</strong>: <em>se laver</em> = to wash <em>oneself</em>.</p>
            <div class="three-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">① Réfléchis</h3>
                <p>The action returns to the subject.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Je <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">me</span> lave. <span class="gloss">I wash myself.</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Elle <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">se</span> regarde. <span class="gloss">She looks at herself.</span></p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">② Réciproques</h3>
                <p>Two or more people, "each other".</p>
                <p class="example-text">Ils <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">se</span> parlent. <span class="gloss">They talk to each other.</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Nous <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">nous</span> rencontrons. <span class="gloss">We meet each other.</span></p>
              </div>
              <div class="box green content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--green);">③ Essentiellement pronominaux</h3>
                <p>They only exist with the pronoun.</p>
                <p class="example-text">se souvenir <span class="gloss">to remember</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">s'en aller <span class="gloss">to go away</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">se moquer <span class="gloss">to make fun of</span></p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field"><strong>Daily-routine verbs you will use constantly:</strong>
                se lever, se laver, s'habiller, se brosser (les dents), se coucher, se réveiller, se dépêcher, se reposer, s'amuser, se promener.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="pron-2" data-step="Formation">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">2</span> Formation</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">La formule — pronom réfléchi + verbe</h2>
            <div class="formula-pipeline">
              <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Sujet</span><span class="f-value">Je</span></div>
              <div class="f-op">+</div>
              <div class="f-box" style="border-color:var(--purple);"><span class="f-label">Pronom réfléchi</span><span class="f-value" style="color:var(--purple);">me / te / se / nous / vous / se</span></div>
              <div class="f-op">+</div>
              <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Verbe conjugué</span><span class="f-value">lève</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">SE LEVER — présent</h3>
                <table class="subj-table">
                  <tr><td>je</td><td class="key-form">me lève</td><td>nous</td><td class="key-form">nous levons</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>tu</td><td class="key-form">te lèves</td><td>vous</td><td class="key-form">vous levez</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>il/elle</td><td class="key-form">se lève</td><td>ils/elles</td><td class="key-form">se lèvent</td></tr>
                </table>
                <p class="gloss">Note the è in je/tu/il/ils — <em>lever</em> is a stem-changing verb.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">The pronoun must match the subject</h3>
                <p>✗ <em>Je <span class="highlight hl-neg">se</span> lève</em> &nbsp;→&nbsp; ✓ Je <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">me</span> lève</p>
                <p>✗ <em>Nous <span class="highlight hl-neg">se</span> levons</em> &nbsp;→&nbsp; ✓ Nous <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">nous</span> levons</p>
                <p><strong>Before a vowel:</strong> me → m', te → t', se → s'</p>
                <p class="example-text">Je <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">m'</span>appelle Ravi. Il <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">s'</span>habille vite. <span class="gloss">My name is Ravi. He gets dressed quickly.</span></p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="pron-3" data-step="Exceptions">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">3</span> Exceptions</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Aux autres temps — et l'accord</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Passé composé — TOUJOURS être</h3>
                <table class="subj-table">
                  <tr><td>je</td><td class="key-form">me suis levé(e)</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>tu</td><td class="key-form">t'es levé(e)</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>il/elle</td><td class="key-form">s'est levé(e)</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>nous</td><td class="key-form">nous sommes levé(e)s</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>vous</td><td class="key-form">vous êtes levé(e)(s)</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>ils/elles</td><td class="key-form">se sont levé(e)s</td></tr>
                </table>
                <p class="gloss">There is no pronominal verb that takes <em>avoir</em>.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Impératif — the pronoun moves</h3>
                <p><strong>Affirmatif</strong> — after, hyphen, me→moi, te→toi:</p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-verb">Lève-toi</span> ! · <span class="highlight hl-verb">Levons-nous</span> ! · <span class="highlight hl-verb">Levez-vous</span> ! <span class="gloss">Get up! · Let's get up! · Get up! (polite/plural)</span></p>
                <p><strong>Négatif</strong> — before, no hyphen:</p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-neg">Ne</span> <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">te</span> lève <span class="highlight hl-neg">pas</span> ! <span class="gloss">Don't get up!</span></p>
                <p><strong>Infinitif</strong> — the pronoun still matches the subject:</p>
                <p class="example-text">Je vais <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">me</span> coucher. Tu veux <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">te</span> reposer ? <span class="gloss">I'm going to bed. Do you want to rest?</span></p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field"><strong>Accord au passé composé:</strong> the participle agrees with the reflexive pronoun when that pronoun is the <em>direct</em> object —
                <em>Elle s'est <span class="highlight hl-verb">lavée</span></em>.
                But if a direct object <strong>follows</strong> the verb, there is no agreement —
                <em>Elle s'est <span class="highlight hl-verb">lavé</span> les mains.</em>
                <span class="gloss">She washed her hands.</span></p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="pron-4" data-step="Pièges">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">4</span> Pièges</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">⚠️ Trap Alert — four classic mistakes</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box red content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--crimson);">✗ Wrong</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Nous <span class="highlight hl-neg">avons</span> nous levés.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Elle s'est <span class="highlight hl-neg">levé</span>.</p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-neg">Ne lève-toi pas</span> !</p>
                <p class="example-text">Je vais <span class="highlight hl-neg">se</span> coucher.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box green content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--green);">✓ Right</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Nous <span class="highlight hl-aux">nous sommes</span> levés. <span class="gloss">always être</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Elle s'est <span class="highlight hl-verb">levée</span>. <span class="gloss">feminine agreement</span></p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-verb">Ne te lève pas</span> ! <span class="gloss">negative → pronoun before</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Je vais <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">me</span> coucher. <span class="gloss">pronoun matches the subject</span></p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field"><strong>Meaning changes without the pronoun:</strong><br>
                <em>Je <span class="highlight hl-verb">lave</span> la voiture.</em> <span class="gloss">I wash the car.</span> &nbsp;·&nbsp;
                <em>Je <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">me</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">lave</span>.</em> <span class="gloss">I wash myself.</span><br>
                <em>Elle <span class="highlight hl-verb">demande</span> l'heure.</em> <span class="gloss">She asks the time.</span> &nbsp;·&nbsp;
                <em>Elle <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">se</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">demande</span>…</em> <span class="gloss">She wonders…</span></p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="pron-5" data-step="Exemples">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">5</span> Exemples travaillés</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Worked examples</h2>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-subject">Je</span> <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">me</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">réveille</span> à six heures et demie.</p>
              <p class="gloss">I wake up at half past six. — présent, pronoun matches <em>je</em></p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-subject">Elles</span> <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">se</span> <span class="highlight hl-aux">sont</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">dépêchées</span> pour prendre le bus.</p>
              <p class="gloss">They hurried to catch the bus. — PC with être + feminine plural</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-neg">Ne</span> <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">vous</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">inquiétez</span> <span class="highlight hl-neg">pas</span>, tout ira bien.</p>
              <p class="gloss">Don't worry, everything will be fine. — negative imperative</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Quand j'étais petit, je <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">m'</span><span class="highlight hl-aux">amusais</span> avec mes cousins.</p>
              <p class="gloss">When I was little, I used to have fun with my cousins. — imparfait</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="pron-6" data-step="En contexte">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">6</span> En contexte</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">In context — describing a daily routine</h2>
            <p class="editable-field gloss">"Une journée typique" is a recurring CBSE writing task — it is built almost entirely from pronominal verbs.</p>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Le matin</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Je <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">me</span> réveille à 6 h, puis je <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">me</span> lève.</p>
                <p class="gloss">I wake up at 6, then I get up.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Je <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">me</span> brosse les dents et je <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">m'</span>habille.</p>
                <p class="gloss">I brush my teeth and I get dressed.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Le soir — L.7 En pleine forme</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Après le dîner, je <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">me</span> repose un peu.</p>
                <p class="gloss">After dinner, I rest a little.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Je <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">me</span> couche vers dix heures pour être en forme.</p>
                <p class="gloss">I go to bed around ten to stay healthy.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">💡 <strong>Exam tip:</strong> link your routine with <em>d'abord, ensuite, puis, enfin</em>
              <span class="gloss">first, then, next, finally</span> — sequencing words earn marks for coherence.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="pron-7" data-step="Pratique QCM">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">7</span> Pratique — QCM</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Choose the correct pronominal form</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="me couche">
                <p class="q-text">1. <span class="q-tag">CBSE 2022</span>Je veux _____ tôt ce soir. <span class="gloss">(se coucher)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">se coucher</button><button class="option-btn">me coucher</button><button class="option-btn">me couche</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="nous sommes levés">
                <p class="q-text">2. Nous _____ à cinq heures ce matin. <span class="gloss">(se lever, PC)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">avons levé</button><button class="option-btn">nous sommes levés</button><button class="option-btn">nous avons levés</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="s'appelle">
                <p class="q-text">3. Ma sœur _____ Anjali. <span class="gloss">(s'appeler)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">se appelle</button><button class="option-btn">s'appelle</button><button class="option-btn">s'appèle</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="Dépêche-toi">
                <p class="q-text">4. _____, nous sommes en retard ! <span class="gloss">(se dépêcher — tu)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">Dépêche-toi</button><button class="option-btn">Te dépêche</button><button class="option-btn">Dépêche-te</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="se sont rencontrées">
                <p class="q-text">5. <span class="q-tag">CBSE 2022</span>L'année dernière, elles _____ dans la rue. <span class="gloss">(se rencontrer, PC)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">se sont rencontré</button><button class="option-btn">se sont rencontrées</button><button class="option-btn">ont se rencontrées</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="pron-8" data-step="Pratique — à compléter">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">8</span> Pratique — à compléter</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Write the pronominal form</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">1. Tous les matins, je _____ (se réveiller) à six heures.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="me réveille" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">2. Hier, elle _____ (se promener) dans le parc.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="s'est promenée" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">3. Comment _____ (s'appeler)-vous ?</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="vous appelez" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">4. Nous _____ (se souvenir) de ce voyage.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="nous souvenons" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">5. Quand j'étais enfant, je _____ (s'amuser) beaucoup.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="m'amusais" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="accent-bar">
                <span class="ab-label">Accents :</span>
                <button class="accent-key">é</button><button class="accent-key">è</button><button class="accent-key">ê</button>
                <button class="accent-key">à</button><button class="accent-key">ç</button><button class="accent-key">ù</button>
                <button class="accent-key">û</button><button class="accent-key">î</button><button class="accent-key">ô</button>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn fib-check student-only">✓ Vérifier</button>
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
