      </section>
      <!-- ==================================================================
           SUB-TOPIC 1.10 — LA NOMINALISATION (under Les Verbes)
           =================================================================== -->
      <section data-topic="verbes" data-topic-name="Les Verbes" data-sub="La Nominalisation">

        <!-- 1 · CONCEPT + SUFFIX RULES -->
        <section data-slide-id="nom-1" data-step="Suffix Rules">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">1</span> Suffix Rules</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">La Nominalisation — turning a verb into a noun</h2>
            <p class="editable-field">Nominalisation means building a <strong>noun</strong> from a <strong>verb</strong>. It is how newspaper headlines and formal writing become compact: <em>« Le président visite… »</em> → <em>« Visite du président… »</em>.</p>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">The five key suffixes</h3>
                <table class="subj-table">
                  <tr><th>Suffix</th><th>Verb → Noun</th></tr>
                  <tr><td class="key-form">-tion</td><td>créer → <strong>la création</strong></td></tr>
                  <tr><td class="key-form">-ment</td><td>changer → <strong>le changement</strong></td></tr>
                  <tr><td class="key-form">-age</td><td>laver → <strong>le lavage</strong></td></tr>
                  <tr><td class="key-form">-ure</td><td>ouvrir → <strong>l'ouverture</strong></td></tr>
                  <tr><td class="key-form">-ée</td><td>arriver → <strong>l'arrivée</strong></td></tr>
                </table>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">More you will meet</h3>
                <p><span class="key-form">-sion / -ssion</span> — décider → <strong>la décision</strong>, discuter → <strong>la discussion</strong></p>
                <p><span class="key-form">-ance / -ence</span> — assister → <strong>l'assistance</strong>, exister → <strong>l'existence</strong></p>
                <p class="gloss">Most abstract-idea suffixes (-tion, -sion, -ance, -ence, -ure, -ée) are <strong>feminine</strong>. The two big masculine ones are <strong>-ment</strong> and <strong>-age</strong>.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- 2 · GENDER PATTERNS -->
        <section data-slide-id="nom-2" data-step="Gender Patterns">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">2</span> Gender Patterns</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Masculine or feminine? Let the suffix tell you</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">➡️ Masculine (le / l')</h3>
                <p><span class="key-form">-ment</span> — le gouvernement, le développement, le mouvement</p>
                <p><span class="key-form">-age</span> — le passage, le voyage, le nettoyage</p>
                <p><span class="highlight hl-neg">⚠️ zero-suffix</span> — le vol, le départ, le retour, le choix</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">➡️ Feminine (la / l')</h3>
                <p><span class="key-form">-tion / -sion</span> — la production, la décision</p>
                <p><span class="key-form">-ure</span> — la fermeture, l'écriture, la blessure</p>
                <p><span class="key-form">-ée</span> — l'entrée, la montée, la pensée</p>
                <p><span class="key-form">-ance / -ence</span> — la naissance, la patience</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">🔑 <strong>Fast rule:</strong> if the noun ends in <span class="highlight hl-verb">-tion, -sion, -ure, -ée, -ance, -ence</span> → <strong>feminine</strong>.
              If it ends in <span class="highlight hl-subject">-ment</span> or <span class="highlight hl-subject">-age</span> → <strong>masculine</strong>.
              <span class="gloss">(Rare exceptions exist — la plage, la page — but those don't come from verbs.)</span></p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- 3 · IRREGULAR / ZERO-SUFFIX -->
        <section data-slide-id="nom-3" data-step="Irregulars & Zero-suffix">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">3</span> Irregulars & Zero-suffix</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Zero-suffix nouns — no ending added</h2>
            <p class="editable-field">Some nouns are built by simply <strong>cutting the verb down</strong>, with no suffix at all. These must be learned individually.</p>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Masculine</h3>
                <table class="subj-table">
                  <tr><td>voler</td><td class="key-form">le vol</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>partir</td><td class="key-form">le départ</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>retourner</td><td class="key-form">le retour</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>choisir</td><td class="key-form">le choix</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>employer</td><td class="key-form">l'emploi</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>oublier</td><td class="key-form">l'oubli</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>travailler</td><td class="key-form">le travail</td></tr>
                </table>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Feminine</h3>
                <table class="subj-table">
                  <tr><td>visiter</td><td class="key-form">la visite</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>marcher</td><td class="key-form">la marche</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>danser</td><td class="key-form">la danse</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>nager</td><td class="key-form">la nage</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>chercher</td><td class="key-form">la recherche</td></tr>
                </table>
                <p class="gloss">⚠️ Zero-suffix nouns can be either gender — there is no shortcut. Memorise these with their article.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- 4 · HEADLINES -->
        <section data-slide-id="nom-4" data-step="CBSE Headlines">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">4</span> CBSE Headlines</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Sentence → headline (the exam task)</h2>
            <p class="editable-field">The board asks you to rewrite a full sentence as a compact headline. Turn the <strong>verb</strong> into a <strong>noun</strong>, and the <strong>subject</strong> becomes <em>de / du / des</em> + subject.</p>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <div class="formula-pipeline">
                <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Sentence</span><span class="f-value" style="font-size:1rem;">Le président visite l'Inde.</span></div>
                <div class="f-op">→</div>
                <div class="f-box" style="border-color:var(--gold);"><span class="f-label">Verb → noun</span><span class="f-value" style="font-size:1rem; color:var(--gold);">visiter → visite</span></div>
                <div class="f-op">→</div>
                <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Headline</span><span class="f-value" style="font-size:.95rem;">Visite du président en Inde.</span></div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <table class="subj-table">
                <tr><th>Phrase complète</th><th>Titre (nominalisé)</th></tr>
                <tr><td>Le prix du pétrole augmente.</td><td class="key-form">Augmentation du prix du pétrole.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Le train arrive en retard.</td><td class="key-form">Arrivée du train en retard.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Les ouvriers manifestent.</td><td class="key-form">Manifestation des ouvriers.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Le gouvernement baisse les impôts.</td><td class="key-form">Baisse des impôts par le gouvernement.</td></tr>
              </table>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- 5 · PRACTICE -->
        <section data-slide-id="nom-5" data-step="Practice">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">5</span> Practice</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Nominalise the verb</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">1. produire → la _____ <span class="gloss">(-tion)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="production" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">2. développer → le _____ <span class="gloss">(-ment)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="développement" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">3. arriver → l'_____ <span class="gloss">(-ée)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="arrivée" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">4. partir → le _____ <span class="gloss">(zero-suffix)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="départ" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">5. Le ministre visite Delhi. → _____ du ministre à Delhi. <span class="gloss">(headline)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="visite|Visite" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="accent-bar">
                <span class="ab-label">Accents :</span>
                <button class="accent-key">é</button><button class="accent-key">è</button><button class="accent-key">ê</button>
                <button class="accent-key">à</button><button class="accent-key">ç</button><button class="accent-key">ù</button>
                <button class="accent-key">û</button><button class="accent-key">î</button><button class="accent-key">ô</button>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn fib-check student-only">✓ Check</button>
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Show answers</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Retry</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </section>
      <!-- ==================================================================
           TOPIC 1 — LES VERBES : synthesis, lab, flashcards, exam
           =================================================================== -->
      <section data-topic="verbes" data-topic-name="Les Verbes" data-sub="Synthèse &amp; Examen">

        <!-- TIMELINE -->
        <section data-slide-id="verbes-fin-1" data-step="La ligne du temps">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">🕐 La ligne du temps — all nine tenses at once</h2>
            <p class="editable-field">Every tense you have studied, placed in time.</p>
            <div class="three-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">⏪ LE PASSÉ</h3>
                <p><span class="highlight hl-pronoun">Plus-que-parfait</span><br><span class="gloss">j'avais parlé — had spoken</span></p>
                <p><span class="highlight hl-aux">Imparfait</span><br><span class="gloss">je parlais — was speaking / used to</span></p>
                <p><span class="highlight hl-verb">Passé composé</span><br><span class="gloss">j'ai parlé — spoke / have spoken</span></p>
              </div>
              <div class="box green content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--green);">⏺ LE PRÉSENT</h3>
                <p><span class="highlight hl-verb">Présent</span><br><span class="gloss">je parle — I speak</span></p>
                <p><span class="highlight hl-verb">Impératif</span><br><span class="gloss">Parle ! — Speak!</span></p>
                <p><span class="highlight hl-pronoun">Conditionnel</span><br><span class="gloss">je parlerais — I would speak</span></p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">⏩ LE FUTUR</h3>
                <p><span class="highlight hl-subject">Futur proche</span><br><span class="gloss">je vais parler — am going to speak</span></p>
                <p><span class="highlight hl-subject">Futur simple</span><br><span class="gloss">je parlerai — will speak</span></p>
                <p><span class="highlight hl-subject">Futur antérieur</span><br><span class="gloss">j'aurai parlé — will have spoken</span></p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">🔑 <strong>The pattern that unlocks four tenses:</strong> compound tenses are just
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">auxiliaire</span> + <span class="highlight hl-verb">participe passé</span>.
                Change only the auxiliary's tense: <em>présent</em> → passé composé · <em>imparfait</em> → plus-que-parfait ·
                <em>futur</em> → futur antérieur · <em>conditionnel</em> → conditionnel passé.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- FORMULA LAB -->
        <section data-slide-id="verbes-fin-2" data-step="Laboratoire de conjugaison">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">🧪 Laboratoire — build any conjugation</h2>
            <p class="editable-field gloss">Pick a verb and a tense. The table rebuilds instantly.</p>

            <div class="formula-lab content-box"
              data-pronouns='["je / j&#39;","tu","il / elle","nous","vous","ils / elles"]'
              data-lab='{
                "parler":{"stem":"parl-","present":["parle","parles","parle","parlons","parlez","parlent"],"imparfait":["parlais","parlais","parlait","parlions","parliez","parlaient"],"pc":["ai parlé","as parlé","a parlé","avons parlé","avez parlé","ont parlé"],"futur":["parlerai","parleras","parlera","parlerons","parlerez","parleront"],"cond":["parlerais","parlerais","parlerait","parlerions","parleriez","parleraient"]},
                "finir":{"stem":"fin- / finiss-","present":["finis","finis","finit","finissons","finissez","finissent"],"imparfait":["finissais","finissais","finissait","finissions","finissiez","finissaient"],"pc":["ai fini","as fini","a fini","avons fini","avez fini","ont fini"],"futur":["finirai","finiras","finira","finirons","finirez","finiront"],"cond":["finirais","finirais","finirait","finirions","finiriez","finiraient"]},
                "vendre":{"stem":"vend-","present":["vends","vends","vend","vendons","vendez","vendent"],"imparfait":["vendais","vendais","vendait","vendions","vendiez","vendaient"],"pc":["ai vendu","as vendu","a vendu","avons vendu","avez vendu","ont vendu"],"futur":["vendrai","vendras","vendra","vendrons","vendrez","vendront"],"cond":["vendrais","vendrais","vendrait","vendrions","vendriez","vendraient"]},
                "aller":{"stem":"all- / ir-","present":["vais","vas","va","allons","allez","vont"],"imparfait":["allais","allais","allait","allions","alliez","allaient"],"pc":["suis allé(e)","es allé(e)","est allé(e)","sommes allé(e)s","êtes allé(e)(s)","sont allé(e)s"],"futur":["irai","iras","ira","irons","irez","iront"],"cond":["irais","irais","irait","irions","iriez","iraient"]},
                "être":{"stem":"ét- / ser-","present":["suis","es","est","sommes","êtes","sont"],"imparfait":["étais","étais","était","étions","étiez","étaient"],"pc":["ai été","as été","a été","avons été","avez été","ont été"],"futur":["serai","seras","sera","serons","serez","seront"],"cond":["serais","serais","serait","serions","seriez","seraient"]},
                "avoir":{"stem":"av- / aur-","present":["ai","as","a","avons","avez","ont"],"imparfait":["avais","avais","avait","avions","aviez","avaient"],"pc":["ai eu","as eu","a eu","avons eu","avez eu","ont eu"],"futur":["aurai","auras","aura","aurons","aurez","auront"],"cond":["aurais","aurais","aurait","aurions","auriez","auraient"]}
              }'>

              <div style="display:flex; gap:6px; flex-wrap:wrap; justify-content:center; margin-bottom:8px;">
                <button class="tb-btn verb-select-btn" data-verb="parler">parler</button>
                <button class="tb-btn verb-select-btn" data-verb="finir">finir</button>
                <button class="tb-btn verb-select-btn" data-verb="vendre">vendre</button>
                <button class="tb-btn verb-select-btn" data-verb="aller">aller</button>
                <button class="tb-btn verb-select-btn" data-verb="être">être</button>
                <button class="tb-btn verb-select-btn" data-verb="avoir">avoir</button>
              </div>
              <div style="display:flex; gap:6px; flex-wrap:wrap; justify-content:center; margin-bottom:10px;">
                <button class="tb-btn tense-select-btn" data-tense="present">Présent</button>
                <button class="tb-btn tense-select-btn" data-tense="imparfait">Imparfait</button>
                <button class="tb-btn tense-select-btn" data-tense="pc">Passé Composé</button>
                <button class="tb-btn tense-select-btn" data-tense="futur">Futur Simple</button>
                <button class="tb-btn tense-select-btn" data-tense="cond">Conditionnel</button>
              </div>

              <div class="formula-pipeline">
                <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Verbe</span><span class="f-value lab-verb">parler</span></div>
                <div class="f-op">→</div>
                <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Radical</span><span class="f-value lab-stem">parl-</span></div>
                <div class="f-op">→</div>
                <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Résultat</span><span class="f-value lab-eq">je parle</span></div>
              </div>

              <div class="box blue content-box" style="margin-top:10px;">
                <table class="subj-table"><tbody class="lab-body"></tbody></table>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- FLASHCARDS -->
        <section data-slide-id="verbes-fin-3" data-step="Cartes mémoire">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">🃏 Cartes mémoire — cliquez pour retourner</h2>
            <p class="editable-field gloss">Mark ✓ when you know it and ↻ when you don't. Your marks are saved, so next time you can drill only the weak ones.</p>
            <div class="flip-card-grid">
              <div class="flip-card">
                <div class="flip-card-inner">
                  <div class="flip-card-front"><strong>ALLER</strong><br><span style="font-size:.8em;">futur simple</span></div>
                  <div class="flip-card-back">j'irai</div>
                </div>
                <div class="fc-marks"><button class="fc-mark" data-mark="known" title="Je sais">✓</button><button class="fc-mark" data-mark="again" title="À revoir">↻</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="flip-card">
                <div class="flip-card-inner">
                  <div class="flip-card-front"><strong>FAIRE</strong><br><span style="font-size:.8em;">passé composé</span></div>
                  <div class="flip-card-back">j'ai fait</div>
                </div>
                <div class="fc-marks"><button class="fc-mark" data-mark="known" title="Je sais">✓</button><button class="fc-mark" data-mark="again" title="À revoir">↻</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="flip-card">
                <div class="flip-card-inner">
                  <div class="flip-card-front"><strong>POUVOIR</strong><br><span style="font-size:.8em;">futur simple</span></div>
                  <div class="flip-card-back">je pourrai</div>
                </div>
                <div class="fc-marks"><button class="fc-mark" data-mark="known" title="Je sais">✓</button><button class="fc-mark" data-mark="again" title="À revoir">↻</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="flip-card">
                <div class="flip-card-inner">
                  <div class="flip-card-front"><strong>VOULOIR</strong><br><span style="font-size:.8em;">conditionnel</span></div>
                  <div class="flip-card-back">je voudrais</div>
                </div>
                <div class="fc-marks"><button class="fc-mark" data-mark="known" title="Je sais">✓</button><button class="fc-mark" data-mark="again" title="À revoir">↻</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="flip-card">
                <div class="flip-card-inner">
                  <div class="flip-card-front"><strong>VENIR</strong><br><span style="font-size:.8em;">passé composé</span></div>
                  <div class="flip-card-back">je suis venu(e)</div>
                </div>
                <div class="fc-marks"><button class="fc-mark" data-mark="known" title="Je sais">✓</button><button class="fc-mark" data-mark="again" title="À revoir">↻</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="flip-card">
                <div class="flip-card-inner">
                  <div class="flip-card-front"><strong>ÊTRE</strong><br><span style="font-size:.8em;">imparfait</span></div>
                  <div class="flip-card-back">j'étais</div>
                </div>
                <div class="fc-marks"><button class="fc-mark" data-mark="known" title="Je sais">✓</button><button class="fc-mark" data-mark="again" title="À revoir">↻</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="flip-card">
                <div class="flip-card-inner">
                  <div class="flip-card-front"><strong>PRENDRE</strong><br><span style="font-size:.8em;">participe passé</span></div>
                  <div class="flip-card-back">pris</div>
                </div>
                <div class="fc-marks"><button class="fc-mark" data-mark="known" title="Je sais">✓</button><button class="fc-mark" data-mark="again" title="À revoir">↻</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="flip-card">
                <div class="flip-card-inner">
                  <div class="flip-card-front"><strong>SE LEVER</strong><br><span style="font-size:.8em;">passé composé (elle)</span></div>
                  <div class="flip-card-back">elle s'est levée</div>
                </div>
                <div class="fc-marks"><button class="fc-mark" data-mark="known" title="Je sais">✓</button><button class="fc-mark" data-mark="again" title="À revoir">↻</button></div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- REFERENCE MATRIX -->
        <section data-slide-id="verbes-fin-4" data-step="Tableau de référence">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">📊 Tableau de référence — endings by tense</h2>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <table class="subj-table">
                <tr>
                  <th>Temps</th><th>Formation</th><th>je</th><th>nous</th><th>ils</th>
                </tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Présent</strong> (-er)</td><td>radical + e/es/e/ons/ez/ent</td><td class="key-form">parle</td><td>parlons</td><td>parlent</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Impératif</strong></td><td>présent sans pronom</td><td>—</td><td class="key-form">Parlons !</td><td>—</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Imparfait</strong></td><td>radical « nous » + ais/ait/ions/aient</td><td class="key-form">parlais</td><td>parlions</td><td>parlaient</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Passé composé</strong></td><td>avoir/être présent + participe</td><td class="key-form">ai parlé</td><td>avons parlé</td><td>ont parlé</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Plus-que-parfait</strong></td><td>avoir/être imparfait + participe</td><td class="key-form">avais parlé</td><td>avions parlé</td><td>avaient parlé</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Futur simple</strong></td><td>infinitif + ai/as/a/ons/ez/ont</td><td class="key-form">parlerai</td><td>parlerons</td><td>parleront</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Futur antérieur</strong></td><td>avoir/être futur + participe</td><td class="key-form">aurai parlé</td><td>aurons parlé</td><td>auront parlé</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Conditionnel</strong></td><td>radical futur + ais/ait/ions/aient</td><td class="key-form">parlerais</td><td>parlerions</td><td>parleraient</td></tr>
              </table>
            </div>
            <p class="editable-field gloss">Print this slide (🖨️ in the top bar) — it makes a one-page revision sheet.</p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- TOPIC-LEVEL CBSE QUIZ -->
        <section data-slide-id="verbes-fin-5" data-step="Examen CBSE — tous les temps">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">📝 Examen blanc — questions réelles du CBSE</h2>
            <p class="editable-field gloss">Mixed tenses, exactly as Question 4 of the board paper presents them. No hints about which tense to use — that is the real challenge.</p>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text"><span class="q-tag">CBSE 2022</span>1. Ma petite, tu _____ (être) heureuse car nous partons en vacances dans un mois !</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="seras" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text"><span class="q-tag">CBSE 2022</span>2. Mes parents _____ (acheter) une nouvelle voiture le mois prochain.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="achèteront" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text"><span class="q-tag">CBSE 2022</span>3. Nous _____ (se rencontrer) au club la semaine dernière.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="nous sommes rencontrés|nous sommes rencontré(e)s|nous sommes rencontrées" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text"><span class="q-tag">CBSE 2022</span>4. En 2021, nous _____ (étudier) souvent en ligne.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="étudiions" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text"><span class="q-tag">CBSE 2022</span>5. Ne _____ (se fâcher) pas, je te prie !</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="te fâche" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text"><span class="q-tag">CBSE 2022</span>6. Dès que l'acteur _____ (revenir), le réalisateur racontera l'histoire.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="sera revenu" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text"><span class="q-tag">CBSE 2022</span>7. Je veux _____ (se coucher) tôt ce soir.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="me coucher" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text"><span class="q-tag">CBSE 2022</span>8. L'année dernière, elles _____ (se rencontrer) dans la rue.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="se sont rencontrées" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="accent-bar">
                <span class="ab-label">Accents :</span>
                <button class="accent-key">é</button><button class="accent-key">è</button><button class="accent-key">ê</button>
                <button class="accent-key">à</button><button class="accent-key">ç</button><button class="accent-key">ù</button>
                <button class="accent-key">û</button><button class="accent-key">î</button><button class="accent-key">ô</button>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn fib-check student-only">✓ Vérifier</button>
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 8</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- EXAM CHECKLIST -->
        <section data-slide-id="verbes-fin-6" data-step="Check-list de l'examen">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">✅ Check-list — before you hand in the paper</h2>
            <p class="editable-field">Run through these six checks on every verb you write. Most lost marks are here, not in the rules.</p>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <p>☐ <strong>Which group?</strong> Check the <em>nous</em> form — <em>finissons</em> or <em>partons</em>?</p>
                <p>☐ <strong>Which tense does the sentence signal?</strong> <em>hier</em> → passé composé · <em>souvent</em> → imparfait · <em>demain</em> → futur</p>
                <p>☐ <strong>Compound tense?</strong> Then ask: <span class="highlight hl-aux">avoir</span> or <span class="highlight hl-aux">être</span>?</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <p>☐ <strong>If être</strong> — did you make the participle agree with the subject?</p>
                <p>☐ <strong>Negation</strong> — does <em>ne … pas</em> wrap the <span class="highlight hl-aux">auxiliary</span>, not the participle?</p>
                <p>☐ <strong>Accents</strong> — <em>é</em> in <em>parlé</em>, <em>è</em> in <em>achète</em>. A missing accent is a missing mark.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">🎯 <strong>Remember the weighting:</strong> verbs are the one <strong>compulsory</strong> question — 5 marks guaranteed to appear.
              You then choose 5 of the remaining 6 topics. Securing verbs protects a sixth of your whole grammar section before you start.</p>
            </div>
            <p class="editable-field gloss">➡️ Press <kbd>→</kbd> to continue to the next grammar topic.</p>
          </div>
        </section>
      </section>
      <!-- ==================================================================
           TOPIC 2 — LE SUBJONCTIF
           =================================================================== -->
      <section data-topic="subjonctif" data-topic-name="Le Subjonctif" data-sub="La Formation">

        <section data-slide-id="subj-form-1" data-step="Description">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">1</span> Description</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Le Subjonctif — the mood of subjectivity</h2>
            <p class="editable-field">The subjonctif is not a tense — it is a <strong>mood</strong>. The indicatif states facts; the subjonctif expresses what someone <strong>wants, feels, doubts or needs</strong>.</p>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Indicatif = fact</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Je sais qu'il <span class="highlight hl-verb">est</span> malade.</p>
                <p class="gloss">I know that he is ill. — a fact</p>
                <p class="example-text">Il <span class="highlight hl-verb">vient</span> demain.</p>
                <p class="gloss">He is coming tomorrow.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Subjonctif = subjective</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Je veux qu'il <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">soit</span> à l'heure.</p>
                <p class="gloss">I want him to be on time. — a wish, not a fact</p>
                <p class="example-text">Il faut qu'il <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">vienne</span> demain.</p>
                <p class="gloss">He must come tomorrow. — a necessity</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">🔑 <strong>The three conditions — all must be true:</strong>
                ① a <span class="highlight hl-aux">trigger</span> expression, ② the word <span class="highlight hl-aux">que</span>,
                ③ <strong>two different subjects</strong>.<br>
                <em>Je veux <span class="highlight hl-subject">que tu</span> partes.</em> ✓ two subjects &nbsp;·&nbsp;
                <em>Je veux <span class="highlight hl-neg">partir</span>.</em> ✗ same subject → infinitive, no subjonctif</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="subj-form-2" data-step="Formation">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">2</span> Formation</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">La formule — le radical de « ILS »</h2>
            <div class="formula-pipeline">
              <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Présent, forme ILS</span><span class="f-value">ils parl<u>ent</u></span></div>
              <div class="f-op">−</div>
              <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Retirer -ent</span><span class="f-value">parl-</span></div>
              <div class="f-op">+</div>
              <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Terminaisons</span><span class="f-value">-e -es -e -ions -iez -ent</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">parler → que je parle</h3>
                <table class="subj-table">
                  <tr><td>que je</td><td class="key-form">parle</td><td>que nous</td><td class="key-form">parlions</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>que tu</td><td class="key-form">parles</td><td>que vous</td><td class="key-form">parliez</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>qu'il/elle</td><td class="key-form">parle</td><td>qu'ils/elles</td><td class="key-form">parlent</td></tr>
                </table>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Same rule for every regular verb</h3>
                <p>finir → ils fin<u>iss</u>ent → que je <span class="key-form">finisse</span></p>
                <p>vendre → ils vend<u>ent</u> → que je <span class="key-form">vende</span></p>
                <p>écrire → ils écriv<u>ent</u> → que j'<span class="key-form">écrive</span></p>
                <p>partir → ils part<u>ent</u> → que je <span class="key-form">parte</span></p>
                <p class="gloss">Always start from <strong>ils</strong>, never from the infinitive.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="subj-form-3" data-step="Exceptions">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">3</span> Exceptions</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Les irréguliers — à apprendre par cœur</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Complètement irréguliers</h3>
                <table class="subj-table">
                  <tr><th></th><th>que je</th><th>que nous</th></tr>
                  <tr><td><strong>être</strong></td><td class="key-form">sois</td><td class="key-form">soyons</td></tr>
                  <tr><td><strong>avoir</strong></td><td class="key-form">aie</td><td class="key-form">ayons</td></tr>
                  <tr><td><strong>aller</strong></td><td class="key-form">aille</td><td class="key-form">allions</td></tr>
                  <tr><td><strong>faire</strong></td><td class="key-form">fasse</td><td class="key-form">fassions</td></tr>
                  <tr><td><strong>pouvoir</strong></td><td class="key-form">puisse</td><td class="key-form">puissions</td></tr>
                  <tr><td><strong>savoir</strong></td><td class="key-form">sache</td><td class="key-form">sachions</td></tr>
                  <tr><td><strong>vouloir</strong></td><td class="key-form">veuille</td><td class="key-form">voulions</td></tr>
                </table>
                <p class="gloss">Impersonal: qu'il <strong>faille</strong> (falloir), qu'il <strong>pleuve</strong> (pleuvoir)</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Les verbes « à deux radicaux »</h3>
                <p>Some verbs use one stem for je/tu/il/ils and another for nous/vous:</p>
                <table class="subj-table">
                  <tr><th>Verbe</th><th>que je</th><th>que nous</th></tr>
                  <tr><td>prendre</td><td class="key-form">prenne</td><td class="key-form">prenions</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>venir</td><td class="key-form">vienne</td><td class="key-form">venions</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>boire</td><td class="key-form">boive</td><td class="key-form">buvions</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>recevoir</td><td class="key-form">reçoive</td><td class="key-form">recevions</td></tr>
                </table>
                <p class="gloss">The nous/vous form copies the <strong>imparfait</strong>.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="subj-form-4" data-step="Pièges">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">4</span> Pièges</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">⚠️ Trap Alert — same subject means NO subjunctive</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box red content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--crimson);">✗ Wrong</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Je veux <span class="highlight hl-neg">que je parte</span>.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Il faut <span class="highlight hl-neg">que tu es</span> à l'heure.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Je pense qu'il <span class="highlight hl-neg">soit</span> malade.</p>
                <p class="example-text">J'espère qu'il <span class="highlight hl-neg">vienne</span>.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box green content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--green);">✓ Right</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Je veux <span class="highlight hl-verb">partir</span>. <span class="gloss">same subject → infinitive</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Il faut que tu <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">sois</span> à l'heure. <span class="gloss">être is irregular</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Je pense qu'il <span class="highlight hl-verb">est</span> malade. <span class="gloss">penser (affirmative) = indicatif</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">J'espère qu'il <span class="highlight hl-verb">viendra</span>. <span class="gloss">espérer never takes subjonctif</span></p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field"><strong>Two famous exceptions students always miss:</strong>
                <span class="highlight hl-neg">espérer que</span> takes the <strong>indicatif</strong> (unlike English "hope"), and
                <span class="highlight hl-neg">après que</span> also takes the indicatif — but <span class="highlight hl-aux">avant que</span> takes the subjonctif.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="subj-form-5" data-step="Exemples">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">5</span> Exemples travaillés</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Worked examples — spot the three conditions</h2>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-aux">Il faut</span> <span class="highlight hl-aux">que</span> <span class="highlight hl-subject">nous</span> <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">partions</span> maintenant.</p>
              <p class="gloss">We must leave now. — trigger <em>il faut</em> + que + new subject <em>nous</em></p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-subject">Je</span> <span class="highlight hl-aux">veux que</span> <span class="highlight hl-subject">tu</span> <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">fasses</span> tes devoirs.</p>
              <p class="gloss">I want you to do your homework. — <em>faire</em> → fasses</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-aux">Bien qu'</span>il <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">soit</span> fatigué, il travaille encore.</p>
              <p class="gloss">Although he is tired, he is still working. — conjunction trigger</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-aux">Je doute qu'</span>ils <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">puissent</span> venir ce soir.</p>
              <p class="gloss">I doubt they can come tonight. — <em>pouvoir</em> → puissent</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="subj-form-6" data-step="En contexte">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">6</span> En contexte</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">In context — Entre Jeunes themes</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">L.2 — Après le bac</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Mes parents veulent que je <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">choisisse</span> les sciences.</p>
                <p class="gloss">My parents want me to choose science.</p>
                <h3>L.7 — En pleine forme</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Il est important que tu <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">dormes</span> huit heures.</p>
                <p class="gloss">It is important that you sleep eight hours.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">L.8 — L'environnement</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Il faut que nous <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">protégions</span> la planète.</p>
                <p class="gloss">We must protect the planet.</p>
                <h3 style="color:var(--gold);">L.5 — Les médias</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Je ne crois pas que la télévision <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">soit</span> toujours mauvaise.</p>
                <p class="gloss">I don't think television is always bad.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">💡 <strong>Essay tip:</strong> one well-placed <em>Il faut que nous…</em> or <em>Bien que…</em> immediately raises the level of your writing. Keep two such sentences ready for any opinion topic.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="subj-form-7" data-step="Pratique QCM">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">7</span> Pratique — QCM</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Choose the correct subjunctive</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="fasses">
                <p class="q-text">1. Il faut que tu _____ tes devoirs. <span class="gloss">(faire)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">fais</button><button class="option-btn">fasses</button><button class="option-btn">feras</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="soit">
                <p class="q-text">2. Je veux qu'il _____ à l'heure. <span class="gloss">(être)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">est</button><button class="option-btn">soit</button><button class="option-btn">sois</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="puisse">
                <p class="q-text">3. Il est possible qu'elle _____ venir. <span class="gloss">(pouvoir)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">peut</button><button class="option-btn">pourra</button><button class="option-btn">puisse</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="alliez">
                <p class="q-text">4. Je souhaite que vous _____ mieux. <span class="gloss">(aller)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">alliez</button><button class="option-btn">allez</button><button class="option-btn">irez</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="viendra">
                <p class="q-text">5. J'espère qu'il _____ demain. <span class="gloss">(venir)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">vienne</button><button class="option-btn">viendra</button><button class="option-btn">viennes</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="subj-form-8" data-step="Pratique — à compléter">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">8</span> Pratique — à compléter</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Write the subjunctive</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">1. <span class="q-tag">CBSE 2024</span>Il est important que nous _____ (pouvoir) assister à cette fête.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="puissions" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">2. <span class="q-tag">CBSE 2024</span>Ma mère exige que nous _____ (manger) ensemble.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="mangions" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">3. Il faut que tu _____ (savoir) la vérité.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="saches" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">4. Je doute qu'ils _____ (avoir) le temps.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="aient" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">5. Bien qu'elle _____ (être) jeune, elle est très sérieuse.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="soit" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="accent-bar">
                <span class="ab-label">Accents :</span>
                <button class="accent-key">é</button><button class="accent-key">è</button><button class="accent-key">ê</button>
                <button class="accent-key">à</button><button class="accent-key">ç</button><button class="accent-key">ù</button>
                <button class="accent-key">û</button><button class="accent-key">î</button><button class="accent-key">ô</button>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn fib-check student-only">✓ Vérifier</button>
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </section>

      <!-- ================= 2.2 VOLONTÉ & DÉSIR ================= -->
      <section data-topic="subjonctif" data-topic-name="Le Subjonctif" data-sub="Volonté &amp; Désir">

        <section data-slide-id="subj-vol-1" data-step="Description">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">1</span> Description</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Volonté &amp; désir — wanting someone else to act</h2>
            <p class="editable-field">When one person <strong>wants, wishes, demands or forbids</strong> that another person do something, French uses the subjonctif.</p>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <p class="example-text">Je <span class="highlight hl-aux">veux</span> <span class="highlight hl-aux">que</span> tu <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">viennes</span>.</p>
              <p class="gloss">I want you to come. — Note that English uses an infinitive here; French cannot.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Les déclencheurs</h3>
              <p>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">vouloir que</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">souhaiter que</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">désirer que</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">exiger que</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">demander que</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">préférer que</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">aimer que</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">interdire que</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">permettre que</span>
              </p>
              <p class="gloss">want · wish · desire · demand · ask · prefer · like · forbid · allow</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="subj-vol-2" data-step="Formation">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">2</span> Formation</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">La formule</h2>
            <div class="formula-pipeline">
              <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Sujet 1 + déclencheur</span><span class="f-value">Je veux</span></div>
              <div class="f-op">+</div>
              <div class="f-box" style="border-color:var(--gold);"><span class="f-label">que</span><span class="f-value" style="color:var(--gold);">que</span></div>
              <div class="f-op">+</div>
              <div class="f-box" style="border-color:var(--purple);"><span class="f-label">Sujet 2 + subjonctif</span><span class="f-value" style="color:var(--purple);">tu viennes</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Deux sujets différents → subjonctif</h3>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-subject">Je</span> veux que <span class="highlight hl-subject">tu</span> <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">partes</span>.</p>
                <p class="gloss">I want you to leave.</p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-subject">Le prof</span> exige que <span class="highlight hl-subject">les élèves</span> <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">soient</span> silencieux.</p>
                <p class="gloss">The teacher demands that the pupils be quiet.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Même sujet → infinitif</h3>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-subject">Je</span> veux <span class="highlight hl-verb">partir</span>.</p>
                <p class="gloss">I want to leave. — no <em>que</em>, no subjunctive</p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-subject">Elle</span> souhaite <span class="highlight hl-verb">réussir</span>.</p>
                <p class="gloss">She wishes to succeed.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="subj-vol-3" data-step="Exceptions">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">3</span> Exceptions</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Les exceptions — espérer et les verbes d'opinion</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box red content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--crimson);">ESPÉRER → indicatif</h3>
                <p>Although it looks like a wish, <em>espérer</em> takes the indicatif.</p>
                <p class="example-text">J'espère qu'il <span class="highlight hl-verb">viendra</span>.</p>
                <p class="gloss">I hope he will come. — futur, not subjonctif</p>
                <p class="example-text">✗ <em>J'espère qu'il vienne.</em></p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Verbs of asking take <em>de</em> + infinitif too</h3>
                <p>Two correct structures exist side by side:</p>
                <p class="example-text">Je demande que tu <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">viennes</span>.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Je te demande <span class="highlight hl-verb">de venir</span>.</p>
                <p class="gloss">Both: I ask you to come. The second is more natural in speech.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field"><strong>Note on <em>préférer</em> and <em>aimer</em>:</strong> with two subjects they take the subjonctif —
              <em>Je préfère que tu <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">restes</span></em> <span class="gloss">I prefer that you stay</span> — but with one subject they simply take an infinitive: <em>Je préfère <span class="highlight hl-verb">rester</span>.</em></p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="subj-vol-4" data-step="Pièges">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">4</span> Pièges</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">⚠️ Trap Alert — English infinitive ≠ French infinitive</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box red content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--crimson);">✗ Wrong — translating word for word</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Je veux <span class="highlight hl-neg">toi de venir</span>.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Je veux <span class="highlight hl-neg">tu viens</span>.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Il exige que je <span class="highlight hl-neg">suis</span> présent.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box green content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--green);">✓ Right</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Je veux <span class="highlight hl-verb">que tu viennes</span>. <span class="gloss">que + subjonctif</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Je veux <span class="highlight hl-verb">que tu viennes</span>. <span class="gloss">not the indicatif <em>viens</em></span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Il exige que je <span class="highlight hl-verb">sois</span> présent. <span class="gloss">être → sois</span></p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">💡 English says "I want <strong>you to come</strong>" with an infinitive. French <strong>cannot</strong> do this — it must open a new clause with <span class="highlight hl-aux">que</span> and put the second verb in the subjonctif. Train yourself to hear "want … to" as a signal for <em>que + subjonctif</em>.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="subj-vol-5" data-step="Exemples">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">5</span> Exemples travaillés</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Worked examples</h2>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <p class="example-text">Mes parents <span class="highlight hl-aux">veulent que</span> je <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">réussisse</span> mes examens.</p>
              <p class="gloss">My parents want me to pass my exams.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Le directeur <span class="highlight hl-aux">exige que</span> tout le monde <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">soit</span> à l'heure.</p>
              <p class="gloss">The headmaster demands that everyone be on time.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Je <span class="highlight hl-aux">souhaite que</span> vous <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">ayez</span> une bonne année.</p>
              <p class="gloss">I wish you a good year. — avoir → ayez</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Elle <span class="highlight hl-aux">préfère que</span> nous <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">prenions</span> le train.</p>
              <p class="gloss">She prefers that we take the train. — prendre → prenions</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="subj-vol-6" data-step="En contexte">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">6</span> En contexte</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">In context — expressing what others want</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">L.2 — Après le bac</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Mon père veut que je <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">devienne</span> ingénieur.</p>
                <p class="gloss">My father wants me to become an engineer.</p>
                <h3>L.3 — Chercher du travail</h3>
                <p class="example-text">L'entreprise exige que les candidats <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">sachent</span> l'anglais.</p>
                <p class="gloss">The company requires candidates to know English.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">L.6 — Chacun ses goûts</h3>
                <p class="example-text">J'aimerais que nous <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">allions</span> au concert ensemble.</p>
                <p class="gloss">I would like us to go to the concert together.</p>
                <h3 style="color:var(--gold);">L.7 — En pleine forme</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Le médecin veut que tu <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">fasses</span> plus d'exercice.</p>
                <p class="gloss">The doctor wants you to do more exercise.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="subj-vol-7" data-step="Pratique QCM">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">7</span> Pratique — QCM</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Choose the correct form</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="viennes">
                <p class="q-text">1. Je veux que tu _____ avec nous. <span class="gloss">(venir)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">viens</button><button class="option-btn">viennes</button><button class="option-btn">viendras</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="partir">
                <p class="q-text">2. Je veux _____ tout de suite. <span class="gloss">(partir — même sujet)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">que je parte</button><button class="option-btn">partir</button><button class="option-btn">que je pars</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="soyez">
                <p class="q-text">3. Elle souhaite que vous _____ heureux. <span class="gloss">(être)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">êtes</button><button class="option-btn">soyez</button><button class="option-btn">serez</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="fassions">
                <p class="q-text">4. Le prof exige que nous _____ le silence. <span class="gloss">(faire)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">faisons</button><button class="option-btn">fassions</button><button class="option-btn">ferons</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="réussira">
                <p class="q-text">5. J'espère qu'elle _____ à l'examen. <span class="gloss">(réussir)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">réussisse</button><button class="option-btn">réussira</button><button class="option-btn">réussirait</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="subj-vol-8" data-step="Pratique — à compléter">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">8</span> Pratique — à compléter</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Complete the sentence</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">1. <span class="q-tag">CBSE 2024</span>Ma mère exige que nous _____ (manger) ensemble.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="mangions" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">2. Je veux que tu me _____ (dire) la vérité.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="dises" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">3. Elle souhaite que ses enfants _____ (avoir) une bonne éducation.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="aient" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">4. Nous préférons que vous _____ (venir) demain.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="veniez" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">5. Le prof interdit que les élèves _____ (sortir) avant midi.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="sortent" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="accent-bar">
                <span class="ab-label">Accents :</span>
                <button class="accent-key">é</button><button class="accent-key">è</button><button class="accent-key">ê</button>
                <button class="accent-key">à</button><button class="accent-key">ç</button><button class="accent-key">ù</button>
                <button class="accent-key">û</button><button class="accent-key">î</button><button class="accent-key">ô</button>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn fib-check student-only">✓ Vérifier</button>
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </section>

      <!-- ================= 2.3 ÉMOTION ================= -->
      <section data-topic="subjonctif" data-topic-name="Le Subjonctif" data-sub="L'Émotion">

        <section data-slide-id="subj-emo-1" data-step="Description">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">1</span> Description</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">L'Émotion — feelings trigger the subjunctive</h2>
            <p class="editable-field">Any expression of <strong>joy, sadness, fear, surprise or regret</strong> about someone else's action requires the subjonctif.</p>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <p class="example-text">Je suis <span class="highlight hl-aux">content que</span> tu <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">sois</span> là.</p>
              <p class="gloss">I am happy that you are here.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Les déclencheurs d'émotion</h3>
              <p>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">être content(e) que</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">être heureux que</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">être triste que</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">être désolé que</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">être surpris que</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">avoir peur que</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">craindre que</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">regretter que</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">c'est dommage que</span>
              </p>
              <p class="gloss">happy · glad · sad · sorry · surprised · afraid · fear · regret · it's a pity</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="subj-emo-2" data-step="Formation">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">2</span> Formation</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">La formule</h2>
            <div class="formula-pipeline">
              <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Émotion</span><span class="f-value">Je suis content</span></div>
              <div class="f-op">+</div>
              <div class="f-box" style="border-color:var(--gold);"><span class="f-label">que</span><span class="f-value" style="color:var(--gold);">que</span></div>
              <div class="f-op">+</div>
              <div class="f-box" style="border-color:var(--purple);"><span class="f-label">Subjonctif</span><span class="f-value" style="color:var(--purple);">tu sois là</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <table class="subj-table">
                <tr><th>Émotion</th><th>Exemple</th><th>Anglais</th></tr>
                <tr><td>joie</td><td>Je suis <strong>ravi</strong> que tu <span class="key-form">viennes</span>.</td><td class="gloss">I'm delighted you're coming.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>tristesse</td><td>Je suis <strong>triste</strong> qu'il <span class="key-form">parte</span>.</td><td class="gloss">I'm sad he's leaving.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>peur</td><td>J'ai <strong>peur</strong> qu'il <span class="key-form">soit</span> malade.</td><td class="gloss">I'm afraid he is ill.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>regret</td><td>C'est <strong>dommage</strong> que vous ne <span class="key-form">puissiez</span> pas venir.</td><td class="gloss">It's a pity you can't come.</td></tr>
              </table>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="subj-emo-3" data-step="Exceptions">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">3</span> Exceptions</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Les exceptions — même sujet, et le « ne » explétif</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Même sujet → de + infinitif</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Je suis content <span class="highlight hl-verb">de partir</span>.</p>
                <p class="gloss">I'm happy to be leaving. — I am happy, I am leaving: one subject</p>
                <p class="example-text">Je suis content <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">que tu partes</span>.</p>
                <p class="gloss">I'm happy that you are leaving. — two subjects</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Le « ne » explétif</h3>
                <p>After <em>avoir peur que</em> and <em>craindre que</em>, a <strong>meaningless</strong> <em>ne</em> may appear. It is <strong>not</strong> a negation.</p>
                <p class="example-text">J'ai peur qu'il <span class="highlight hl-neg">ne</span> <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">soit</span> en retard.</p>
                <p class="gloss">I'm afraid he may be late. — NOT "he is not late"</p>
                <p class="gloss">It is optional and mostly literary; you will not be penalised for leaving it out.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="subj-emo-4" data-step="Pièges">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">4</span> Pièges</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">⚠️ Trap Alert — emotion vs. certainty</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Émotion → SUBJONCTIF</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Je suis <strong>surpris</strong> qu'il <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">soit</span> ici.</p>
                <p class="gloss">I'm surprised he is here. — reaction, subjective</p>
                <p class="example-text">C'est dommage qu'elle <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">ait</span> échoué.</p>
                <p class="gloss">It's a pity she failed.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Certitude → INDICATIF</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Je suis <strong>sûr</strong> qu'il <span class="highlight hl-verb">est</span> ici.</p>
                <p class="gloss">I'm sure he is here. — certainty, factual</p>
                <p class="example-text">Il est <strong>évident</strong> qu'elle <span class="highlight hl-verb">a</span> échoué.</p>
                <p class="gloss">It is obvious she failed.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box red content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field"><strong>Watch these pairs:</strong>
                <em>être sûr / certain / évident / clair que</em> → <span class="highlight hl-verb">indicatif</span>, but
                <em>ne pas être sûr / certain que</em> → <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">subjonctif</span>.
                Negation turns certainty into doubt, and doubt takes the subjunctive.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="subj-emo-5" data-step="Exemples">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">5</span> Exemples travaillés</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Worked examples</h2>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <p class="example-text">Je suis <span class="highlight hl-aux">heureux que</span> tu <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">aies</span> réussi.</p>
              <p class="gloss">I'm happy that you succeeded.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Nous <span class="highlight hl-aux">regrettons que</span> vous ne <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">puissiez</span> pas rester.</p>
              <p class="gloss">We regret that you cannot stay.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Elle a <span class="highlight hl-aux">peur que</span> son fils <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">fasse</span> une bêtise.</p>
              <p class="gloss">She is afraid her son will do something silly.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">C'est <span class="highlight hl-aux">dommage qu'</span>il <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">pleuve</span> aujourd'hui.</p>
              <p class="gloss">It's a pity it's raining today. — pleuvoir → qu'il pleuve</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="subj-emo-6" data-step="En contexte">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">6</span> En contexte</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">In context — reacting to news in a letter</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Bonne nouvelle</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Je suis très content que tu <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">viennes</span> en Inde !</p>
                <p class="gloss">I'm very happy that you are coming to India!</p>
                <p class="example-text">Je suis ravi que vous <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">ayez</span> trouvé un travail.</p>
                <p class="gloss">I'm delighted you have found a job.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Mauvaise nouvelle</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Je suis désolé que ton grand-père <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">soit</span> malade.</p>
                <p class="gloss">I'm sorry that your grandfather is ill.</p>
                <p class="example-text">C'est dommage que tu ne <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">puisses</span> pas venir.</p>
                <p class="gloss">It's a pity you can't come.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">💡 <strong>Letter tip:</strong> reacting to your friend's news is worth marks for content. Open the reply with
              <em>Je suis content(e) que…</em> or <em>Je suis désolé(e) que…</em> — instant subjunctive, instant relevance.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="subj-emo-7" data-step="Pratique QCM">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">7</span> Pratique — QCM</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Subjonctif or indicatif?</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="soit">
                <p class="q-text">1. Je suis content que tu _____ ici. <span class="gloss">(être)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">es</button><button class="option-btn">soit</button><button class="option-btn">sois</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="est">
                <p class="q-text">2. Je suis sûr qu'il _____ à la maison. <span class="gloss">(être)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">soit</button><button class="option-btn">est</button><button class="option-btn">serait</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="ait">
                <p class="q-text">3. C'est dommage qu'elle n'_____ pas le temps. <span class="gloss">(avoir)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">a</button><button class="option-btn">ait</button><button class="option-btn">aura</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="fasse">
                <p class="q-text">4. J'ai peur qu'il _____ froid ce soir. <span class="gloss">(faire)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">fait</button><button class="option-btn">fera</button><button class="option-btn">fasse</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="de partir">
                <p class="q-text">5. Je suis triste _____ si tôt. <span class="gloss">(partir — même sujet)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">que je parte</button><button class="option-btn">de partir</button><button class="option-btn">que je pars</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="subj-emo-8" data-step="Pratique — à compléter">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">8</span> Pratique — à compléter</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Complete the sentence</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">1. Je suis heureux que vous _____ (être) parmi nous.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="soyez" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">2. Nous regrettons qu'ils ne _____ (pouvoir) pas assister.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="puissent" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">3. C'est dommage que tu _____ (avoir) tant de travail.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="aies" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">4. Elle est surprise que nous _____ (savoir) la nouvelle.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="sachions" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">5. Je suis désolé que le train _____ (partir) sans toi.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="parte" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="accent-bar">
                <span class="ab-label">Accents :</span>
                <button class="accent-key">é</button><button class="accent-key">è</button><button class="accent-key">ê</button>
                <button class="accent-key">à</button><button class="accent-key">ç</button><button class="accent-key">ù</button>
                <button class="accent-key">û</button><button class="accent-key">î</button><button class="accent-key">ô</button>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn fib-check student-only">✓ Vérifier</button>
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </section>
      <!-- ================= 2.4 NÉCESSITÉ IMPERSONNELLE ================= -->
      <section data-topic="subjonctif" data-topic-name="Le Subjonctif" data-sub="La Nécessité">

        <section data-slide-id="subj-nec-1" data-step="Description">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">1</span> Description</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">La Nécessité — impersonal expressions</h2>
            <p class="editable-field">Expressions beginning with <strong>il</strong> (an impersonal "it", not a person) that state a <strong>necessity, obligation or possibility</strong> take the subjonctif.</p>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-aux">Il faut que</span> tu <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">viennes</span> tout de suite.</p>
              <p class="gloss">You must come at once. — <em>il faut que</em> is the single most useful subjunctive trigger in the exam.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Les déclencheurs impersonnels</h3>
              <p>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">il faut que</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">il est nécessaire que</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">il est important que</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">il est essentiel que</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">il vaut mieux que</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">il est temps que</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">il est possible que</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">il se peut que</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">il est dommage que</span>
              </p>
              <p class="gloss">must · it is necessary · important · essential · better · time · possible · may · a pity</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="subj-nec-2" data-step="Formation">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">2</span> Formation</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">La formule</h2>
            <div class="formula-pipeline">
              <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Expression impersonnelle</span><span class="f-value">Il faut</span></div>
              <div class="f-op">+</div>
              <div class="f-box" style="border-color:var(--gold);"><span class="f-label">que</span><span class="f-value" style="color:var(--gold);">que</span></div>
              <div class="f-op">+</div>
              <div class="f-box" style="border-color:var(--purple);"><span class="f-label">Sujet + subjonctif</span><span class="f-value" style="color:var(--purple);">je parte</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <h3 style="margin-top:0;">IL FAUT QUE — conjugated for every person</h3>
              <table class="subj-table">
                <tr><td>Il faut que je</td><td class="key-form">parte</td><td>Il faut que nous</td><td class="key-form">partions</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Il faut que tu</td><td class="key-form">partes</td><td>Il faut que vous</td><td class="key-form">partiez</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Il faut qu'il/elle</td><td class="key-form">parte</td><td>Il faut qu'ils/elles</td><td class="key-form">partent</td></tr>
              </table>
              <p class="gloss">Note that <em>il faut</em> itself never changes — only the second verb is conjugated.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="subj-nec-3" data-step="Exceptions">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">3</span> Exceptions</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Les exceptions — certitude et infinitif</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box red content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--crimson);">Certainty → INDICATIF</h3>
                <p>Impersonal expressions of <strong>certainty</strong> do NOT take the subjonctif:</p>
                <p class="example-text">Il est <strong>vrai</strong> qu'il <span class="highlight hl-verb">est</span> tard.</p>
                <p class="gloss">It's true that it is late.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Il est <strong>évident</strong> qu'elle <span class="highlight hl-verb">a</span> raison.</p>
                <p class="gloss">It is obvious she is right.</p>
                <p class="gloss">Also: il est certain / clair / sûr que → indicatif.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">No specific person → infinitif</h3>
                <p>When the obligation applies to everyone in general, drop <em>que</em>:</p>
                <p class="example-text">Il faut <span class="highlight hl-verb">travailler</span> pour réussir.</p>
                <p class="gloss">One must work to succeed. — general truth</p>
                <p class="example-text">Il faut que tu <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">travailles</span>.</p>
                <p class="gloss">YOU must work. — specific person</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field"><strong>Negation flips it back:</strong> <em>Il n'est pas vrai qu'il <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">soit</span> tard.</em>
              <span class="gloss">It is not true that it is late.</span> — once certainty is denied, the subjonctif returns.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="subj-nec-4" data-step="Pièges">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">4</span> Pièges</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">⚠️ Trap Alert — <em>il faut</em> vs <em>devoir</em></h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">IL FAUT QUE + subjonctif</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Il faut que je <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">finisse</span> ce travail.</p>
                <p class="gloss">I must finish this work.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box green content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--green);">DEVOIR + infinitif</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Je <span class="highlight hl-verb">dois finir</span> ce travail.</p>
                <p class="gloss">I must finish this work. — same meaning, no subjunctive</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box red content-box fragment">
              <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--crimson);">Common errors</h3>
              <p class="example-text">✗ Il faut que je <span class="highlight hl-neg">dois</span> partir. <span class="gloss">don't stack both structures</span></p>
              <p class="example-text">✗ Il faut que tu <span class="highlight hl-neg">vas</span> à l'école. <span class="gloss">aller → ailles</span></p>
              <p class="example-text">✗ Il est important <span class="highlight hl-neg">de</span> tu viennes. <span class="gloss">use <em>que</em> before a subject</span></p>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">💡 If the sentence names <strong>who</strong> must act → <em>il faut <span class="highlight hl-aux">que</span></em> + subjonctif.
              If it is advice to people in general → <em>il faut</em> + infinitive. Decide that first, then conjugate.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="subj-nec-5" data-step="Exemples">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">5</span> Exemples travaillés</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Worked examples</h2>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-aux">Il faut que</span> nous <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">soyons</span> à la gare avant huit heures.</p>
              <p class="gloss">We must be at the station before eight.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-aux">Il est important qu'</span>elle <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">sache</span> la vérité.</p>
              <p class="gloss">It is important that she knows the truth. — savoir → sache</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-aux">Il vaut mieux que</span> tu <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">prennes</span> un taxi.</p>
              <p class="gloss">It's better that you take a taxi. — prendre → prennes</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-aux">Il se peut qu'</span>il <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">pleuve</span> demain.</p>
              <p class="gloss">It may rain tomorrow.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="subj-nec-6" data-step="En contexte">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">6</span> En contexte</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">In context — giving strong advice</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">L.7 — En pleine forme</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Il faut que tu <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">manges</span> plus de légumes.</p>
                <p class="gloss">You must eat more vegetables.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Il est essentiel que nous <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">fassions</span> du sport.</p>
                <p class="gloss">It is essential that we do sport.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">L.8 — L'environnement</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Il faut que chacun <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">fasse</span> un effort.</p>
                <p class="gloss">Everyone must make an effort.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Il est nécessaire que les villes <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">réduisent</span> la pollution.</p>
                <p class="gloss">It is necessary that cities reduce pollution.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">💡 <strong>Advice letters:</strong> vary your structures — one <em>impératif</em> (<em>Mange bien !</em>),
              one <em>conditionnel</em> (<em>tu devrais…</em>), one <em>subjonctif</em> (<em>Il faut que tu…</em>). Three different structures reads far better than three imperatives.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="subj-nec-7" data-step="Pratique QCM">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">7</span> Pratique — QCM</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Choose the correct form</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="ailles">
                <p class="q-text">1. Il faut que tu _____ chez le médecin. <span class="gloss">(aller)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">vas</button><button class="option-btn">ailles</button><button class="option-btn">iras</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="puissions">
                <p class="q-text">2. <span class="q-tag">CBSE 2024</span>Il est important que nous _____ assister à cette fête. <span class="gloss">(pouvoir)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">pouvons</button><button class="option-btn">puissions</button><button class="option-btn">pourrons</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="est">
                <p class="q-text">3. Il est évident qu'il _____ fatigué. <span class="gloss">(être)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">soit</button><button class="option-btn">est</button><button class="option-btn">serait</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="fasse">
                <p class="q-text">4. Il vaut mieux qu'elle _____ ses devoirs maintenant. <span class="gloss">(faire)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">fait</button><button class="option-btn">fasse</button><button class="option-btn">fera</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="travailler">
                <p class="q-text">5. Il faut _____ pour réussir dans la vie. <span class="gloss">(travailler — général)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">travailler</button><button class="option-btn">que travaille</button><button class="option-btn">qu'on travaillera</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="subj-nec-8" data-step="Pratique — à compléter">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">8</span> Pratique — à compléter</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Complete the sentence</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">1. Il faut que je _____ (finir) ce travail ce soir.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="finisse" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">2. Il est nécessaire que vous _____ (être) présents.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="soyez" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">3. Il est temps que nous _____ (partir).</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="partions" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">4. Il se peut qu'ils _____ (venir) plus tard.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="viennent" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">5. Il vaut mieux que tu _____ (prendre) ton parapluie.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="prennes" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="accent-bar">
                <span class="ab-label">Accents :</span>
                <button class="accent-key">é</button><button class="accent-key">è</button><button class="accent-key">ê</button>
                <button class="accent-key">à</button><button class="accent-key">ç</button><button class="accent-key">ù</button>
                <button class="accent-key">û</button><button class="accent-key">î</button><button class="accent-key">ô</button>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn fib-check student-only">✓ Vérifier</button>
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
