      <!-- ================= 3.6 NE… QUE ================= -->
      <section data-topic="negation" data-topic-name="La Négation" data-sub="Ne… que">

        <section data-slide-id="neg-que-1" data-step="Description">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">1</span> Description</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Ne… que — "only" (a restriction, not a negation)</h2>
            <p class="editable-field">Despite the <em>ne</em>, this structure is <strong>not negative</strong>. It restricts: it says the sentence is true of <em>only</em> that one thing.</p>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <p class="example-text">Je <span class="highlight hl-neg">n'</span>ai <span class="highlight hl-aux">que</span> dix euros.</p>
              <p class="gloss">I only have ten euros. — I <em>do</em> have money; just not much.</p>
              <p class="example-text">Il <span class="highlight hl-neg">ne</span> boit <span class="highlight hl-aux">que</span> de l'eau.</p>
              <p class="gloss">He only drinks water. — he definitely drinks.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field"><strong>Synonyme:</strong> <em>seulement</em> means the same thing —
                <em>J'ai <span class="highlight hl-aux">seulement</span> dix euros</em> = <em>Je <span class="highlight hl-neg">n'</span>ai <span class="highlight hl-aux">que</span> dix euros.</em>
                Being able to rewrite one as the other is a classic exam task.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="neg-que-2" data-step="Formation">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">2</span> Formation</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">La formule — QUE se place devant l'élément restreint</h2>
            <div class="formula-pipeline">
              <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Sujet + NE</span><span class="f-value">Je ne</span></div>
              <div class="f-op">+</div>
              <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Verbe</span><span class="f-value">mange</span></div>
              <div class="f-op">+</div>
              <div class="f-box" style="border-color:var(--gold);"><span class="f-label">QUE + l'élément</span><span class="f-value" style="color:var(--gold);">que des légumes</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <p class="editable-field">Move <em>que</em> and you change the meaning — it always sits <strong>immediately before</strong> what is restricted:</p>
              <table class="subj-table">
                <tr><td>Je <strong>ne</strong> lis <span class="key-form">que</span> des romans le soir.</td><td class="gloss">I read only novels in the evening. (nothing else)</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Je <strong>ne</strong> lis des romans <span class="key-form">que</span> le soir.</td><td class="gloss">I read novels only in the evening. (not at other times)</td></tr>
              </table>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--green);">Temps composé — que après le participe</h3>
              <p class="example-text">Je <span class="highlight hl-neg">n'</span>ai <span class="highlight hl-verb">bu</span> <span class="highlight hl-aux">que</span> de l'eau.</p>
              <p class="gloss">I only drank water. — like <em>personne</em>, it follows the participle</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="neg-que-3" data-step="Exceptions">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">3</span> Exceptions</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">L'exception majeure — l'article NE change PAS</h2>
            <p class="editable-field">This is what separates <em>ne… que</em> from every real negation.</p>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box red content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--crimson);">Vraie négation → DE</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Je <span class="highlight hl-neg">ne</span> bois <span class="highlight hl-neg">pas</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">de</span> café.</p>
                <p class="gloss">I don't drink coffee.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Il <span class="highlight hl-neg">n'</span>a <span class="highlight hl-neg">pas</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">de</span> frères.</p>
                <p class="gloss">He has no brothers.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box green content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--green);">Restriction → article normal</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Je <span class="highlight hl-neg">ne</span> bois <span class="highlight hl-aux">que</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">du</span> café.</p>
                <p class="gloss">I only drink coffee.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Il <span class="highlight hl-neg">n'</span>a <span class="highlight hl-aux">que</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">des</span> frères.</p>
                <p class="gloss">He only has brothers.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field"><strong>Also:</strong> <em>ne… pas que</em> means "not only" —
              <em>Il <span class="highlight hl-neg">n'</span>y a <span class="highlight hl-neg">pas que</span> toi qui travailles !</em>
              <span class="gloss">You're not the only one who works!</span></p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="neg-que-4" data-step="Pièges">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">4</span> Pièges</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">⚠️ Trap Alert — the article and the meaning</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box red content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--crimson);">✗ Wrong</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Je ne mange que <span class="highlight hl-neg">de</span> légumes.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Je ne <span class="highlight hl-neg">pas</span> mange que du riz.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Il n'a <span class="highlight hl-neg">que pas</span> un ami.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box green content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--green);">✓ Right</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Je ne mange que <span class="highlight hl-verb">des</span> légumes. <span class="gloss">article unchanged</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Je ne mange que du riz. <span class="gloss">no <em>pas</em> — <em>que</em> replaces it</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Il n'a <span class="highlight hl-verb">qu'</span>un ami. <span class="gloss">que → qu' before a vowel</span></p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">🔑 <strong>Test it:</strong> replace <em>ne… que</em> with <em>seulement</em>. If the sentence still makes sense, it is a restriction — so keep the normal article.
                <em>Je ne bois que du thé</em> → <em>Je bois seulement du thé</em> ✓</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="neg-que-5" data-step="Exemples">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">5</span> Exemples travaillés</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Worked examples</h2>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <p class="example-text">Je <span class="highlight hl-neg">n'</span>ai <span class="highlight hl-aux">qu'</span>une sœur.</p>
              <p class="gloss">I only have one sister. — qu' before a vowel</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Elle <span class="highlight hl-neg">ne</span> travaille <span class="highlight hl-aux">que</span> le week-end.</p>
              <p class="gloss">She only works at weekends.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Nous <span class="highlight hl-neg">n'</span>avons <span class="highlight hl-verb">mangé</span> <span class="highlight hl-aux">que</span> du pain.</p>
              <p class="gloss">We only ate bread. — que after the participle, <em>du</em> kept</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Ce magasin <span class="highlight hl-neg">n'</span>ouvre <span class="highlight hl-aux">que</span> l'après-midi.</p>
              <p class="gloss">This shop only opens in the afternoon.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="neg-que-6" data-step="En contexte">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">6</span> En contexte</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">In context — Entre Jeunes themes</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">L.7 — En pleine forme</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Je ne bois que de l'eau pendant les repas.</p>
                <p class="gloss">I only drink water during meals.</p>
                <h3>L.4 — Le plaisir de lire</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Il ne lit que des bandes dessinées.</p>
                <p class="gloss">He only reads comics.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">L.3 — Chercher du travail</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Je n'ai qu'une année d'expérience.</p>
                <p class="gloss">I only have one year of experience.</p>
                <h3 style="color:var(--gold);">L.5 — Les médias</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Elle ne regarde que les documentaires.</p>
                <p class="gloss">She only watches documentaries.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="neg-que-7" data-step="Pratique QCM">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">7</span> Pratique — QCM</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Choose the correct form</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="que du thé">
                <p class="q-text">1. Je ne bois _____. <span class="gloss">(seulement du thé)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">que de thé</button><button class="option-btn">que du thé</button><button class="option-btn">pas de thé</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="qu'un">
                <p class="q-text">2. Il n'a _____ ami dans cette classe.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">que un</button><button class="option-btn">qu'un</button><button class="option-btn">que d'un</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="n'avons mangé que">
                <p class="q-text">3. Nous _____ des fruits. <span class="gloss">(manger — PC)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">n'avons que mangé</button><button class="option-btn">n'avons mangé que</button><button class="option-btn">avons mangé que</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="de">
                <p class="q-text">4. Je ne mange pas _____ viande. <span class="gloss">(vraie négation)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">de</button><button class="option-btn">de la</button><button class="option-btn">que de la</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="seulement le dimanche">
                <p class="q-text">5. Il ne travaille que le dimanche. = Il travaille _____.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">seulement le dimanche</button><button class="option-btn">jamais le dimanche</button><button class="option-btn">pas le dimanche</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="neg-que-8" data-step="Pratique — à compléter">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">8</span> Pratique — à compléter</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Transformez avec « ne… que »</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">1. J'ai seulement deux euros. → Je _____ deux euros.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="n'ai que" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">2. Elle mange seulement des légumes. → Elle _____ des légumes.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="ne mange que" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">3. Il travaille seulement le matin. → Il _____ le matin.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="ne travaille que" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">4. Nous avons vu seulement un film. → Nous _____ un film.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="n'avons vu qu'" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">5. Je parle seulement français. → Je _____ français.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="ne parle que" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="accent-bar">
                <span class="ab-label">Accents :</span>
                <button class="accent-key">é</button><button class="accent-key">è</button><button class="accent-key">ê</button>
                <button class="accent-key">à</button><button class="accent-key">ç</button><button class="accent-key">ù</button>
                <button class="accent-key">û</button><button class="accent-key">î</button><button class="accent-key">ô</button>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn fib-check student-only">✓ Vérifier</button>
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </section>

      <!-- ================= 3.7 NE… NI… NI ================= -->
      <section data-topic="negation" data-topic-name="La Négation" data-sub="Ne… ni… ni">

        <section data-slide-id="neg-ni-1" data-step="Description">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">1</span> Description</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Ne… ni… ni — neither… nor</h2>
            <p class="editable-field">Used to negate <strong>two or more elements at once</strong>. It is the negative of <em>et… et</em> or <em>ou… ou</em>.</p>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <p class="example-text">J'aime <span class="highlight hl-verb">le thé et le café</span>.</p>
              <p class="gloss">I like tea and coffee.</p>
              <p class="example-text">Je <span class="highlight hl-neg">n'</span>aime <span class="highlight hl-neg">ni</span> le thé <span class="highlight hl-neg">ni</span> le café.</p>
              <p class="gloss">I like neither tea nor coffee.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">It can join <strong>nouns, adjectives or verbs</strong>:</p>
              <p class="example-text">Il <span class="highlight hl-neg">n'</span>est <span class="highlight hl-neg">ni</span> grand <span class="highlight hl-neg">ni</span> petit. <span class="gloss">He is neither tall nor short.</span></p>
              <p class="example-text">Elle <span class="highlight hl-neg">ne</span> veut <span class="highlight hl-neg">ni</span> sortir <span class="highlight hl-neg">ni</span> rester. <span class="gloss">She wants neither to go out nor to stay.</span></p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="neg-ni-2" data-step="Formation">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">2</span> Formation</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">La formule</h2>
            <div class="formula-pipeline">
              <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Sujet + NE</span><span class="f-value">Je n'</span></div>
              <div class="f-op">+</div>
              <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Verbe</span><span class="f-value">aime</span></div>
              <div class="f-op">+</div>
              <div class="f-box" style="border-color:var(--crimson);"><span class="f-label">NI … NI …</span><span class="f-value" style="color:var(--crimson);">ni X ni Y</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Comme complément</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Il <span class="highlight hl-neg">ne</span> boit <span class="highlight hl-neg">ni</span> vin <span class="highlight hl-neg">ni</span> bière.</p>
                <p class="gloss">He drinks neither wine nor beer.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Comme sujet — <em>ne</em> reste devant le verbe</h3>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-neg">Ni</span> Paul <span class="highlight hl-neg">ni</span> Marie <span class="highlight hl-neg">ne</span> sont venus.</p>
                <p class="gloss">Neither Paul nor Marie came.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">You may repeat <em>ni</em> more than twice:
              <em>Je <span class="highlight hl-neg">n'</span>ai <span class="highlight hl-neg">ni</span> stylo <span class="highlight hl-neg">ni</span> crayon <span class="highlight hl-neg">ni</span> gomme.</em>
              <span class="gloss">I have neither pen nor pencil nor eraser.</span></p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="neg-ni-3" data-step="Exceptions">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">3</span> Exceptions</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">L'article disparaît — sauf l'article défini</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box red content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--crimson);">Indéfini / partitif → SUPPRIMÉ</h3>
                <p>un, une, des, du, de la disappear completely — not even <em>de</em> remains.</p>
                <p class="example-text">J'ai <strong>un</strong> frère et <strong>une</strong> sœur.<br>→ Je n'ai <span class="highlight hl-neg">ni</span> frère <span class="highlight hl-neg">ni</span> sœur.</p>
                <p class="gloss">I have neither brother nor sister.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Il boit <strong>du</strong> vin et <strong>de la</strong> bière.<br>→ Il ne boit <span class="highlight hl-neg">ni</span> vin <span class="highlight hl-neg">ni</span> bière.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box green content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--green);">Défini → CONSERVÉ</h3>
                <p>le, la, les stay exactly as they are.</p>
                <p class="example-text">J'aime <strong>le</strong> thé et <strong>le</strong> café.<br>→ Je n'aime <span class="highlight hl-neg">ni</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">le</span> thé <span class="highlight hl-neg">ni</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">le</span> café.</p>
                <p class="gloss">I like neither tea nor coffee.</p>
                <p class="gloss">Possessives also stay: <em>ni mon frère ni ma sœur</em>.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="neg-ni-4" data-step="Pièges">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">4</span> Pièges</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">⚠️ Trap Alert — no <em>pas</em>, and mind the article</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box red content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--crimson);">✗ Wrong</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Je <span class="highlight hl-neg">ne bois pas ni</span> thé ni café.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Je n'ai ni <span class="highlight hl-neg">un</span> frère ni <span class="highlight hl-neg">une</span> sœur.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Je n'ai ni <span class="highlight hl-neg">de</span> frère ni <span class="highlight hl-neg">de</span> sœur.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Ni Paul ni Marie <span class="highlight hl-neg">sont</span> venus.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box green content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--green);">✓ Right</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Je <span class="highlight hl-verb">ne bois ni</span> thé ni café. <span class="gloss">no <em>pas</em></span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Je n'ai <span class="highlight hl-verb">ni frère ni sœur</span>. <span class="gloss">article dropped</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Je n'ai ni frère ni sœur. <span class="gloss">not even <em>de</em></span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Ni Paul ni Marie <span class="highlight hl-verb">ne sont</span> venus. <span class="gloss">keep <em>ne</em></span></p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">💡 <strong>Two-step method:</strong> ① write the affirmative sentence;
              ② if the articles are <em>un/une/des/du/de la</em>, delete them; if they are <em>le/la/les</em>, keep them. Then insert <em>ni … ni</em> and remove <em>pas</em>.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="neg-ni-5" data-step="Exemples">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">5</span> Exemples travaillés</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Worked examples</h2>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <p class="example-text">Je <span class="highlight hl-neg">n'</span>ai <span class="highlight hl-neg">ni</span> frère <span class="highlight hl-neg">ni</span> sœur.</p>
              <p class="gloss">I have neither brother nor sister. — indefinite articles dropped</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Elle <span class="highlight hl-neg">n'</span>aime <span class="highlight hl-neg">ni</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">le</span> sport <span class="highlight hl-neg">ni</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">la</span> musique.</p>
              <p class="gloss">She likes neither sport nor music. — definite articles kept</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Ce film <span class="highlight hl-neg">n'</span>est <span class="highlight hl-neg">ni</span> bon <span class="highlight hl-neg">ni</span> mauvais.</p>
              <p class="gloss">This film is neither good nor bad. — adjectives</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-neg">Ni</span> mon père <span class="highlight hl-neg">ni</span> ma mère <span class="highlight hl-neg">ne</span> parlent français.</p>
              <p class="gloss">Neither my father nor my mother speaks French. — as subject</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="neg-ni-6" data-step="En contexte">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">6</span> En contexte</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">In context — Entre Jeunes themes</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">L.6 — Chacun ses goûts</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Je n'aime ni le rap ni le jazz.</p>
                <p class="gloss">I like neither rap nor jazz.</p>
                <h3>L.7 — En pleine forme</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Il ne fume ni ne boit.</p>
                <p class="gloss">He neither smokes nor drinks.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">L.2 — Après le bac</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Je ne veux étudier ni la médecine ni le droit.</p>
                <p class="gloss">I want to study neither medicine nor law.</p>
                <h3 style="color:var(--gold);">L.8 — L'environnement</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Cette ville n'a ni parcs ni jardins.</p>
                <p class="gloss">This town has neither parks nor gardens.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="neg-ni-7" data-step="Pratique QCM">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">7</span> Pratique — QCM</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Choose the correct form</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="ni frère ni sœur">
                <p class="q-text">1. Je n'ai _____. <span class="gloss">(un frère / une sœur)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">ni un frère ni une sœur</button><button class="option-btn">ni frère ni sœur</button><button class="option-btn">ni de frère ni de sœur</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="ni le thé ni le café">
                <p class="q-text">2. Je n'aime _____. <span class="gloss">(le thé / le café)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">ni thé ni café</button><button class="option-btn">ni le thé ni le café</button><button class="option-btn">ni du thé ni du café</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="ne sont">
                <p class="q-text">3. Ni Marc ni Léa _____ venus.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">sont</button><button class="option-btn">ne sont</button><button class="option-btn">n'ont</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="n'est ni grand ni petit">
                <p class="q-text">4. Il _____. <span class="gloss">(grand / petit)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">n'est pas ni grand ni petit</button><button class="option-btn">n'est ni grand ni petit</button><button class="option-btn">est ni grand ni petit</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="ni vin ni bière">
                <p class="q-text">5. Il ne boit _____. <span class="gloss">(du vin / de la bière)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">ni vin ni bière</button><button class="option-btn">ni du vin ni de la bière</button><button class="option-btn">ni de vin ni de bière</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="neg-ni-8" data-step="Pratique — à compléter">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">8</span> Pratique — à compléter</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Transformez avec « ne… ni… ni »</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">1. J'ai un chat et un chien. → Je n'ai _____.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="ni chat ni chien" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">2. Elle aime la danse et le théâtre. → Elle n'aime _____.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="ni la danse ni le théâtre" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">3. Paul et Marie sont venus. → Ni Paul ni Marie _____ venus.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="ne sont" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">4. Il est riche et célèbre. → Il n'est _____.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="ni riche ni célèbre" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">5. Nous mangeons du poisson et de la viande. → Nous ne mangeons _____.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="ni poisson ni viande" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="accent-bar">
                <span class="ab-label">Accents :</span>
                <button class="accent-key">é</button><button class="accent-key">è</button><button class="accent-key">ê</button>
                <button class="accent-key">à</button><button class="accent-key">ç</button><button class="accent-key">ù</button>
                <button class="accent-key">û</button><button class="accent-key">î</button><button class="accent-key">ô</button>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn fib-check student-only">✓ Vérifier</button>
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </section>

      <!-- ================= TOPIC 3 CLOSER ================= -->
      <section data-topic="negation" data-topic-name="La Négation" data-sub="Synthèse &amp; Examen">

        <section data-slide-id="neg-fin-1" data-step="Tableau de référence">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">📊 Tableau de référence — toutes les négations</h2>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <table class="subj-table">
                <tr><th>Négation</th><th>Sens</th><th>Position (PC)</th><th>Article</th></tr>
                <tr><td class="key-form">ne… pas</td><td>not</td><td>n'ai <strong>pas</strong> vu</td><td>→ de</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="key-form">ne… jamais</td><td>never</td><td>n'ai <strong>jamais</strong> vu</td><td>→ de</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="key-form">ne… plus</td><td>no longer</td><td>n'ai <strong>plus</strong> vu</td><td>→ de</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="key-form">ne… rien</td><td>nothing</td><td>n'ai <strong>rien</strong> vu</td><td>→ de</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="key-form">ne… personne</td><td>nobody</td><td>n'ai vu <strong>personne</strong></td><td>→ de</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="key-form">ne… que</td><td>only</td><td>n'ai vu <strong>que</strong>…</td><td><strong>inchangé</strong></td></tr>
                <tr><td class="key-form">ne… ni… ni</td><td>neither… nor</td><td>n'ai vu <strong>ni</strong> X <strong>ni</strong> Y</td><td><strong>supprimé</strong></td></tr>
              </table>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">🔑 <strong>Three things decide every answer:</strong> ① which second word,
              ② where it goes in a compound tense, ③ what happens to the article. The last two rows are the exceptions — learn them separately.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="neg-fin-2" data-step="Examen CBSE">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">📝 Examen blanc — La Négation</h2>
            <p class="editable-field gloss">Mettez les phrases à la forme négative en utilisant l'expression indiquée.</p>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text"><span class="q-tag">CBSE 2024</span>1. Voulez-vous du sel ou du poivre ? → Je ne veux _____ sel _____ poivre. <span class="gloss">(ni… ni — écrivez « ni ... ni »)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="ni ... ni|ni…ni|ni ni" placeholder="ni ... ni"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text"><span class="q-tag">CBSE 2024</span>2. Tout le monde sait nager dans votre classe ? → _____ sait nager. <span class="gloss">(personne)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="personne ne" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">3. J'ai encore de l'argent. → Je _____ argent. <span class="gloss">(ne… plus)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="n'ai plus d'" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">4. Il a tout compris. → Il _____. <span class="gloss">(ne… rien)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="n'a rien compris" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">5. Elle va souvent au cinéma. → Elle _____ au cinéma. <span class="gloss">(ne… jamais)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="ne va jamais" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">6. J'ai seulement un livre. → Je _____ livre. <span class="gloss">(ne… que)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="n'ai qu'un" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="accent-bar">
                <span class="ab-label">Accents :</span>
                <button class="accent-key">é</button><button class="accent-key">è</button><button class="accent-key">ê</button>
                <button class="accent-key">à</button><button class="accent-key">ç</button><button class="accent-key">ù</button>
                <button class="accent-key">û</button><button class="accent-key">î</button><button class="accent-key">ô</button>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn fib-check student-only">✓ Vérifier</button>
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 6</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="neg-fin-3" data-step="Check-list">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">✅ Check-list — La Négation</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <p>☐ Did I write <strong>ne</strong> (or n')? It is never optional in writing.</p>
                <p>☐ Only <strong>one</strong> second word — no <em>pas</em> stacked with <em>jamais/rien/personne/que/ni</em>.</p>
                <p>☐ Compound tense: is the second word in the right place? <em>rien</em> before, <em>personne</em> and <em>que</em> after.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <p>☐ Article: <em>un/une/des/du/de la</em> → <strong>de</strong> after a true negation.</p>
                <p>☐ But after <strong>ne… que</strong> the article is <strong>unchanged</strong>.</p>
                <p>☐ And after <strong>ni… ni</strong> the indefinite article is <strong>deleted</strong>.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">🎯 <strong>Exam note:</strong> La Négation is 5 marks in Section C and appears almost every year — often as
              "mettez à la forme négative". The marks are won or lost on the <strong>article</strong> and the <strong>position</strong>, not on knowing the words.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </section>
      <!-- ==================================================================
           TOPIC 4 — LES PRONOMS PERSONNELS
           =================================================================== -->
      <section data-topic="pronoms" data-topic-name="Les Pronoms Personnels" data-sub="Le COD">

        <section data-slide-id="cod-1" data-step="Description">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">1</span> Description</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Le COD — direct object pronouns</h2>
            <p class="editable-field">A <strong>COD</strong> (complément d'objet direct) answers <em>qui ?</em> or <em>quoi ?</em> straight after the verb — with <strong>no preposition</strong> in between.</p>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Comment le trouver</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Je regarde <span class="highlight hl-verb">la télévision</span>.</p>
                <p class="gloss">Je regarde <strong>quoi</strong> ? → la télévision = COD</p>
                <p class="example-text">→ Je <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">la</span> regarde.</p>
                <p class="gloss">I watch it.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Les six pronoms COD</h3>
                <table class="subj-table">
                  <tr><td>me / m'</td><td class="gloss">me</td><td>nous</td><td class="gloss">us</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>te / t'</td><td class="gloss">you</td><td>vous</td><td class="gloss">you</td></tr>
                  <tr><td class="key-form">le / la / l'</td><td class="gloss">him / her / it</td><td class="key-form">les</td><td class="gloss">them</td></tr>
                </table>
                <p class="gloss">Only <em>le, la, les</em> are new — the others are the same as the COI.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="cod-2" data-step="Formation">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">2</span> Formation</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">La formule — le pronom passe DEVANT le verbe</h2>
            <div class="formula-pipeline">
              <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Sujet</span><span class="f-value">Je</span></div>
              <div class="f-op">+</div>
              <div class="f-box" style="border-color:var(--purple);"><span class="f-label">Pronom COD</span><span class="f-value" style="color:var(--purple);">le / la / les</span></div>
              <div class="f-op">+</div>
              <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Verbe</span><span class="f-value">regarde</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Temps simple</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Je <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">le</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">vois</span>.</p>
                <p class="gloss">I see him/it.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Nous <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">les</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">connaissons</span>.</p>
                <p class="gloss">We know them.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Autres structures</h3>
                <p><strong>Passé composé</strong> — before the auxiliary:<br>
                  <em>Je <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">l'</span>ai vu.</em> <span class="gloss">I saw him.</span></p>
                <p><strong>Négation</strong> — inside the sandwich:<br>
                  <em>Je <span class="highlight hl-neg">ne</span> <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">le</span> vois <span class="highlight hl-neg">pas</span>.</em></p>
                <p><strong>Infinitif</strong> — before the infinitive:<br>
                  <em>Je vais <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">le</span> faire.</em> <span class="gloss">I'm going to do it.</span></p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="cod-3" data-step="Exceptions">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">3</span> Exceptions</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">L'accord du participe passé</h2>
            <p class="editable-field">This is the rule that makes the COD worth knowing: with <strong>avoir</strong>, the participle agrees with a COD that comes <strong>before</strong> the verb.</p>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <table class="subj-table">
                <tr><th>Sans pronom (pas d'accord)</th><th>Avec pronom COD (accord)</th></tr>
                <tr><td>J'ai vu <strong>le film</strong>.</td><td>Je <span class="key-form">l'</span>ai <span class="key-form">vu</span>. <span class="gloss">masc. sing.</span></td></tr>
                <tr><td>J'ai vu <strong>la pièce</strong>.</td><td>Je <span class="key-form">l'</span>ai <span class="key-form">vue</span>. <span class="gloss">+ e</span></td></tr>
                <tr><td>J'ai vu <strong>les films</strong>.</td><td>Je <span class="key-form">les</span> ai <span class="key-form">vus</span>. <span class="gloss">+ s</span></td></tr>
                <tr><td>J'ai vu <strong>les pièces</strong>.</td><td>Je <span class="key-form">les</span> ai <span class="key-form">vues</span>. <span class="gloss">+ es</span></td></tr>
              </table>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field"><strong>L'impératif affirmatif</strong> is the one place the pronoun goes <strong>after</strong> the verb, with a hyphen:
                <em><span class="highlight hl-verb">Regarde-le</span> !</em> <span class="gloss">Look at it!</span> ·
                <em><span class="highlight hl-verb">Prends-les</span> !</em> <span class="gloss">Take them!</span><br>
                But in the negative it returns to its normal place: <em><span class="highlight hl-neg">Ne</span> <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">le</span> regarde <span class="highlight hl-neg">pas</span> !</em></p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="cod-4" data-step="Pièges">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">4</span> Pièges</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">⚠️ Trap Alert — COD or COI?</h2>
            <p class="editable-field">Look for the preposition <strong>à</strong>. No <em>à</em> → COD. With <em>à</em> → COI.</p>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">COD — pas de préposition</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Je vois <span class="highlight hl-verb">Marie</span>. → Je <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">la</span> vois.</p>
                <p class="gloss">voir quelqu'un — direct</p>
                <p class="example-text">J'aime <span class="highlight hl-verb">ce livre</span>. → Je <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">l'</span>aime.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">COI — avec « à »</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Je parle <span class="highlight hl-aux">à</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">Marie</span>. → Je <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">lui</span> parle.</p>
                <p class="gloss">parler à quelqu'un — indirect</p>
                <p class="example-text">Je téléphone <span class="highlight hl-aux">à</span> mes amis. → Je <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">leur</span> téléphone.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box red content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field"><strong>Beware the English mismatch:</strong> some verbs are direct in French but indirect in English, and vice versa.<br>
                <em>écouter <span class="highlight hl-verb">la radio</span></em> <span class="gloss">to listen TO the radio — but direct in French → je l'écoute</span><br>
                <em>regarder <span class="highlight hl-verb">la télé</span></em> <span class="gloss">to look AT the TV — direct in French → je la regarde</span><br>
                <em>téléphoner <span class="highlight hl-aux">à</span> Paul</em> <span class="gloss">to phone Paul — indirect in French → je lui téléphone</span></p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="cod-5" data-step="Exemples">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">5</span> Exemples travaillés</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Worked examples</h2>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <p class="example-text">Tu connais <span class="highlight hl-verb">mon frère</span> ? → Oui, je <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">le</span> connais.</p>
              <p class="gloss">Do you know my brother? — Yes, I know him.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Elle a acheté <span class="highlight hl-verb">ces chaussures</span>. → Elle <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">les</span> a <span class="highlight hl-verb">achetées</span>.</p>
              <p class="gloss">She bought these shoes → She bought them. — agreement: fem. plural</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Je <span class="highlight hl-neg">ne</span> <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">t'</span>ai <span class="highlight hl-neg">pas</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">oublié</span>.</p>
              <p class="gloss">I haven't forgotten you.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Ce devoir ? Je vais <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">le</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">finir</span> ce soir.</p>
              <p class="gloss">This homework? I'm going to finish it tonight. — before the infinitive</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="cod-6" data-step="En contexte">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">6</span> En contexte</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">In context — avoiding repetition</h2>
            <p class="editable-field gloss">Pronouns exist so you don't repeat the noun. Using them is what makes writing sound natural.</p>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box red content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--crimson);">Lourd — répétitif</h3>
                <p class="example-text">J'ai acheté ce livre. J'ai lu ce livre et j'ai aimé ce livre.</p>
                <p class="gloss">I bought this book. I read this book and I liked this book.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box green content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--green);">Naturel — avec pronoms</h3>
                <p class="example-text">J'ai acheté ce livre. Je <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">l'</span>ai lu et je <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">l'</span>ai aimé.</p>
                <p class="gloss">I bought this book. I read it and I liked it.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <h3 style="margin-top:0;">L.4 — Le plaisir de lire</h3>
              <p class="example-text">Ce roman ? Je <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">l'</span>ai lu trois fois.</p>
              <p class="gloss">This novel? I've read it three times.</p>
              <h3>L.5 — Les médias</h3>
              <p class="example-text">Les informations, je <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">les</span> regarde tous les soirs.</p>
              <p class="gloss">The news, I watch it every evening.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="cod-7" data-step="Pratique QCM">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">7</span> Pratique — QCM</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Replace with the correct COD pronoun</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="Je la regarde">
                <p class="q-text">1. Je regarde la télévision. → _____</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">Je le regarde</button><button class="option-btn">Je la regarde</button><button class="option-btn">Je lui regarde</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="Nous les invitons">
                <p class="q-text">2. Nous invitons nos cousins. → _____</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">Nous les invitons</button><button class="option-btn">Nous leur invitons</button><button class="option-btn">Nous en invitons</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="Je l'ai vue">
                <p class="q-text">3. J'ai vu Sophie. → _____</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">Je l'ai vu</button><button class="option-btn">Je l'ai vue</button><button class="option-btn">Je lui ai vu</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="Prends-le">
                <p class="q-text">4. Prends ce stylo ! → _____ !</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">Le prends</button><button class="option-btn">Prends-le</button><button class="option-btn">Prends-lui</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="Je ne les aime pas">
                <p class="q-text">5. Je n'aime pas ces gâteaux. → _____</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">Je ne les aime pas</button><button class="option-btn">Je n'aime pas les</button><button class="option-btn">Je ne leur aime pas</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="cod-8" data-step="Pratique — à compléter">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">8</span> Pratique — à compléter</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Remplacez le mot souligné par un pronom COD</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">1. Je lis <u>le journal</u>. → Je _____ lis.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="le" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">2. Elle aide <u>ses amies</u>. → Elle _____ aide.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="les" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">3. Nous avons fini <u>la leçon</u>. → Nous _____ avons finie.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="l'" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">4. Il va acheter <u>ce vélo</u>. → Il va _____ acheter.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="l'" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">5. Écoute <u>cette chanson</u> ! → Écoute-_____ !</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="la" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="accent-bar">
                <span class="ab-label">Accents :</span>
                <button class="accent-key">é</button><button class="accent-key">è</button><button class="accent-key">ê</button>
                <button class="accent-key">à</button><button class="accent-key">ç</button><button class="accent-key">ù</button>
                <button class="accent-key">û</button><button class="accent-key">î</button><button class="accent-key">ô</button>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn fib-check student-only">✓ Vérifier</button>
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </section>

      <!-- ================= 4.2 LE COI ================= -->
      <section data-topic="pronoms" data-topic-name="Les Pronoms Personnels" data-sub="Le COI">

        <section data-slide-id="coi-1" data-step="Description">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">1</span> Description</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Le COI — indirect object pronouns</h2>
            <p class="editable-field">A <strong>COI</strong> answers <em>à qui ?</em> — the verb reaches the person <strong>through the preposition à</strong>. It is almost always a person.</p>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Comment le trouver</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Je parle <span class="highlight hl-aux">à</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">mon père</span>.</p>
                <p class="gloss">Je parle <strong>à qui</strong> ? → à mon père = COI</p>
                <p class="example-text">→ Je <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">lui</span> parle.</p>
                <p class="gloss">I speak to him.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Les six pronoms COI</h3>
                <table class="subj-table">
                  <tr><td>me / m'</td><td class="gloss">to me</td><td>nous</td><td class="gloss">to us</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>te / t'</td><td class="gloss">to you</td><td>vous</td><td class="gloss">to you</td></tr>
                  <tr><td class="key-form">lui</td><td class="gloss">to him / to her</td><td class="key-form">leur</td><td class="gloss">to them</td></tr>
                </table>
                <p class="gloss">⚠️ <strong>lui</strong> covers both genders; <strong>leur</strong> never takes an -s.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="coi-2" data-step="Formation">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">2</span> Formation</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">La formule — même place que le COD</h2>
            <div class="formula-pipeline">
              <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Sujet</span><span class="f-value">Je</span></div>
              <div class="f-op">+</div>
              <div class="f-box" style="border-color:var(--purple);"><span class="f-label">Pronom COI</span><span class="f-value" style="color:var(--purple);">lui / leur</span></div>
              <div class="f-op">+</div>
              <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Verbe</span><span class="f-value">parle</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Les verbes qui demandent « à »</h3>
              <p>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">parler à</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">téléphoner à</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">donner à</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">dire à</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">écrire à</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">demander à</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">répondre à</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">offrir à</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">montrer à</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">envoyer à</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">prêter à</span>
              </p>
              <p class="gloss">Learn these as a block — they are the ones that appear in the exam.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field"><strong>Pas d'accord du participe avec le COI :</strong>
                <em>Je <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">lui</span> ai <span class="highlight hl-verb">parlé</span>.</em> ·
                <em>Je <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">leur</span> ai <span class="highlight hl-verb">écrit</span>.</em>
                <span class="gloss">Never "parlée" or "écrits" — agreement happens with the COD only.</span></p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="coi-3" data-step="Exceptions">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">3</span> Exceptions</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Les exceptions — les verbes qui gardent « à + pronom tonique »</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box red content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--crimson);">Verbes « à + tonique »</h3>
                <p>A few verbs refuse <em>lui/leur</em> and keep <em>à</em> + a stressed pronoun:</p>
                <p><span class="highlight hl-aux">penser à</span> · <span class="highlight hl-aux">faire attention à</span> ·
                   <span class="highlight hl-aux">s'intéresser à</span> · <span class="highlight hl-aux">s'habituer à</span> ·
                   <span class="highlight hl-aux">tenir à</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Je pense <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">à lui</span>. <span class="gloss">I think about him.</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">✗ <em>Je lui pense.</em></p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">L'impératif affirmatif</h3>
                <p>me → <strong>moi</strong>, and the pronoun follows with a hyphen:</p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-verb">Donne-moi</span> le livre !</p>
                <p class="gloss">Give me the book!</p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-verb">Téléphone-lui</span> ce soir !</p>
                <p class="gloss">Phone him/her tonight!</p>
                <p class="gloss">Negative: <em>Ne <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">me</span> donne pas…</em></p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="coi-4" data-step="Pièges">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">4</span> Pièges</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">⚠️ Trap Alert — <em>lui</em> has two jobs</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">LUI = pronom COI</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Je <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">lui</span> parle.</p>
                <p class="gloss">I speak to him <strong>or</strong> to her — gender-neutral.</p>
                <p class="gloss">Placed before the verb.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">LUI = pronom tonique</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Je pense à <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">lui</span>.</p>
                <p class="gloss">I think about <strong>him</strong> — masculine only (elle for her).</p>
                <p class="gloss">Placed after a preposition.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box red content-box fragment">
              <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--crimson);">Erreurs fréquentes</h3>
              <p class="example-text">✗ Je <span class="highlight hl-neg">leurs</span> ai parlé. → ✓ Je <span class="highlight hl-verb">leur</span> ai parlé. <span class="gloss">leur is invariable as a pronoun</span></p>
              <p class="example-text">✗ Je <span class="highlight hl-neg">lui</span> ai vu. → ✓ Je <span class="highlight hl-verb">l'</span>ai vu. <span class="gloss">voir is direct</span></p>
              <p class="example-text">✗ Je <span class="highlight hl-neg">le</span> téléphone. → ✓ Je <span class="highlight hl-verb">lui</span> téléphone. <span class="gloss">téléphoner à</span></p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="coi-5" data-step="Exemples">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">5</span> Exemples travaillés</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Worked examples</h2>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <p class="example-text">Je téléphone <span class="highlight hl-aux">à ma sœur</span>. → Je <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">lui</span> téléphone.</p>
              <p class="gloss">I phone my sister → I phone her.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Il a écrit <span class="highlight hl-aux">à ses parents</span>. → Il <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">leur</span> a <span class="highlight hl-verb">écrit</span>.</p>
              <p class="gloss">He wrote to his parents → He wrote to them. — no agreement</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Nous <span class="highlight hl-neg">ne</span> <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">lui</span> avons <span class="highlight hl-neg">pas</span> répondu.</p>
              <p class="gloss">We didn't answer him/her.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Ce cadeau ? Je vais <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">le</span> <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">lui</span> offrir.</p>
              <p class="gloss">This present? I'm going to give it to him. — COD + COI together</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="coi-6" data-step="En contexte">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">6</span> En contexte</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">In context — writing a letter</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Dans une lettre</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Je t'écris pour te raconter mes vacances.</p>
                <p class="gloss">I'm writing to you to tell you about my holiday.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Réponds-moi vite !</p>
                <p class="gloss">Reply to me quickly!</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">L.3 — Chercher du travail</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Le directeur m'a proposé un entretien ; je lui ai répondu tout de suite.</p>
                <p class="gloss">The director offered me an interview; I replied to him at once.</p>
                <h3 style="color:var(--gold);">L.1 — La famille</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Mes grands-parents ? Je leur téléphone chaque dimanche.</p>
                <p class="gloss">My grandparents? I phone them every Sunday.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">💡 <strong>Letter tip:</strong> <em>je t'écris, réponds-moi, dis-moi, raconte-moi</em> are ready-made COI phrases.
              They make an informal letter sound authentic and cost you nothing to memorise.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="coi-7" data-step="Pratique QCM">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">7</span> Pratique — QCM</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">COD or COI?</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="lui">
                <p class="q-text">1. Je parle à Paul. → Je _____ parle.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">le</button><button class="option-btn">lui</button><button class="option-btn">y</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="les">
                <p class="q-text">2. J'invite mes voisins. → Je _____ invite.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">leur</button><button class="option-btn">les</button><button class="option-btn">en</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="leur">
                <p class="q-text">3. Elle écrit à ses cousines. → Elle _____ écrit.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">les</button><button class="option-btn">leur</button><button class="option-btn">leurs</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="à lui">
                <p class="q-text">4. Je pense à mon frère. → Je pense _____.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">lui</button><button class="option-btn">à lui</button><button class="option-btn">y</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="Donne-moi">
                <p class="q-text">5. Donne le livre à moi ! → _____ le livre !</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">Donne-me</button><button class="option-btn">Donne-moi</button><button class="option-btn">Me donne</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="coi-8" data-step="Pratique — à compléter">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">8</span> Pratique — à compléter</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Remplacez par un pronom COI</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">1. Je donne un cadeau <u>à ma mère</u>. → Je _____ donne un cadeau.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="lui" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">2. Il répond <u>aux élèves</u>. → Il _____ répond.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="leur" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">3. Nous avons téléphoné <u>à Marie</u>. → Nous _____ avons téléphoné.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="lui" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">4. Tu montres les photos <u>à tes amis</u> ? → Tu _____ montres les photos ?</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="leur" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">5. Écris <u>à ton oncle</u> ! → Écris-_____ !</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="lui" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="accent-bar">
                <span class="ab-label">Accents :</span>
                <button class="accent-key">é</button><button class="accent-key">è</button><button class="accent-key">ê</button>
                <button class="accent-key">à</button><button class="accent-key">ç</button><button class="accent-key">ù</button>
                <button class="accent-key">û</button><button class="accent-key">î</button><button class="accent-key">ô</button>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn fib-check student-only">✓ Vérifier</button>
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </section>

      <!-- ================= 4.3 LE PRONOM Y ================= -->
      <section data-topic="pronoms" data-topic-name="Les Pronoms Personnels" data-sub="Le pronom Y">

        <section data-slide-id="y-1" data-step="Description">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">1</span> Description</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Le pronom Y — "there" / "about it"</h2>
            <p class="editable-field"><em>Y</em> replaces a <strong>place</strong>, or a <strong>thing</strong> introduced by <em>à</em>. It never replaces a person.</p>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">① Un lieu</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Je vais <span class="highlight hl-aux">à Paris</span>. → J'<span class="highlight hl-pronoun">y</span> vais.</p>
                <p class="gloss">I'm going to Paris → I'm going there.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Il habite <span class="highlight hl-aux">en France</span>. → Il <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">y</span> habite.</p>
                <p class="gloss">Works for à, en, dans, sur, sous, chez…</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">② À + une chose</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Je pense <span class="highlight hl-aux">à mon travail</span>. → J'<span class="highlight hl-pronoun">y</span> pense.</p>
                <p class="gloss">I think about my work → I think about it.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Elle répond <span class="highlight hl-aux">à la lettre</span>. → Elle <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">y</span> répond.</p>
                <p class="gloss">⚠️ A <strong>thing</strong>, not a person.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="y-2" data-step="Formation">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">2</span> Formation</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">La formule — Y devant le verbe</h2>
            <div class="formula-pipeline">
              <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Sujet</span><span class="f-value">J'</span></div>
              <div class="f-op">+</div>
              <div class="f-box" style="border-color:var(--purple);"><span class="f-label">Y</span><span class="f-value" style="color:var(--purple);">y</span></div>
              <div class="f-op">+</div>
              <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Verbe</span><span class="f-value">vais</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Toutes les structures</h3>
                <p><strong>Présent</strong> — J'<span class="highlight hl-pronoun">y</span> vais. <span class="gloss">I'm going there.</span></p>
                <p><strong>Passé composé</strong> — J'<span class="highlight hl-pronoun">y</span> suis allé. <span class="gloss">I went there.</span></p>
                <p><strong>Négation</strong> — Je n'<span class="highlight hl-pronoun">y</span> vais pas. <span class="gloss">I'm not going there.</span></p>
                <p><strong>Infinitif</strong> — Je vais <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">y</span> aller. <span class="gloss">I'm going to go there.</span></p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">L'impératif</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Vas-<span class="highlight hl-pronoun">y</span> ! <span class="gloss">Go on! / Go there!</span></p>
                <p class="gloss">⚠️ The -s of <em>va</em> comes back before <em>y</em> for pronunciation.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Allons-<span class="highlight hl-pronoun">y</span> ! <span class="gloss">Let's go!</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">N'<span class="highlight hl-pronoun">y</span> va pas ! <span class="gloss">Don't go there!</span></p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="y-3" data-step="Exceptions">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">3</span> Exceptions</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Les exceptions — jamais pour une personne</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box red content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--crimson);">Personne → PAS de « y »</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Je pense <span class="highlight hl-aux">à mon frère</span>.</p>
                <p class="gloss">→ Je pense <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">à lui</span>. ✓</p>
                <p class="gloss">→ ✗ <em>J'y pense.</em> (would mean "about it")</p>
                <p class="example-text">Je parle <span class="highlight hl-aux">à Marie</span>. → Je <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">lui</span> parle. ✓</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Expressions figées avec « y »</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Il <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">y</span> a… <span class="gloss">There is / there are…</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Ça <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">y</span> est ! <span class="gloss">That's it! / Done!</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Je m'<span class="highlight hl-pronoun">y</span> intéresse. <span class="gloss">I'm interested in it.</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">On <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">y</span> va ? <span class="gloss">Shall we go?</span></p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field"><strong>Avec « aller » au futur:</strong> French avoids <em>y</em> before the futur of <em>aller</em> —
              one says <em>J'irai</em> rather than <em>J'y irai</em>, because the sound would clash.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="y-4" data-step="Pièges">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">4</span> Pièges</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">⚠️ Trap Alert — Y (à) vs EN (de)</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Y remplace « à … »</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Je vais <span class="highlight hl-aux">à</span> la banque. → J'<span class="highlight hl-pronoun">y</span> vais.</p>
                <p class="gloss">I'm going to the bank → there</p>
                <p class="example-text">Je pense <span class="highlight hl-aux">à</span> l'examen. → J'<span class="highlight hl-pronoun">y</span> pense.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">EN remplace « de … »</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Je viens <span class="highlight hl-aux">de</span> la banque. → J'<span class="highlight hl-pronoun">en</span> viens.</p>
                <p class="gloss">I'm coming from the bank → from there</p>
                <p class="example-text">Je parle <span class="highlight hl-aux">de</span> l'examen. → J'<span class="highlight hl-pronoun">en</span> parle.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box red content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">🔑 <strong>One-second test:</strong> find the preposition in the original sentence.
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">à</span> (or a place) → <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">y</span>.
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">de</span> (or a quantity) → <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">en</span>.
                A <strong>person</strong> → lui / leur / à + tonique.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="y-5" data-step="Exemples">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">5</span> Exemples travaillés</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Worked examples</h2>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <p class="example-text">Tu vas <span class="highlight hl-aux">au marché</span> ? → Oui, j'<span class="highlight hl-pronoun">y</span> vais.</p>
              <p class="gloss">Are you going to the market? — Yes, I'm going there.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Elle est allée <span class="highlight hl-aux">en Italie</span>. → Elle <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">y</span> est allée.</p>
              <p class="gloss">She went to Italy → She went there.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Nous <span class="highlight hl-neg">n'</span><span class="highlight hl-pronoun">y</span> avons <span class="highlight hl-neg">pas</span> pensé.</p>
              <p class="gloss">We didn't think about it.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-verb">Vas-y</span> ! Le train part dans cinq minutes.</p>
              <p class="gloss">Go on! The train leaves in five minutes.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="y-6" data-step="En contexte">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">6</span> En contexte</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">In context — Entre Jeunes themes</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">L.5 — Les voyages / médias</h3>
                <p class="example-text">La France ? J'y suis allé l'année dernière.</p>
                <p class="gloss">France? I went there last year.</p>
                <h3>L.2 — Après le bac</h3>
                <p class="example-text">L'université de Delhi ? J'y pense sérieusement.</p>
                <p class="gloss">Delhi University? I'm thinking about it seriously.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">L.7 — En pleine forme</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Le club de sport ? J'y vais trois fois par semaine.</p>
                <p class="gloss">The sports club? I go there three times a week.</p>
                <h3 style="color:var(--gold);">L.8 — L'environnement</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Au recyclage, il faut y penser tous les jours.</p>
                <p class="gloss">Recycling — one must think about it every day.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="y-7" data-step="Pratique QCM">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">7</span> Pratique — QCM</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Y, en, lui or leur?</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="y">
                <p class="q-text">1. Je vais à la bibliothèque. → J'_____ vais.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">y</button><button class="option-btn">en</button><button class="option-btn">lui</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="y">
                <p class="q-text">2. Elle pense à son avenir. → Elle _____ pense.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">lui</button><button class="option-btn">y</button><button class="option-btn">en</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="à eux">
                <p class="q-text">3. Je pense à mes parents. → Je pense _____.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">y</button><button class="option-btn">leur</button><button class="option-btn">à eux</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="Vas-y">
                <p class="q-text">4. Va au tableau ! → _____ !</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">Va-y</button><button class="option-btn">Vas-y</button><button class="option-btn">Y va</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="n'y suis pas allé">
                <p class="q-text">5. Je ne suis pas allé au cinéma. → Je _____.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">n'y suis pas allé</button><button class="option-btn">ne suis pas y allé</button><button class="option-btn">n'en suis pas allé</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="y-8" data-step="Pratique — à compléter">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">8</span> Pratique — à compléter</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Remplacez par « y »</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">1. Nous allons <u>au restaurant</u>. → Nous _____ allons.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="y" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">2. Il habite <u>à Mumbai</u>. → Il _____ habite.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="y" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">3. Elle a répondu <u>à la question</u>. → Elle _____ a répondu.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="y" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">4. <span class="q-tag">CBSE 2019</span>Entre dans ce salon ! → _____ !</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="entres-y" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">5. Je ne vais pas <u>à la piscine</u>. → Je _____ vais pas.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="n'y" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="accent-bar">
                <span class="ab-label">Accents :</span>
                <button class="accent-key">é</button><button class="accent-key">è</button><button class="accent-key">ê</button>
                <button class="accent-key">à</button><button class="accent-key">ç</button><button class="accent-key">ù</button>
                <button class="accent-key">û</button><button class="accent-key">î</button><button class="accent-key">ô</button>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn fib-check student-only">✓ Vérifier</button>
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </section>
      <!-- ================= 4.4 LE PRONOM EN ================= -->
      <section data-topic="pronoms" data-topic-name="Les Pronoms Personnels" data-sub="Le pronom EN">

        <section data-slide-id="en-1" data-step="Description">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">1</span> Description</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Le pronom EN — "of it", "some", "from there"</h2>
            <p class="editable-field"><em>En</em> replaces anything introduced by <strong>de</strong> — including partitive articles and quantities.</p>
            <div class="three-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">① Partitif (du, de la, des)</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Je bois <span class="highlight hl-aux">du</span> café. → J'<span class="highlight hl-pronoun">en</span> bois.</p>
                <p class="gloss">I drink some → I drink some.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">② De + chose</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Je parle <span class="highlight hl-aux">de</span> mon voyage. → J'<span class="highlight hl-pronoun">en</span> parle.</p>
                <p class="gloss">I talk about it.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box green content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--green);">③ Un lieu d'origine</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Je viens <span class="highlight hl-aux">de</span> Paris. → J'<span class="highlight hl-pronoun">en</span> viens.</p>
                <p class="gloss">I come from there.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field"><strong>④ Avec une quantité — le nombre reste !</strong><br>
                J'ai <span class="highlight hl-aux">trois</span> frères. → J'<span class="highlight hl-pronoun">en</span> ai <span class="highlight hl-aux">trois</span>.
                <span class="gloss">I have three of them.</span><br>
                Elle a <span class="highlight hl-aux">beaucoup</span> d'amis. → Elle <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">en</span> a <span class="highlight hl-aux">beaucoup</span>.
                <span class="gloss">She has a lot of them.</span></p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="en-2" data-step="Formation">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">2</span> Formation</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">La formule — EN devant le verbe</h2>
            <div class="formula-pipeline">
              <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Sujet</span><span class="f-value">J'</span></div>
              <div class="f-op">+</div>
              <div class="f-box" style="border-color:var(--purple);"><span class="f-label">EN</span><span class="f-value" style="color:var(--purple);">en</span></div>
              <div class="f-op">+</div>
              <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Verbe (+ quantité)</span><span class="f-value">ai trois</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Toutes les structures</h3>
                <p><strong>Présent</strong> — J'<span class="highlight hl-pronoun">en</span> veux. <span class="gloss">I want some.</span></p>
                <p><strong>Passé composé</strong> — J'<span class="highlight hl-pronoun">en</span> ai pris. <span class="gloss">I took some.</span></p>
                <p><strong>Négation</strong> — Je n'<span class="highlight hl-pronoun">en</span> veux pas. <span class="gloss">I don't want any.</span></p>
                <p><strong>Infinitif</strong> — Je vais <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">en</span> acheter. <span class="gloss">I'm going to buy some.</span></p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">L'impératif</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Prends-<span class="highlight hl-pronoun">en</span> ! <span class="gloss">Take some!</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Manges-<span class="highlight hl-pronoun">en</span> ! <span class="gloss">Eat some!</span></p>
                <p class="gloss">⚠️ The -s returns on -er verbs before <em>en</em>, exactly as before <em>y</em>.</p>
                <p class="example-text">N'<span class="highlight hl-pronoun">en</span> prends pas ! <span class="gloss">Don't take any!</span></p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="en-3" data-step="Exceptions">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">3</span> Exceptions</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Les exceptions — la quantité et les personnes</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">La quantité doit être répétée</h3>
                <p class="example-text">— Combien de livres as-tu ?<br>— J'<span class="highlight hl-pronoun">en</span> ai <span class="highlight hl-aux">cinq</span>.</p>
                <p class="gloss">I have five of them. — never just "J'en ai"</p>
                <p class="example-text">— Tu veux du pain ?<br>— Oui, j'<span class="highlight hl-pronoun">en</span> veux <span class="highlight hl-aux">un peu</span>.</p>
                <p class="gloss">Yes, I'd like a little.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Personnes → de + tonique</h3>
                <p>With <em>parler de</em> + a person, use a stressed pronoun:</p>
                <p class="example-text">Je parle <span class="highlight hl-aux">de</span> Marie. → Je parle <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">d'elle</span>.</p>
                <p class="gloss">I'm talking about her.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Je parle <span class="highlight hl-aux">de</span> mon travail. → J'<span class="highlight hl-pronoun">en</span> parle.</p>
                <p class="gloss">A thing → en.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field"><strong>Expressions figées:</strong>
                <em>Il y <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">en</span> a</em> <span class="gloss">there is/are some</span> ·
                <em>J'<span class="highlight hl-pronoun">en</span> ai assez !</em> <span class="gloss">I've had enough!</span> ·
                <em>Je m'<span class="highlight hl-pronoun">en</span> vais</em> <span class="gloss">I'm leaving</span></p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="en-4" data-step="Pièges">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">4</span> Pièges</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">⚠️ Trap Alert — forgetting the quantity</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box red content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--crimson);">✗ Wrong</h3>
                <p class="example-text">J'ai deux chats. → <span class="highlight hl-neg">J'en ai.</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Je parle de Paul. → <span class="highlight hl-neg">J'en parle.</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Je bois du thé. → <span class="highlight hl-neg">Je le bois.</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Je viens de Delhi. → <span class="highlight hl-neg">J'y viens.</span></p>
              </div>
              <div class="box green content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--green);">✓ Right</h3>
                <p class="example-text">→ J'<span class="highlight hl-verb">en</span> ai <span class="highlight hl-verb">deux</span>. <span class="gloss">keep the number</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">→ Je parle <span class="highlight hl-verb">de lui</span>. <span class="gloss">person → tonique</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">→ J'<span class="highlight hl-verb">en</span> bois. <span class="gloss">partitive → en, not le</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">→ J'<span class="highlight hl-verb">en</span> viens. <span class="gloss">de → en (y is for à)</span></p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">🔑 <strong>Decide in three steps:</strong> ① Find the preposition or article.
              ② <em>du/de la/des/de</em> → <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">en</span> · <em>à</em>/place → <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">y</span> · <em>le/la/les/ce</em> → <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">le/la/les</span>.
              ③ If a number or quantity word was there, <strong>write it again</strong> after the verb.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="en-5" data-step="Exemples">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">5</span> Exemples travaillés</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Worked examples</h2>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <p class="example-text">Tu veux <span class="highlight hl-aux">du</span> gâteau ? → Oui, j'<span class="highlight hl-pronoun">en</span> veux.</p>
              <p class="gloss">Do you want some cake? — Yes, I want some.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Elle a <span class="highlight hl-aux">beaucoup de</span> patience. → Elle <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">en</span> a <span class="highlight hl-aux">beaucoup</span>.</p>
              <p class="gloss">She has a lot of patience → She has a lot of it.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Nous avons parlé <span class="highlight hl-aux">de</span> ce problème. → Nous <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">en</span> avons parlé.</p>
              <p class="gloss">We talked about this problem → We talked about it.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Il n'y <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">en</span> a <span class="highlight hl-neg">plus</span>.</p>
              <p class="gloss">There is none left.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="en-6" data-step="En contexte">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">6</span> En contexte</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">In context — answering questions naturally</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">L.8 — Faire des achats</h3>
                <p class="example-text">— Vous voulez des pommes ?<br>— Oui, j'en veux un kilo.</p>
                <p class="gloss">— Do you want apples? — Yes, I'd like a kilo of them.</p>
                <h3>L.7 — En pleine forme</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Du sucre ? Je n'en prends jamais.</p>
                <p class="gloss">Sugar? I never take any.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">L.3 — Chercher du travail</h3>
                <p class="example-text">De l'expérience ? J'en ai deux ans.</p>
                <p class="gloss">Experience? I have two years of it.</p>
                <h3 style="color:var(--gold);">L.8 — L'environnement</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Des solutions ? Il en existe plusieurs.</p>
                <p class="gloss">Solutions? Several of them exist.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">💡 <strong>Speaking tip:</strong> in a shop dialogue, <em>J'en voudrais…</em> + quantity
              (<em>un kilo, une bouteille, deux</em>) is the natural French answer. Practise it — it appears in role-play tasks.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="en-7" data-step="Pratique QCM">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">7</span> Pratique — QCM</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Y or EN?</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="en">
                <p class="q-text">1. Je bois du lait. → J'_____ bois.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">y</button><button class="option-btn">en</button><button class="option-btn">le</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="J'en ai quatre">
                <p class="q-text">2. J'ai quatre cousins. → _____</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">J'en ai</button><button class="option-btn">J'en ai quatre</button><button class="option-btn">Je les ai quatre</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="en">
                <p class="q-text">3. Elle revient de l'école. → Elle _____ revient.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">y</button><button class="option-btn">en</button><button class="option-btn">lui</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="de lui">
                <p class="q-text">4. Je parle de mon professeur. → Je parle _____.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">en</button><button class="option-btn">de lui</button><button class="option-btn">lui</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="Prends-en">
                <p class="q-text">5. Prends du pain ! → _____ !</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">Prend-en</button><button class="option-btn">Prends-en</button><button class="option-btn">En prends</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="en-8" data-step="Pratique — à compléter">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">8</span> Pratique — à compléter</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Remplacez par « en »</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">1. Je mange <u>des légumes</u>. → J'_____ mange.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="en" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">2. Il a <u>deux</u> voitures. → Il _____ a deux.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="en" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">3. Nous parlons <u>de ce film</u>. → Nous _____ parlons.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="en" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">4. Elle n'a pas <u>de temps</u>. → Elle n'_____ a pas.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="en" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">5. Tu veux du café ? → Oui, j'_____ veux bien.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="en" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="accent-bar">
                <span class="ab-label">Accents :</span>
                <button class="accent-key">é</button><button class="accent-key">è</button><button class="accent-key">ê</button>
                <button class="accent-key">à</button><button class="accent-key">ç</button><button class="accent-key">ù</button>
                <button class="accent-key">û</button><button class="accent-key">î</button><button class="accent-key">ô</button>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn fib-check student-only">✓ Vérifier</button>
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </section>

      <!-- ================= 4.5 PRONOMS TONIQUES ================= -->
      <section data-topic="pronoms" data-topic-name="Les Pronoms Personnels" data-sub="Les Pronoms Toniques">

        <section data-slide-id="ton-1" data-step="Description">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">1</span> Description</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Les Pronoms Toniques — the stressed pronouns</h2>
            <p class="editable-field">These stand <strong>alone</strong> or after a <strong>preposition</strong>. They are the only pronouns that can be separated from the verb.</p>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Les huit formes</h3>
                <table class="subj-table">
                  <tr><th>Sujet</th><th>Tonique</th><th>Sujet</th><th>Tonique</th></tr>
                  <tr><td>je</td><td class="key-form">moi</td><td>nous</td><td class="key-form">nous</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>tu</td><td class="key-form">toi</td><td>vous</td><td class="key-form">vous</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>il</td><td class="key-form">lui</td><td>ils</td><td class="key-form">eux</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>elle</td><td class="key-form">elle</td><td>elles</td><td class="key-form">elles</td></tr>
                </table>
                <p class="gloss">Only <em>moi, toi, lui, eux</em> are genuinely new.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Quand les utiliser</h3>
                <p>① <strong>Après une préposition</strong> — avec <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">moi</span>, chez <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">lui</span>, pour <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">eux</span></p>
                <p>② <strong>Insistance</strong> — <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">Moi</span>, je pense que…</p>
                <p>③ <strong>Après c'est</strong> — C'est <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">moi</span>.</p>
                <p>④ <strong>Comparaison</strong> — plus grand que <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">lui</span></p>
                <p>⑤ <strong>Seul</strong> — Qui vient ? <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">Moi</span> !</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="ton-2" data-step="Formation">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">2</span> Formation</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">La formule — après une préposition</h2>
            <div class="formula-pipeline">
              <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Préposition</span><span class="f-value">avec / chez / pour</span></div>
              <div class="f-op">+</div>
              <div class="f-box" style="border-color:var(--purple);"><span class="f-label">Pronom tonique</span><span class="f-value" style="color:var(--purple);">moi / toi / lui / eux</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <table class="subj-table">
                <tr><th>Structure</th><th>Exemple</th><th>Anglais</th></tr>
                <tr><td>avec + tonique</td><td>Tu viens avec <span class="key-form">moi</span> ?</td><td class="gloss">Are you coming with me?</td></tr>
                <tr><td>chez + tonique</td><td>On va chez <span class="key-form">eux</span>.</td><td class="gloss">We're going to their place.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>pour + tonique</td><td>C'est pour <span class="key-form">toi</span>.</td><td class="gloss">It's for you.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>sans + tonique</td><td>Je pars sans <span class="key-form">lui</span>.</td><td class="gloss">I'm leaving without him.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>à + tonique</td><td>Je pense à <span class="key-form">elle</span>.</td><td class="gloss">I'm thinking about her.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>que + tonique</td><td>Il est plus âgé que <span class="key-form">moi</span>.</td><td class="gloss">He is older than me.</td></tr>
              </table>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="ton-3" data-step="Exceptions">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">3</span> Exceptions</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Les emplois particuliers</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Avec « -même(s) » — insistance</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Je l'ai fait <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">moi-même</span>.</p>
                <p class="gloss">I did it myself.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Ils l'ont construit <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">eux-mêmes</span>.</p>
                <p class="gloss">They built it themselves. — note the -s</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Sujets multiples</h3>
                <p>When two subjects are joined, use toniques then sum them up:</p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-pronoun">Toi</span> et <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">moi</span>, <span class="highlight hl-subject">nous</span> sommes amis.</p>
                <p class="gloss">You and I, we are friends.</p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-pronoun">Lui</span> et <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">elle</span> travaillent ensemble.</p>
                <p class="gloss">He and she work together.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field"><strong>À l'impératif affirmatif</strong> the object pronouns <em>me</em> and <em>te</em> become the toniques
              <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">moi</span> and <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">toi</span>:
              <em>Donne-<span class="highlight hl-pronoun">moi</span> !</em> · <em>Lève-<span class="highlight hl-pronoun">toi</span> !</em>
              — but in the negative they revert: <em>Ne <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">me</span> donne pas.</em></p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="ton-4" data-step="Pièges">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">4</span> Pièges</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">⚠️ Trap Alert — tonique or object pronoun?</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box red content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--crimson);">✗ Wrong</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Tu viens avec <span class="highlight hl-neg">je</span> ?</p>
                <p class="example-text">C'est <span class="highlight hl-neg">je</span>.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Il est plus grand que <span class="highlight hl-neg">je</span>.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Je pense à <span class="highlight hl-neg">ils</span>.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box green content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--green);">✓ Right</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Tu viens avec <span class="highlight hl-verb">moi</span> ? <span class="gloss">after a preposition</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">C'est <span class="highlight hl-verb">moi</span>. <span class="gloss">after c'est</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Il est plus grand que <span class="highlight hl-verb">moi</span>. <span class="gloss">after que</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Je pense à <span class="highlight hl-verb">eux</span>. <span class="gloss">penser à + person</span></p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">🔑 <strong>Rule of thumb:</strong> if the pronoun is <strong>touching the verb</strong>, it's an object pronoun (le, la, lui, leur).
              If it stands <strong>after a preposition or alone</strong>, it's a tonique (moi, toi, lui, eux).</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="ton-5" data-step="Exemples">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">5</span> Exemples travaillés</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Worked examples</h2>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-pronoun">Moi</span>, je préfère le thé ; <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">toi</span>, tu préfères le café.</p>
              <p class="gloss">I prefer tea; you prefer coffee. — contrast and emphasis</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Ce cadeau est pour <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">elle</span>, pas pour <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">lui</span>.</p>
              <p class="gloss">This present is for her, not for him.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Nous allons chez <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">eux</span> ce week-end.</p>
              <p class="gloss">We're going to their place this weekend.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">— Qui a cassé le vase ? — Pas <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">moi</span> !</p>
              <p class="gloss">— Who broke the vase? — Not me!</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="ton-6" data-step="En contexte">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">6</span> En contexte</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">In context — expressing opinions</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">L.6 — Chacun ses goûts</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Moi, j'adore le cinéma ; lui, il préfère le sport.</p>
                <p class="gloss">Me, I love cinema; him, he prefers sport.</p>
                <h3>L.1 — La famille</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Chez nous, on dîne à huit heures.</p>
                <p class="gloss">At our place, we have dinner at eight.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">L.5 — Les médias</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Selon moi, les réseaux sociaux ont changé nos vies.</p>
                <p class="gloss">In my opinion, social networks have changed our lives.</p>
                <h3 style="color:var(--gold);">L.2 — Après le bac</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Pour eux, le choix de la filière est difficile.</p>
                <p class="gloss">For them, choosing a stream is difficult.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">💡 <strong>Essay opener:</strong> <em>Selon moi…</em> / <em>Quant à moi…</em> / <em>Moi, je pense que…</em>
              <span class="gloss">In my view… / As for me… / I think that…</span> Three ready-made ways to state an opinion, all built on a tonique.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="ton-7" data-step="Pratique QCM">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">7</span> Pratique — QCM</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Choose the correct pronoun</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="moi">
                <p class="q-text">1. Tu viens avec _____ ?</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">je</button><button class="option-btn">moi</button><button class="option-btn">me</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="eux">
                <p class="q-text">2. Nous dînons chez _____ ce soir. <span class="gloss">(ils)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">ils</button><button class="option-btn">leur</button><button class="option-btn">eux</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="lui">
                <p class="q-text">3. Elle est plus jeune que _____. <span class="gloss">(il)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">il</button><button class="option-btn">lui</button><button class="option-btn">le</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="toi">
                <p class="q-text">4. C'est _____ qui as gagné !</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">tu</button><button class="option-btn">toi</button><button class="option-btn">te</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="elles">
                <p class="q-text">5. Je pense souvent à _____. <span class="gloss">(mes sœurs)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">leur</button><button class="option-btn">elles</button><button class="option-btn">y</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="ton-8" data-step="Pratique — à compléter">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">8</span> Pratique — à compléter</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Complétez avec un pronom tonique</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">1. Ce livre est à _____. <span class="gloss">(je)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="moi" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">2. Ils partent sans _____. <span class="gloss">(nous)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="nous" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">3. _____, elle adore voyager. <span class="gloss">(elle — insistance)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="elle" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">4. Je l'ai réparé _____-même. <span class="gloss">(je)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="moi" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">5. Nous parlons souvent d'_____. <span class="gloss">(ils)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="eux" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="accent-bar">
                <span class="ab-label">Accents :</span>
                <button class="accent-key">é</button><button class="accent-key">è</button><button class="accent-key">ê</button>
                <button class="accent-key">à</button><button class="accent-key">ç</button><button class="accent-key">ù</button>
                <button class="accent-key">û</button><button class="accent-key">î</button><button class="accent-key">ô</button>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn fib-check student-only">✓ Vérifier</button>
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </section>

      <!-- ================= 4.6 L'ORDRE DES PRONOMS ================= -->
      <section data-topic="pronoms" data-topic-name="Les Pronoms Personnels" data-sub="L'Ordre des Pronoms">

        <section data-slide-id="ordre-1" data-step="Description">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">1</span> Description</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">L'Ordre — when two pronouns meet</h2>
            <p class="editable-field">French allows <strong>two object pronouns</strong> before the verb — but only in a fixed order. Getting the order right is the whole skill.</p>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <p class="example-text">Il donne <span class="highlight hl-verb">le livre</span> <span class="highlight hl-aux">à Marie</span>.</p>
              <p class="gloss">He gives the book to Marie.</p>
              <p class="example-text">→ Il <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">le</span> <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">lui</span> donne.</p>
              <p class="gloss">He gives it to her. — COD then COI</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">In English you can say "he gives her it" or "he gives it to her". French has <strong>one</strong> possible order, and it depends on which pronouns are involved.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="ordre-2" data-step="Formation">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">2</span> Formation</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">La formule — l'ordre officiel</h2>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <div class="formula-pipeline" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr 1fr 1fr 1fr;">
                <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">1</span><span class="f-value" style="font-size:1rem;">me<br>te<br>se<br>nous<br>vous</span></div>
                <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">2</span><span class="f-value" style="font-size:1rem;">le<br>la<br>les</span></div>
                <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">3</span><span class="f-value" style="font-size:1rem;">lui<br>leur</span></div>
                <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">4</span><span class="f-value" style="font-size:1rem;">y</span></div>
                <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">5</span><span class="f-value" style="font-size:1rem;">en</span></div>
              </div>
              <p class="editable-field gloss" style="text-align:center; margin-top:8px;">Read left to right. Two pronouns always appear in this column order, then the verb.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Exemples</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Il <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">me</span> <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">le</span> donne. <span class="gloss">1 + 2 — He gives it to me.</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Je <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">le</span> <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">lui</span> donne. <span class="gloss">2 + 3 — I give it to him.</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Il y <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">en</span> a. <span class="gloss">4 + 5 — There is some.</span></p>
              </div>
              <div class="box green content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--green);">Mémo</h3>
                <p><strong>me te se nous vous</strong> → <strong>le la les</strong> → <strong>lui leur</strong> → <strong>y</strong> → <strong>en</strong></p>
                <p class="gloss">Notice: <em>le/la/les</em> come <strong>before</strong> <em>lui/leur</em>, but <strong>after</strong> <em>me/te/nous/vous</em>. That switch is the trap.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="ordre-3" data-step="Exceptions">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">3</span> Exceptions</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">L'impératif affirmatif inverse tout</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Affirmatif — COD avant COI, après le verbe</h3>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-verb">Donne</span>-<span class="highlight hl-pronoun">le</span>-<span class="highlight hl-pronoun">moi</span> !</p>
                <p class="gloss">Give it to me! — verb, then COD, then COI, joined by hyphens</p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-verb">Montre</span>-<span class="highlight hl-pronoun">les</span>-<span class="highlight hl-pronoun">lui</span> !</p>
                <p class="gloss">Show them to him!</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Négatif — retour à l'ordre normal</h3>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-neg">Ne</span> <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">me</span> <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">le</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">donne</span> <span class="highlight hl-neg">pas</span> !</p>
                <p class="gloss">Don't give it to me!</p>
                <p class="gloss">Before the verb, in the standard column order, with no hyphens.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field"><strong>Aux temps composés</strong> both pronouns go before the <strong>auxiliary</strong>:
              <em>Il <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">me</span> <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">l'</span>a donné.</em> <span class="gloss">He gave it to me.</span>
              Never between the auxiliary and the participle.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="ordre-4" data-step="Pièges">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">4</span> Pièges</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">⚠️ Trap Alert — the order switches</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box red content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--crimson);">✗ Wrong</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Je <span class="highlight hl-neg">lui le</span> donne.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Il <span class="highlight hl-neg">le me</span> donne.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Donne-<span class="highlight hl-neg">moi-le</span> !</p>
                <p class="example-text">Il m'a <span class="highlight hl-neg">le</span> donné.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box green content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--green);">✓ Right</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Je <span class="highlight hl-verb">le lui</span> donne. <span class="gloss">le (2) before lui (3)</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Il <span class="highlight hl-verb">me le</span> donne. <span class="gloss">me (1) before le (2)</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Donne-<span class="highlight hl-verb">le-moi</span> ! <span class="gloss">imperative reverses it</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Il <span class="highlight hl-verb">me l'</span>a donné. <span class="gloss">both before the auxiliary</span></p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">🔑 <strong>The one thing to remember:</strong> <em>me/te/nous/vous</em> come <strong>first</strong>,
              but <em>lui/leur</em> come <strong>last</strong> — with <em>le/la/les</em> always in the middle.
              Say <strong>"me – le – lui"</strong> aloud until it sticks.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="ordre-5" data-step="Exemples">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">5</span> Exemples travaillés</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Worked examples</h2>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <p class="example-text">Il donne le livre à Paul. → Il <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">le</span> <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">lui</span> donne.</p>
              <p class="gloss">He gives it to him.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Tu me prêtes ta voiture ? → Tu <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">me</span> <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">la</span> prêtes ?</p>
              <p class="gloss">Will you lend it to me?</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Elle a envoyé les photos à ses amis. → Elle <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">les</span> <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">leur</span> a envoyées.</p>
              <p class="gloss">She sent them to them. — agreement with the preceding COD</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Des gâteaux ? Il y <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">en</span> a encore. Prends-<span class="highlight hl-pronoun">en</span> !</p>
              <p class="gloss">Cakes? There are some left. Take some!</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="ordre-6" data-step="En contexte">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">6</span> En contexte</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">In context — natural conversation</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Dialogue quotidien</h3>
                <p class="example-text">— Tu as rendu le livre à Léa ?<br>— Oui, je le lui ai rendu hier.</p>
                <p class="gloss">— Did you return the book to Léa? — Yes, I returned it to her yesterday.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">L.8 — Faire des achats</h3>
                <p class="example-text">— Vous me le montrez, s'il vous plaît ?<br>— Bien sûr, je vous le montre.</p>
                <p class="gloss">— Will you show it to me, please? — Of course, I'll show it to you.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">💡 <strong>Why it matters:</strong> double pronouns are what separate a good answer from a very good one.
              Even one correct <em>je le lui ai donné</em> in a letter shows the examiner you control the pronoun system.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="ordre-7" data-step="Pratique QCM">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">7</span> Pratique — QCM</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Put the pronouns in the right order</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="Je le lui donne">
                <p class="q-text">1. Je donne le stylo à Marc. → _____</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">Je lui le donne</button><button class="option-btn">Je le lui donne</button><button class="option-btn">Je le donne lui</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="Il me les montre">
                <p class="q-text">2. Il montre les photos à moi. → _____</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">Il les me montre</button><button class="option-btn">Il me les montre</button><button class="option-btn">Il me montre les</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="Donne-le-moi">
                <p class="q-text">3. Donne-moi ce livre ! → _____ !</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">Donne-moi-le</button><button class="option-btn">Donne-le-moi</button><button class="option-btn">Me le donne</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="Elle la leur a offerte">
                <p class="q-text">4. Elle a offert la tarte à ses voisins. → _____</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">Elle leur l'a offerte</button><button class="option-btn">Elle la leur a offerte</button><button class="option-btn">Elle a la leur offerte</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="Il y en a">
                <p class="q-text">5. Il reste des places. → _____ encore.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">Il en y a</button><button class="option-btn">Il y en a</button><button class="option-btn">Il y a en</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="ordre-8" data-step="Pratique — à compléter">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">8</span> Pratique — à compléter</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Remplacez les deux compléments</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">1. Je prête <u>mon vélo</u> <u>à mon frère</u>. → Je _____ prête.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="le lui" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">2. Il explique <u>la règle</u> <u>aux élèves</u>. → Il _____ explique.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="la leur" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">3. Tu me donnes <u>ton adresse</u> ? → Tu _____ donnes ?</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="me la" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">4. Envoie <u>la lettre</u> <u>à ta tante</u> ! → Envoie-_____ !</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="la-lui" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">5. Elle nous a raconté <u>l'histoire</u>. → Elle _____ a racontée.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="nous l'" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="accent-bar">
                <span class="ab-label">Accents :</span>
                <button class="accent-key">é</button><button class="accent-key">è</button><button class="accent-key">ê</button>
                <button class="accent-key">à</button><button class="accent-key">ç</button><button class="accent-key">ù</button>
                <button class="accent-key">û</button><button class="accent-key">î</button><button class="accent-key">ô</button>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn fib-check student-only">✓ Vérifier</button>
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </section>

      <!-- ================= TOPIC 4 CLOSER ================= -->
      <section data-topic="pronoms" data-topic-name="Les Pronoms Personnels" data-sub="Synthèse &amp; Examen">

        <section data-slide-id="pron-fin-1" data-step="Tableau de référence">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">📊 Tableau de référence — tous les pronoms</h2>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <table class="subj-table">
                <tr><th>Sujet</th><th>COD</th><th>COI</th><th>Tonique</th><th>Réfléchi</th></tr>
                <tr><td>je</td><td>me</td><td>me</td><td class="key-form">moi</td><td>me</td></tr>
                <tr><td>tu</td><td>te</td><td>te</td><td class="key-form">toi</td><td>te</td></tr>
                <tr><td>il</td><td class="key-form">le</td><td class="key-form">lui</td><td class="key-form">lui</td><td>se</td></tr>
                <tr><td>elle</td><td class="key-form">la</td><td class="key-form">lui</td><td class="key-form">elle</td><td>se</td></tr>
                <tr><td>nous</td><td>nous</td><td>nous</td><td>nous</td><td>nous</td></tr>
                <tr><td>vous</td><td>vous</td><td>vous</td><td>vous</td><td>vous</td></tr>
                <tr><td>ils</td><td class="key-form">les</td><td class="key-form">leur</td><td class="key-form">eux</td><td>se</td></tr>
                <tr><td>elles</td><td class="key-form">les</td><td class="key-form">leur</td><td class="key-form">elles</td><td>se</td></tr>
              </table>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field"><strong>Y</strong> = à + chose / lieu &nbsp;·&nbsp; <strong>EN</strong> = de + chose / quantité<br>
              <strong>Ordre :</strong> me te se nous vous → le la les → lui leur → y → en</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="pron-fin-2" data-step="Examen CBSE">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">📝 Examen blanc — Les Pronoms</h2>
            <p class="editable-field gloss">Remplacez les mots soulignés par le pronom qui convient.</p>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text"><span class="q-tag">CBSE 2019</span>1. Ce sont mes tantes qui rient. → Ce sont _____ qui rient. <span class="gloss">(tonique)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="elles" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">2. Je téléphone <u>à mes amis</u>. → Je _____ téléphone.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="leur" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">3. Nous allons <u>au marché</u>. → Nous _____ allons.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="y" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">4. Elle achète <u>du pain</u>. → Elle _____ achète.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="en" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">5. J'ai vu <u>tes cousines</u>. → Je _____ ai vues.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="les" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">6. Il donne <u>le cadeau</u> <u>à sa mère</u>. → Il _____ donne.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="le lui" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="accent-bar">
                <span class="ab-label">Accents :</span>
                <button class="accent-key">é</button><button class="accent-key">è</button><button class="accent-key">ê</button>
                <button class="accent-key">à</button><button class="accent-key">ç</button><button class="accent-key">ù</button>
                <button class="accent-key">û</button><button class="accent-key">î</button><button class="accent-key">ô</button>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn fib-check student-only">✓ Vérifier</button>
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 6</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="pron-fin-3" data-step="Check-list">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">✅ Check-list — Les Pronoms</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <p>☐ Is there a preposition? No <em>à</em> → <strong>COD</strong>. With <em>à</em> + person → <strong>COI</strong>.</p>
                <p>☐ Is it a <strong>place</strong> or <em>à</em> + thing? → <strong>y</strong></p>
                <p>☐ Is it <em>de</em> + thing, or a <strong>quantity</strong>? → <strong>en</strong> (and repeat the number!)</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <p>☐ Is the pronoun <strong>before the verb</strong> (or the auxiliary)?</p>
                <p>☐ COD before the verb with <em>avoir</em> → did the participle <strong>agree</strong>?</p>
                <p>☐ Two pronouns → is the order <strong>me · le · lui · y · en</strong>?</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">🎯 <strong>Exam note:</strong> personal pronouns carry 5 marks and are tested every single year
              (the syllabus states they continue to be tested from Class 9). The commonest lost mark is the <strong>participle agreement</strong> after a COD.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </section>
      <!-- ==================================================================
           TOPIC 5 — LES PRONOMS RELATIFS
           =================================================================== -->
      <section data-topic="relatifs" data-topic-name="Les Pronoms Relatifs" data-sub="QUI">

        <section data-slide-id="qui-1" data-step="Description">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">1</span> Description</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">QUI — the subject of the relative clause</h2>
            <p class="editable-field">A relative pronoun <strong>joins two sentences</strong> that share a noun, so you don't repeat it. <em>Qui</em> is used when that shared noun is the <strong>subject</strong> of the second verb.</p>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <p class="example-text">Je connais un garçon. <span class="highlight hl-subject">Ce garçon</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">parle</span> cinq langues.</p>
              <p class="gloss">I know a boy. This boy speaks five languages.</p>
              <p class="example-text">→ Je connais un garçon <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">qui</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">parle</span> cinq langues.</p>
              <p class="gloss">I know a boy who speaks five languages.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">🔑 <strong>The test:</strong> after the relative pronoun comes a <strong>verb</strong> → use <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">qui</span>.<br>
              <em>… qui <span class="highlight hl-verb">parle</span></em> · <em>… qui <span class="highlight hl-verb">est</span></em> · <em>… qui <span class="highlight hl-verb">habite</span></em></p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="qui-2" data-step="Formation">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">2</span> Formation</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">La formule</h2>
            <div class="formula-pipeline">
              <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Antécédent</span><span class="f-value">le garçon</span></div>
              <div class="f-op">+</div>
              <div class="f-box" style="border-color:var(--purple);"><span class="f-label">QUI</span><span class="f-value" style="color:var(--purple);">qui</span></div>
              <div class="f-op">+</div>
              <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Verbe</span><span class="f-value">parle</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Personnes ET choses</h3>
                <p class="example-text">La femme <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">qui</span> chante est ma tante.</p>
                <p class="gloss">The woman who is singing is my aunt.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Le train <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">qui</span> arrive vient de Lyon.</p>
                <p class="gloss">The train which is arriving comes from Lyon.</p>
                <p class="gloss">Unlike English (who / which), French uses <strong>qui</strong> for both.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Le verbe s'accorde avec l'antécédent</h3>
                <p class="example-text">C'est <span class="highlight hl-subject">moi</span> qui <span class="highlight hl-verb">suis</span> responsable.</p>
                <p class="gloss">It is I who am responsible.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Ce sont <span class="highlight hl-subject">mes tantes</span> qui <span class="highlight hl-verb">rient</span>.</p>
                <p class="gloss">It's my aunts who are laughing. — plural verb</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="qui-3" data-step="Exceptions">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">3</span> Exceptions</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Les exceptions — QUI ne s'élide jamais</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box red content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--crimson);">QUI garde son -i</h3>
                <p class="example-text">L'homme <span class="highlight hl-verb">qui a</span> téléphoné…</p>
                <p class="gloss">✗ never <em>qu'a</em></p>
                <p class="example-text">La fille <span class="highlight hl-verb">qui est</span> venue…</p>
                <p class="gloss">✗ never <em>qu'est</em></p>
                <p class="gloss">Compare: <em>que</em> DOES elide → <em>qu'il</em>, <em>qu'elle</em>.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">QUI après une préposition = personne</h3>
                <p>After a preposition, <em>qui</em> refers only to <strong>people</strong>:</p>
                <p class="example-text">La personne <span class="highlight hl-aux">avec</span> <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">qui</span> je parle…</p>
                <p class="gloss">The person with whom I'm speaking…</p>
                <p class="example-text">L'ami <span class="highlight hl-aux">pour</span> <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">qui</span> j'ai acheté ce cadeau…</p>
                <p class="gloss">The friend for whom I bought this present…</p>
                <p class="gloss">For things, use <em>lequel</em> — see sub-topic 5.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field"><strong>Ce qui</strong> — when there is no specific noun before it:
                <em><span class="highlight hl-pronoun">Ce qui</span> m'intéresse, c'est la musique.</em>
                <span class="gloss">What interests me is music.</span></p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="qui-4" data-step="Pièges">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">4</span> Pièges</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">⚠️ Trap Alert — QUI vs QUE</h2>
            <p class="editable-field">This is the single most tested distinction of the topic. Look at <strong>what follows</strong> the pronoun.</p>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">QUI + VERBE</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Le livre <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">qui</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">est</span> sur la table…</p>
                <p class="gloss">The book which is on the table… — <em>livre</em> does the action</p>
                <p class="example-text">L'homme <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">qui</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">travaille</span> ici…</p>
                <p class="gloss">The man who works here…</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">QUE + SUJET + VERBE</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Le livre <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">que</span> <span class="highlight hl-subject">je</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">lis</span>…</p>
                <p class="gloss">The book which I am reading… — <em>je</em> does the action</p>
                <p class="example-text">L'homme <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">que</span> <span class="highlight hl-subject">tu</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">connais</span>…</p>
                <p class="gloss">The man whom you know…</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box red content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">🔑 <strong>Two-second test:</strong> cover the antecedent and read on.
              If a <strong>verb</strong> comes straight after → <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">qui</span>.
              If a <strong>new subject</strong> comes → <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">que</span>.<br>
              ✗ <em>Le film qui j'ai vu</em> → ✓ <em>Le film <span class="highlight hl-verb">que</span> j'ai vu</em></p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="qui-5" data-step="Exemples">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">5</span> Exemples travaillés</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Worked examples</h2>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <p class="example-text">J'ai un ami <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">qui</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">habite</span> à Paris.</p>
              <p class="gloss">I have a friend who lives in Paris.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Le train <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">qui</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">part</span> à midi est complet.</p>
              <p class="gloss">The train which leaves at noon is full.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Ce sont mes cousins <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">qui</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">ont</span> gagné le match.</p>
              <p class="gloss">It's my cousins who won the match. — plural verb</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">L'élève <span class="highlight hl-aux">avec</span> <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">qui</span> je travaille est très sérieux.</p>
              <p class="gloss">The pupil with whom I work is very serious.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="qui-6" data-step="En contexte">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">6</span> En contexte</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">In context — describing people and things</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">L.1 — La famille</h3>
                <p class="example-text">J'ai une sœur qui étudie la médecine.</p>
                <p class="gloss">I have a sister who is studying medicine.</p>
                <h3>L.4 — Le plaisir de lire</h3>
                <p class="example-text">C'est un roman qui raconte la vie d'un jeune homme.</p>
                <p class="gloss">It's a novel which tells the life of a young man.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">L.3 — Chercher du travail</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Je cherche un emploi qui me permette de voyager.</p>
                <p class="gloss">I'm looking for a job that allows me to travel.</p>
                <h3 style="color:var(--gold);">L.8 — L'environnement</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Les gens qui recyclent aident la planète.</p>
                <p class="gloss">People who recycle help the planet.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">💡 <strong>Writing tip:</strong> relative clauses turn two short sentences into one longer, better sentence.
              Examiners reward that. Instead of <em>J'ai un ami. Il habite à Paris.</em> write <em>J'ai un ami qui habite à Paris.</em></p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="qui-7" data-step="Pratique QCM">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">7</span> Pratique — QCM</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">QUI or QUE?</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="qui">
                <p class="q-text">1. La fille _____ chante est ma cousine.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">qui</button><button class="option-btn">que</button><button class="option-btn">dont</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="que">
                <p class="q-text">2. Le livre _____ je lis est passionnant.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">qui</button><button class="option-btn">que</button><button class="option-btn">où</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="qui">
                <p class="q-text">3. J'ai un chien _____ aboie beaucoup.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">que</button><button class="option-btn">qui</button><button class="option-btn">dont</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="qui sont">
                <p class="q-text">4. Ce sont mes amis _____ venus hier.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">qui est</button><button class="option-btn">qui sont</button><button class="option-btn">que sont</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="avec qui">
                <p class="q-text">5. La personne _____ je parle est mon professeur.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">avec qui</button><button class="option-btn">avec que</button><button class="option-btn">qui avec</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="qui-8" data-step="Pratique — à compléter">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">8</span> Pratique — à compléter</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Reliez les deux phrases avec « qui »</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">1. J'ai un frère. Il travaille à Paris. → J'ai un frère _____ travaille à Paris.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="qui" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">2. Voici le bus. Il va à la gare. → Voici le bus _____ va à la gare.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="qui" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">3. C'est une ville. Elle est très ancienne. → C'est une ville _____ est très ancienne.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="qui" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">4. Ce sont les élèves. Ils ont réussi. → Ce sont les élèves _____ ont réussi.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="qui" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">5. Le film _____ passe au cinéma est français. <span class="gloss">(qui / que ?)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="qui" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="accent-bar">
                <span class="ab-label">Accents :</span>
                <button class="accent-key">é</button><button class="accent-key">è</button><button class="accent-key">ê</button>
                <button class="accent-key">à</button><button class="accent-key">ç</button><button class="accent-key">ù</button>
                <button class="accent-key">û</button><button class="accent-key">î</button><button class="accent-key">ô</button>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn fib-check student-only">✓ Vérifier</button>
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </section>

      <!-- ================= 5.2 QUE ================= -->
      <section data-topic="relatifs" data-topic-name="Les Pronoms Relatifs" data-sub="QUE">

        <section data-slide-id="que-1" data-step="Description">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">1</span> Description</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">QUE — the direct object of the relative clause</h2>
            <p class="editable-field"><em>Que</em> is used when the shared noun is the <strong>object</strong> of the second verb — somebody else does the action <em>to</em> it.</p>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <p class="example-text">Je lis un livre. <span class="highlight hl-subject">Mon frère</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">a acheté</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">ce livre</span>.</p>
              <p class="gloss">I'm reading a book. My brother bought this book.</p>
              <p class="example-text">→ Je lis un livre <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">que</span> <span class="highlight hl-subject">mon frère</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">a acheté</span>.</p>
              <p class="gloss">I'm reading a book which my brother bought.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">🔑 <strong>The test:</strong> after <em>que</em> comes a <strong>new subject</strong> (a noun or pronoun), then the verb.<br>
              <em>… que <span class="highlight hl-subject">je</span> lis</em> · <em>… que <span class="highlight hl-subject">tu</span> connais</em> · <em>… que <span class="highlight hl-subject">mes parents</span> ont vu</em></p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="que-2" data-step="Formation">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">2</span> Formation</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">La formule</h2>
            <div class="formula-pipeline">
              <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Antécédent</span><span class="f-value">le livre</span></div>
              <div class="f-op">+</div>
              <div class="f-box" style="border-color:var(--purple);"><span class="f-label">QUE</span><span class="f-value" style="color:var(--purple);">que / qu'</span></div>
              <div class="f-op">+</div>
              <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Sujet + verbe</span><span class="f-value">je lis</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">QUE s'élide en QU'</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Le film <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">qu'</span>il regarde…</p>
                <p class="gloss">The film which he is watching…</p>
                <p class="example-text">La maison <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">qu'</span>elle a achetée…</p>
                <p class="gloss">The house which she bought…</p>
                <p class="gloss">Before a vowel or silent h, always <em>qu'</em>.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Personnes et choses</h3>
                <p class="example-text">L'homme <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">que</span> je connais…</p>
                <p class="gloss">The man whom I know…</p>
                <p class="example-text">Le stylo <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">que</span> tu m'as prêté…</p>
                <p class="gloss">The pen which you lent me…</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="que-3" data-step="Exceptions">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">3</span> Exceptions</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">L'accord du participe passé après QUE</h2>
            <p class="editable-field">Because <em>que</em> is a direct object placed <strong>before</strong> the verb, the participle must agree with the antecedent.</p>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <table class="subj-table">
                <tr><th>Antécédent</th><th>Phrase</th><th>Accord</th></tr>
                <tr><td>masc. sing.</td><td>Le livre que j'ai <span class="key-form">lu</span></td><td class="gloss">no change</td></tr>
                <tr><td>fém. sing.</td><td>La lettre que j'ai <span class="key-form">lue</span></td><td class="gloss">+ e</td></tr>
                <tr><td>masc. plur.</td><td>Les livres que j'ai <span class="key-form">lus</span></td><td class="gloss">+ s</td></tr>
                <tr><td>fém. plur.</td><td>Les lettres que j'ai <span class="key-form">lues</span></td><td class="gloss">+ es</td></tr>
              </table>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field"><strong>Comparez:</strong> after <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">qui</span> there is <strong>no</strong> such agreement, because <em>qui</em> is a subject, not an object:<br>
              <em>La fille <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">qui</span> est <span class="highlight hl-verb">venue</span></em> <span class="gloss">— this -e comes from <em>être</em>, not from <em>qui</em></span><br>
              <em>La fille <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">que</span> j'ai <span class="highlight hl-verb">vue</span></em> <span class="gloss">— this -e comes from the preceding COD</span></p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="que-4" data-step="Pièges">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">4</span> Pièges</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">⚠️ Trap Alert — English drops it, French never does</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box red content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--crimson);">✗ Wrong</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Le film <span class="highlight hl-neg">j'ai vu</span> était bon.</p>
                <p class="gloss">— copying English "the film I saw"</p>
                <p class="example-text">La fille <span class="highlight hl-neg">qui</span> j'ai rencontrée…</p>
                <p class="example-text">Les photos que j'ai <span class="highlight hl-neg">pris</span>…</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box green content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--green);">✓ Right</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Le film <span class="highlight hl-verb">que</span> j'ai vu était bon. <span class="gloss">que is compulsory</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">La fille <span class="highlight hl-verb">que</span> j'ai rencontrée… <span class="gloss">object → que</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Les photos que j'ai <span class="highlight hl-verb">prises</span>… <span class="gloss">fem. plural agreement</span></p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">💡 English lets you say "the book I read" with nothing in between. <strong>French never allows this.</strong>
              If two clauses share a noun, a relative pronoun <em>must</em> appear.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="que-5" data-step="Exemples">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">5</span> Exemples travaillés</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Worked examples</h2>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <p class="example-text">Le gâteau <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">que</span> tu as fait était délicieux.</p>
              <p class="gloss">The cake which you made was delicious.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">La chanson <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">qu'</span>elle a <span class="highlight hl-verb">chantée</span> est très connue.</p>
              <p class="gloss">The song which she sang is very well known. — feminine agreement</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Les amis <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">que</span> nous avons <span class="highlight hl-verb">invités</span> arrivent à huit heures.</p>
              <p class="gloss">The friends whom we invited arrive at eight. — masculine plural</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-pronoun">Ce que</span> je préfère, c'est le chocolat.</p>
              <p class="gloss">What I prefer is chocolate. — no specific antecedent → ce que</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="que-6" data-step="En contexte">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">6</span> En contexte</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">In context — Entre Jeunes themes</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">L.4 — Le plaisir de lire</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Le roman que j'ai lu l'été dernier m'a beaucoup plu.</p>
                <p class="gloss">The novel I read last summer pleased me a lot.</p>
                <h3>L.6 — Chacun ses goûts</h3>
                <p class="example-text">La musique que j'écoute est surtout indienne.</p>
                <p class="gloss">The music I listen to is mainly Indian.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">L.5 — Les médias</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Les émissions que les jeunes regardent ont changé.</p>
                <p class="gloss">The programmes young people watch have changed.</p>
                <h3 style="color:var(--gold);">L.2 — Après le bac</h3>
                <p class="example-text">La filière que j'ai choisie est difficile mais intéressante.</p>
                <p class="gloss">The stream I chose is difficult but interesting.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="que-7" data-step="Pratique QCM">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">7</span> Pratique — QCM</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Choose the correct relative pronoun</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="que">
                <p class="q-text">1. Voici la robe _____ j'ai achetée.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">qui</button><button class="option-btn">que</button><button class="option-btn">où</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="qu'">
                <p class="q-text">2. Le film _____ il a vu était long.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">qui</button><button class="option-btn">qu'</button><button class="option-btn">que il</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="vues">
                <p class="q-text">3. Les photos que j'ai _____ sont belles. <span class="gloss">(voir)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">vu</button><button class="option-btn">vus</button><button class="option-btn">vues</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="Ce que">
                <p class="q-text">4. _____ je veux, c'est réussir.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">Ce qui</button><button class="option-btn">Ce que</button><button class="option-btn">Que</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="que">
                <p class="q-text">5. L'homme _____ tu as rencontré est mon oncle.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">qui</button><button class="option-btn">que</button><button class="option-btn">dont</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="que-8" data-step="Pratique — à compléter">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">8</span> Pratique — à compléter</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Complétez avec « qui » ou « que »</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">1. C'est le professeur _____ enseigne le français.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="qui" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">2. Voici le cadeau _____ je t'ai apporté.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="que" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">3. La maison _____ nous avons visitée est ancienne.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="que" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">4. Les enfants _____ jouent dans le jardin sont mes voisins.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="qui" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">5. Le sac _____ elle porte est très lourd.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="qu'" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="accent-bar">
                <span class="ab-label">Accents :</span>
                <button class="accent-key">é</button><button class="accent-key">è</button><button class="accent-key">ê</button>
                <button class="accent-key">à</button><button class="accent-key">ç</button><button class="accent-key">ù</button>
                <button class="accent-key">û</button><button class="accent-key">î</button><button class="accent-key">ô</button>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn fib-check student-only">✓ Vérifier</button>
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </section>

      <!-- ================= 5.3 OÙ ================= -->
      <section data-topic="relatifs" data-topic-name="Les Pronoms Relatifs" data-sub="OÙ">

        <section data-slide-id="ou-1" data-step="Description">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">1</span> Description</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">OÙ — place and time</h2>
            <p class="editable-field"><em>Où</em> replaces an expression of <strong>place</strong> or <strong>time</strong>. English uses "where" for place but "when" for time — French uses <em>où</em> for both.</p>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">① Le lieu</h3>
                <p class="example-text">La ville <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">où</span> j'habite est grande.</p>
                <p class="gloss">The city where I live is big.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Le pays <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">où</span> je suis né…</p>
                <p class="gloss">The country where I was born…</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">② Le temps</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Le jour <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">où</span> nous sommes partis…</p>
                <p class="gloss">The day (when) we left…</p>
                <p class="example-text">L'année <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">où</span> il est né…</p>
                <p class="gloss">The year (when) he was born…</p>
                <p class="gloss">⚠️ Never <em>quand</em> as a relative pronoun.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="ou-2" data-step="Formation">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">2</span> Formation</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">La formule</h2>
            <div class="formula-pipeline">
              <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Antécédent (lieu/temps)</span><span class="f-value">la ville</span></div>
              <div class="f-op">+</div>
              <div class="f-box" style="border-color:var(--purple);"><span class="f-label">OÙ</span><span class="f-value" style="color:var(--purple);">où</span></div>
              <div class="f-op">+</div>
              <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Sujet + verbe</span><span class="f-value">j'habite</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <p class="editable-field">Two sentences become one:</p>
              <p class="example-text">C'est la maison. J'ai grandi <span class="highlight hl-aux">dans cette maison</span>.</p>
              <p class="example-text">→ C'est la maison <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">où</span> j'ai grandi.</p>
              <p class="gloss">This is the house where I grew up.</p>
              <p class="example-text">Je me souviens du jour. Nous nous sommes rencontrés <span class="highlight hl-aux">ce jour-là</span>.</p>
              <p class="example-text">→ Je me souviens du jour <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">où</span> nous nous sommes rencontrés.</p>
              <p class="gloss">I remember the day we met.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="ou-3" data-step="Exceptions">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">3</span> Exceptions</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Les exceptions — d'où et là où</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">D'OÙ — origine</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Le village <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">d'où</span> je viens est petit.</p>
                <p class="gloss">The village I come from is small.</p>
                <p class="example-text">La fenêtre <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">d'où</span> on voit la mer…</p>
                <p class="gloss">The window from which one sees the sea…</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">LÀ OÙ — sans antécédent précis</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Je vais <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">là où</span> tu veux.</p>
                <p class="gloss">I'll go wherever you want.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Reste <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">là où</span> tu es.</p>
                <p class="gloss">Stay where you are.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field"><strong>Attention à l'accent:</strong>
                <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">où</span> (with the accent) = where/when ·
                <span class="highlight hl-neg">ou</span> (no accent) = or.<br>
                <em>La ville <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">où</span> j'habite</em> <span class="gloss">the city where I live</span> ·
                <em>le thé <span class="highlight hl-neg">ou</span> le café</em> <span class="gloss">tea or coffee</span><br>
                Missing the accent changes the word — and costs the mark.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="ou-4" data-step="Pièges">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">4</span> Pièges</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">⚠️ Trap Alert — never use QUAND as a relative</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box red content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--crimson);">✗ Wrong</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Le jour <span class="highlight hl-neg">quand</span> je suis arrivé…</p>
                <p class="example-text">Le moment <span class="highlight hl-neg">que</span> je l'ai vu…</p>
                <p class="example-text">La ville <span class="highlight hl-neg">que</span> j'habite…</p>
                <p class="example-text">La maison <span class="highlight hl-neg">ou</span> je vis… <span class="gloss">missing accent</span></p>
              </div>
              <div class="box green content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--green);">✓ Right</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Le jour <span class="highlight hl-verb">où</span> je suis arrivé…</p>
                <p class="example-text">Le moment <span class="highlight hl-verb">où</span> je l'ai vu…</p>
                <p class="example-text">La ville <span class="highlight hl-verb">où</span> j'habite… <span class="gloss">habiter + place</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">La maison <span class="highlight hl-verb">où</span> je vis…</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">🔑 <strong>Careful:</strong> not every place noun takes <em>où</em>. If the verb takes a direct object, use <em>que</em>:<br>
              <em>La ville <span class="highlight hl-verb">que</span> j'ai visitée</em> <span class="gloss">visiter quelque chose — direct object</span><br>
              <em>La ville <span class="highlight hl-verb">où</span> j'habite</em> <span class="gloss">habiter dans — place</span></p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="ou-5" data-step="Exemples">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">5</span> Exemples travaillés</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Worked examples</h2>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <p class="example-text">Voici l'école <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">où</span> j'ai étudié pendant dix ans.</p>
              <p class="gloss">This is the school where I studied for ten years.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Je n'oublierai jamais le jour <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">où</span> j'ai reçu mes résultats.</p>
              <p class="gloss">I'll never forget the day I received my results.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Le pays <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">d'où</span> vient ma famille est l'Inde.</p>
              <p class="gloss">The country my family comes from is India.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">C'était l'époque <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">où</span> il n'y avait pas d'Internet.</p>
              <p class="gloss">It was the time when there was no Internet.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="ou-6" data-step="En contexte">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">6</span> En contexte</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">In context — describing places and memories</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">L.5 — Les voyages</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Goa est la région où nous passons nos vacances.</p>
                <p class="gloss">Goa is the region where we spend our holidays.</p>
                <h3>L.2 — Après le bac</h3>
                <p class="example-text">C'est l'année où je dois choisir ma filière.</p>
                <p class="gloss">This is the year when I must choose my stream.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">L.8 — L'environnement</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Nous vivons à une époque où la pollution augmente.</p>
                <p class="gloss">We live in a time when pollution is increasing.</p>
                <h3 style="color:var(--gold);">L.1 — La famille</h3>
                <p class="example-text">La maison où mes grands-parents habitent est très ancienne.</p>
                <p class="gloss">The house where my grandparents live is very old.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="ou-7" data-step="Pratique QCM">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">7</span> Pratique — QCM</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Choose the correct relative pronoun</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="où">
                <p class="q-text">1. C'est le café _____ nous nous retrouvons.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">que</button><button class="option-btn">où</button><button class="option-btn">qui</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="où">
                <p class="q-text">2. Je me souviens du jour _____ tu es arrivé.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">quand</button><button class="option-btn">où</button><button class="option-btn">que</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="que">
                <p class="q-text">3. La ville _____ nous avons visitée est magnifique.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">où</button><button class="option-btn">que</button><button class="option-btn">qui</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="d'où">
                <p class="q-text">4. Le village _____ je viens est en montagne.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">où</button><button class="option-btn">d'où</button><button class="option-btn">que</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="où">
                <p class="q-text">5. L'année _____ je suis né était 2009.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">qui</button><button class="option-btn">que</button><button class="option-btn">où</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="ou-8" data-step="Pratique — à compléter">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">8</span> Pratique — à compléter</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Complétez avec qui, que ou où</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">1. Voici la chambre _____ je dors.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="où" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">2. C'est le moment _____ tout a changé.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="où" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">3. Le restaurant _____ nous avons dîné était cher.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="où" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">4. La personne _____ m'a aidé était très gentille.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="qui" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">5. Le livre _____ tu m'as offert est passionnant.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="que" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="accent-bar">
                <span class="ab-label">Accents :</span>
                <button class="accent-key">é</button><button class="accent-key">è</button><button class="accent-key">ê</button>
                <button class="accent-key">à</button><button class="accent-key">ç</button><button class="accent-key">ù</button>
                <button class="accent-key">û</button><button class="accent-key">î</button><button class="accent-key">ô</button>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn fib-check student-only">✓ Vérifier</button>
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </section>
      <!-- ================= 5.4 DONT ================= -->
      <section data-topic="relatifs" data-topic-name="Les Pronoms Relatifs" data-sub="DONT">

        <section data-slide-id="dont-1" data-step="Description">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">1</span> Description</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">DONT — replaces "de + noun"</h2>
            <p class="editable-field"><em>Dont</em> is used whenever the second sentence would contain <strong>de</strong> — because of the verb, or to show possession.</p>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">① Verbe + DE</h3>
                <p class="example-text">C'est le livre. Je parle <span class="highlight hl-aux">de ce livre</span>.</p>
                <p class="example-text">→ C'est le livre <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">dont</span> je parle.</p>
                <p class="gloss">It's the book I'm talking about.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">② Possession</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Je connais un homme. <span class="highlight hl-aux">Sa</span> fille est médecin.</p>
                <p class="example-text">→ Je connais un homme <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">dont</span> la fille est médecin.</p>
                <p class="gloss">I know a man whose daughter is a doctor.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field"><strong>Les verbes avec « de » les plus courants:</strong>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">parler de</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">avoir besoin de</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">avoir envie de</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">se souvenir de</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">rêver de</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">s'occuper de</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">être fier de</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">être content de</span></p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="dont-2" data-step="Formation">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">2</span> Formation</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">La formule — DONT + sujet + verbe</h2>
            <div class="formula-pipeline">
              <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Antécédent</span><span class="f-value">le livre</span></div>
              <div class="f-op">+</div>
              <div class="f-box" style="border-color:var(--purple);"><span class="f-label">DONT</span><span class="f-value" style="color:var(--purple);">dont</span></div>
              <div class="f-op">+</div>
              <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Sujet + verbe</span><span class="f-value">je parle</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <p class="editable-field">The word order after <em>dont</em> is <strong>always</strong> subject → verb → rest. Nothing is inverted.</p>
              <table class="subj-table">
                <tr><th>Phrase de départ</th><th>Avec DONT</th></tr>
                <tr><td>J'ai besoin <strong>de ce stylo</strong>.</td><td>le stylo <span class="key-form">dont</span> j'ai besoin</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Je me souviens <strong>de ce jour</strong>.</td><td>le jour <span class="key-form">dont</span> je me souviens</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Elle est fière <strong>de son fils</strong>.</td><td>le fils <span class="key-form">dont</span> elle est fière</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Le toit</strong> de la maison est rouge.</td><td>la maison <span class="key-form">dont</span> le toit est rouge</td></tr>
              </table>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="dont-3" data-step="Exceptions">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">3</span> Exceptions</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Les exceptions — l'article remplace le possessif</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Possession — pas de « son / sa / ses »</h3>
                <p class="example-text">✗ L'homme dont <span class="highlight hl-neg">sa</span> fille est médecin…</p>
                <p class="example-text">✓ L'homme dont <span class="highlight hl-verb">la</span> fille est médecin…</p>
                <p class="gloss">The man whose daughter is a doctor.</p>
                <p class="gloss"><em>Dont</em> already carries the idea of "whose", so the possessive would be a repetition.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Ce dont — sans antécédent</h3>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-pronoun">Ce dont</span> j'ai besoin, c'est du repos.</p>
                <p class="gloss">What I need is rest.</p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-pronoun">Ce dont</span> tu parles est intéressant.</p>
                <p class="gloss">What you're talking about is interesting.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field"><strong>Où DONT ne marche pas:</strong> after a preposition + de (such as <em>à côté de</em>, <em>près de</em>, <em>au milieu de</em>),
              French uses <em>duquel / de laquelle</em> instead:<br>
              <em>La maison <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">à côté de laquelle</span> j'habite…</em> <span class="gloss">The house next to which I live…</span></p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="dont-4" data-step="Pièges">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">4</span> Pièges</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">⚠️ Trap Alert — spotting the hidden « de »</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box red content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--crimson);">✗ Wrong</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Le film <span class="highlight hl-neg">que</span> je parle…</p>
                <p class="example-text">Le stylo <span class="highlight hl-neg">que</span> j'ai besoin…</p>
                <p class="example-text">La fille dont <span class="highlight hl-neg">son</span> père est prof…</p>
                <p class="example-text">Le livre dont <span class="highlight hl-neg">j'en</span> parle…</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box green content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--green);">✓ Right</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Le film <span class="highlight hl-verb">dont</span> je parle… <span class="gloss">parler DE</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Le stylo <span class="highlight hl-verb">dont</span> j'ai besoin… <span class="gloss">avoir besoin DE</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">La fille dont <span class="highlight hl-verb">le</span> père est prof… <span class="gloss">article, not possessive</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Le livre <span class="highlight hl-verb">dont</span> je parle… <span class="gloss">no extra <em>en</em></span></p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">🔑 <strong>The routine:</strong> rebuild the second sentence on its own.
              If it needs <span class="highlight hl-aux">de</span> — <em>je parle <strong>de</strong>…, j'ai besoin <strong>de</strong>…, le toit <strong>de</strong>…</em> — the answer is <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">dont</span>.
              If it needs <strong>à</strong> or nothing, it is not <em>dont</em>.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="dont-5" data-step="Exemples">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">5</span> Exemples travaillés</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Worked examples</h2>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <p class="example-text">Voici le dictionnaire <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">dont</span> j'ai besoin.</p>
              <p class="gloss">Here is the dictionary I need. — avoir besoin de</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">C'est un professeur <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">dont</span> tous les élèves parlent.</p>
              <p class="gloss">He's a teacher all the pupils talk about.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">J'ai un voisin <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">dont</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">le</span> chien aboie toute la nuit.</p>
              <p class="gloss">I have a neighbour whose dog barks all night.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-pronoun">Ce dont</span> je rêve, c'est de visiter la France.</p>
              <p class="gloss">What I dream of is visiting France.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="dont-6" data-step="En contexte">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">6</span> En contexte</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">In context — Entre Jeunes themes</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">L.4 — Le plaisir de lire</h3>
                <p class="example-text">C'est le roman dont tout le monde parle.</p>
                <p class="gloss">It's the novel everyone is talking about.</p>
                <h3>L.3 — Chercher du travail</h3>
                <p class="example-text">L'expérience dont j'ai besoin me manque encore.</p>
                <p class="gloss">The experience I need is still lacking.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">L.1 — La famille</h3>
                <p class="example-text">J'ai une amie dont les parents sont français.</p>
                <p class="gloss">I have a friend whose parents are French.</p>
                <h3 style="color:var(--gold);">L.2 — Après le bac</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Le métier dont je rêve, c'est architecte.</p>
                <p class="gloss">The job I dream of is architect.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="dont-7" data-step="Pratique QCM">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">7</span> Pratique — QCM</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Choose the correct relative pronoun</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="dont">
                <p class="q-text">1. C'est le film _____ je t'ai parlé.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">que</button><button class="option-btn">dont</button><button class="option-btn">où</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="dont">
                <p class="q-text">2. Voici l'outil _____ j'ai besoin.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">qui</button><button class="option-btn">que</button><button class="option-btn">dont</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="dont la">
                <p class="q-text">3. Je connais une dame _____ fille est avocate.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">dont sa</button><button class="option-btn">dont la</button><button class="option-btn">que la</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="que">
                <p class="q-text">4. Le livre _____ j'ai acheté est cher.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">dont</button><button class="option-btn">que</button><button class="option-btn">où</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="Ce dont">
                <p class="q-text">5. _____ j'ai envie, c'est d'un café.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">Ce que</button><button class="option-btn">Ce dont</button><button class="option-btn">Ce qui</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="dont-8" data-step="Pratique — à compléter">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">8</span> Pratique — à compléter</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Complétez avec « dont »</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">1. C'est l'ami _____ je t'ai parlé hier.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="dont" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">2. Le sac _____ tu as envie coûte cher.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="dont" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">3. J'ai un cousin _____ _____ femme est italienne. <span class="gloss">(dont + article)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="dont la" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">4. Le jour _____ je me souviens le mieux, c'est mon anniversaire.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="dont" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">5. C'est une ville _____ les monuments sont célèbres.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="dont" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="accent-bar">
                <span class="ab-label">Accents :</span>
                <button class="accent-key">é</button><button class="accent-key">è</button><button class="accent-key">ê</button>
                <button class="accent-key">à</button><button class="accent-key">ç</button><button class="accent-key">ù</button>
                <button class="accent-key">û</button><button class="accent-key">î</button><button class="accent-key">ô</button>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn fib-check student-only">✓ Vérifier</button>
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </section>

      <!-- ================= 5.5 LEQUEL & COMPOSÉS ================= -->
      <section data-topic="relatifs" data-topic-name="Les Pronoms Relatifs" data-sub="LEQUEL &amp; composés">

        <section data-slide-id="lequel-1" data-step="Description">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">1</span> Description</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">LEQUEL — the compound relative pronouns</h2>
            <p class="editable-field">These are used <strong>after a preposition</strong> when the antecedent is a <strong>thing</strong>. Unlike <em>qui/que/où/dont</em>, they change for gender and number.</p>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <table class="subj-table">
                <tr><th></th><th>Masculin</th><th>Féminin</th></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Singulier</strong></td><td class="key-form">lequel</td><td class="key-form">laquelle</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Pluriel</strong></td><td class="key-form">lesquels</td><td class="key-form">lesquelles</td></tr>
              </table>
              <p class="example-text" style="margin-top:8px;">C'est la raison <span class="highlight hl-aux">pour</span> <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">laquelle</span> je suis venu.</p>
              <p class="gloss">That's the reason for which I came.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">⚠️ <strong>For people, prefer <em>qui</em>:</strong>
                <em>L'ami <span class="highlight hl-aux">avec</span> <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">qui</span> je travaille</em> ✓ <span class="gloss">(not "avec lequel", though it is not wrong)</span><br>
                <strong>For things, <em>lequel</em> is required:</strong>
                <em>Le stylo <span class="highlight hl-aux">avec</span> <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">lequel</span> j'écris</em> ✓</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="lequel-2" data-step="Formation">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">2</span> Formation</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">La formule — les contractions avec À et DE</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">À + lequel</h3>
                <table class="subj-table">
                  <tr><td>à + lequel</td><td class="key-form">auquel</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>à + laquelle</td><td class="key-form">à laquelle</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>à + lesquels</td><td class="key-form">auxquels</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>à + lesquelles</td><td class="key-form">auxquelles</td></tr>
                </table>
                <p class="gloss">Only the feminine singular does not contract.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">DE + lequel</h3>
                <table class="subj-table">
                  <tr><td>de + lequel</td><td class="key-form">duquel</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>de + laquelle</td><td class="key-form">de laquelle</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>de + lesquels</td><td class="key-form">desquels</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>de + lesquelles</td><td class="key-form">desquelles</td></tr>
                </table>
                <p class="gloss">Same pattern as <em>au/du</em> with ordinary articles.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Le projet <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">auquel</span> je pense est ambitieux.</p>
              <p class="gloss">The project I'm thinking about is ambitious. — penser à</p>
              <p class="example-text">Les questions <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">auxquelles</span> j'ai répondu étaient faciles.</p>
              <p class="gloss">The questions I answered were easy. — répondre à</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="lequel-3" data-step="Exceptions">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">3</span> Exceptions</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Les exceptions — quand DONT cède la place</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Locutions en « de » → duquel</h3>
                <p>After compound prepositions ending in <em>de</em>, <em>dont</em> is impossible:</p>
                <p class="example-text">à côté <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">de laquelle</span> · près <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">duquel</span> · au milieu <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">duquel</span> · au cours <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">duquel</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">La maison <span class="highlight hl-aux">à côté de laquelle</span> j'habite est bleue.</p>
                <p class="gloss">The house next to which I live is blue.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Personnes après préposition</h3>
                <p>With people, both are possible but <em>qui</em> is more natural:</p>
                <p class="example-text">La personne <span class="highlight hl-verb">avec qui</span> je travaille… ✓ <span class="gloss">preferred</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">La personne <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">avec laquelle</span> je travaille… ✓ <span class="gloss">correct, more formal</span></p>
                <p class="gloss">But after <em>parmi</em> and <em>entre</em>, <strong>lequel</strong> is compulsory even for people:
                  <em>les amis <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">parmi lesquels</span>…</em></p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="lequel-4" data-step="Pièges">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">4</span> Pièges</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">⚠️ Trap Alert — agreement and contraction</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box red content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--crimson);">✗ Wrong</h3>
                <p class="example-text">La raison pour <span class="highlight hl-neg">lequel</span> je viens…</p>
                <p class="example-text">Le projet <span class="highlight hl-neg">à lequel</span> je pense…</p>
                <p class="example-text">Les questions <span class="highlight hl-neg">auxquels</span> j'ai répondu… <span class="gloss">(questions is feminine)</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">La table <span class="highlight hl-neg">dont</span> je suis assis à côté…</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box green content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--green);">✓ Right</h3>
                <p class="example-text">La raison pour <span class="highlight hl-verb">laquelle</span>… <span class="gloss">fem. sing.</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Le projet <span class="highlight hl-verb">auquel</span> je pense… <span class="gloss">à + lequel</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Les questions <span class="highlight hl-verb">auxquelles</span>… <span class="gloss">fem. plural</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">La table <span class="highlight hl-verb">à côté de laquelle</span> je suis assis…</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">🔑 <strong>Two checks every time:</strong>
                ① What <strong>gender and number</strong> is the antecedent? Pick lequel / laquelle / lesquels / lesquelles.
                ② Does the verb or phrase need <strong>à</strong> or <strong>de</strong>? Then contract.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="lequel-5" data-step="Exemples">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">5</span> Exemples travaillés</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Worked examples</h2>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <p class="example-text">C'est la raison <span class="highlight hl-aux">pour</span> <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">laquelle</span> j'ai refusé.</p>
              <p class="gloss">That's the reason why I refused. — feminine singular</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Voici le stylo <span class="highlight hl-aux">avec</span> <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">lequel</span> j'ai écrit la lettre.</p>
              <p class="gloss">Here is the pen with which I wrote the letter.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Le sujet <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">auquel</span> je m'intéresse est l'histoire.</p>
              <p class="gloss">The subject I'm interested in is history. — s'intéresser à</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Les amis <span class="highlight hl-aux">parmi</span> <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">lesquels</span> j'ai grandi habitent toujours ici.</p>
              <p class="gloss">The friends among whom I grew up still live here.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="lequel-6" data-step="En contexte">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">6</span> En contexte</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">In context — more formal writing</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">L.3 — Chercher du travail</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Le poste auquel je postule exige de l'expérience.</p>
                <p class="gloss">The post I'm applying for requires experience.</p>
                <h3>L.2 — Après le bac</h3>
                <p class="example-text">L'université à laquelle j'ai écrit m'a répondu.</p>
                <p class="gloss">The university I wrote to replied to me.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">L.8 — L'environnement</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Le problème auquel nous faisons face est mondial.</p>
                <p class="gloss">The problem we are facing is global.</p>
                <h3 style="color:var(--gold);">L.10 — Vive la République</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Les valeurs sur lesquelles repose la République sont essentielles.</p>
                <p class="gloss">The values on which the Republic rests are essential.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">💡 <strong>Register note:</strong> <em>lequel</em> sounds formal. In a letter to a friend, prefer <em>qui/que/où/dont</em>.
              Save the compound forms for essays and formal letters — where they earn credit.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="lequel-7" data-step="Pratique QCM">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">7</span> Pratique — QCM</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Choose the correct compound pronoun</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="laquelle">
                <p class="q-text">1. C'est la raison pour _____ je pars.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">lequel</button><button class="option-btn">laquelle</button><button class="option-btn">lesquelles</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="auquel">
                <p class="q-text">2. Le projet _____ je participe est important. <span class="gloss">(participer à)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">à lequel</button><button class="option-btn">auquel</button><button class="option-btn">duquel</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="auxquelles">
                <p class="q-text">3. Les questions _____ j'ai répondu étaient difficiles.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">auxquels</button><button class="option-btn">auxquelles</button><button class="option-btn">desquelles</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="avec qui">
                <p class="q-text">4. L'ami _____ je voyage est indien.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">avec qui</button><button class="option-btn">avec que</button><button class="option-btn">dont</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="sur lesquels">
                <p class="q-text">5. Les principes _____ repose la loi sont clairs.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">sur lesquels</button><button class="option-btn">sur lequels</button><button class="option-btn">auxquels</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="lequel-8" data-step="Pratique — à compléter">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">8</span> Pratique — à compléter</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Complétez avec un pronom relatif composé</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">1. La table sur _____ j'ai posé mes clés. <span class="gloss">(fém. sing.)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="laquelle" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">2. Le concours _____ je me prépare est en mai. <span class="gloss">(se préparer à)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="auquel" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">3. Les raisons pour _____ il est parti restent mystérieuses.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="lesquelles" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">4. Le bâtiment à côté _____ se trouve l'école. <span class="gloss">(masc. sing.)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="duquel" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">5. Les collègues avec _____ je travaille sont sympathiques. <span class="gloss">(masc. plur.)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="lesquels|qui" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="accent-bar">
                <span class="ab-label">Accents :</span>
                <button class="accent-key">é</button><button class="accent-key">è</button><button class="accent-key">ê</button>
                <button class="accent-key">à</button><button class="accent-key">ç</button><button class="accent-key">ù</button>
                <button class="accent-key">û</button><button class="accent-key">î</button><button class="accent-key">ô</button>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn fib-check student-only">✓ Vérifier</button>
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </section>

      <!-- ================= TOPIC 5 CLOSER ================= -->
      <section data-topic="relatifs" data-topic-name="Les Pronoms Relatifs" data-sub="Synthèse &amp; Examen">

        <section data-slide-id="rel-fin-1" data-step="Arbre de décision">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">🌳 Arbre de décision — quel pronom relatif ?</h2>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <table class="subj-table">
                <tr><th>Question à se poser</th><th>Réponse</th><th>Exemple</th></tr>
                <tr><td>Un <strong>verbe</strong> suit directement ?</td><td class="key-form">QUI</td><td>l'homme <strong>qui</strong> parle</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Un <strong>nouveau sujet</strong> suit ?</td><td class="key-form">QUE</td><td>le livre <strong>que</strong> je lis</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Un <strong>lieu</strong> ou un <strong>temps</strong> ?</td><td class="key-form">OÙ</td><td>la ville <strong>où</strong> j'habite</td></tr>
                <tr><td>La phrase contient <strong>de</strong> ?</td><td class="key-form">DONT</td><td>le film <strong>dont</strong> je parle</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Une <strong>préposition</strong> + une chose ?</td><td class="key-form">LEQUEL</td><td>la raison pour <strong>laquelle</strong></td></tr>
                <tr><td>Une <strong>préposition</strong> + une personne ?</td><td class="key-form">QUI</td><td>l'ami avec <strong>qui</strong></td></tr>
              </table>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">🔑 <strong>Method in the exam:</strong> split the sentence back into two.
              Look at what the <strong>second</strong> sentence needs — a subject, an object, a place, a <em>de</em>, or a preposition.
              That tells you the pronoun in under five seconds.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="rel-fin-2" data-step="Examen CBSE">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">📝 Examen blanc — Les Pronoms Relatifs</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text"><span class="q-tag">CBSE 2024</span>1. Elle a bien réussi à ce contrôle. Elle avait fait bien attention à ce contrôle.<br>→ Elle a bien réussi au contrôle _____ elle avait fait bien attention.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="auquel" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">2. Voici le professeur _____ enseigne l'histoire.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="qui" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">3. Le film _____ nous avons vu hier était excellent.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="que" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">4. C'est la maison _____ je suis né.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="où" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">5. L'ordinateur _____ j'ai besoin coûte cher.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="dont" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">6. La raison pour _____ il est absent est simple.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="laquelle" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="accent-bar">
                <span class="ab-label">Accents :</span>
                <button class="accent-key">é</button><button class="accent-key">è</button><button class="accent-key">ê</button>
                <button class="accent-key">à</button><button class="accent-key">ç</button><button class="accent-key">ù</button>
                <button class="accent-key">û</button><button class="accent-key">î</button><button class="accent-key">ô</button>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn fib-check student-only">✓ Vérifier</button>
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 6</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="rel-fin-3" data-step="Check-list">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">✅ Check-list — Les Pronoms Relatifs</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <p>☐ What follows the pronoun — a <strong>verb</strong> (qui) or a <strong>subject</strong> (que)?</p>
                <p>☐ Did I write <strong>où</strong> with its accent, and never <em>quand</em> as a relative?</p>
                <p>☐ Does the second clause need <strong>de</strong>? → dont</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <p>☐ After <em>dont</em>, did I use <strong>le/la/les</strong> and not <em>son/sa/ses</em>?</p>
                <p>☐ After <em>que</em> + avoir, did the <strong>participle agree</strong>?</p>
                <p>☐ With <em>lequel</em>, does it match in <strong>gender and number</strong>, and is à/de contracted?</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">🎯 <strong>Exam note:</strong> relative pronouns are 5 marks and appear as "reliez les deux phrases" or a fill-in.
              <strong>qui vs que</strong> alone accounts for most of the marks — master that pair first, then <em>dont</em>.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </section>
      <!-- ==================================================================
           TOPIC 6 — LE DISCOURS DIRECT ET INDIRECT
           =================================================================== -->
      <section data-topic="discours" data-topic-name="Discours Direct / Indirect" data-sub="Le Déclaratif">

        <section data-slide-id="disc-dec-1" data-step="Description">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">1</span> Description</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Le Discours Indirect — reporting what someone said</h2>
            <p class="editable-field"><strong>Direct speech</strong> quotes the exact words inside « guillemets ». <strong>Indirect speech</strong> reports them inside a subordinate clause — no quotation marks, no comma.</p>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Discours direct</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Paul dit : <span class="highlight hl-verb">« Je suis fatigué. »</span></p>
                <p class="gloss">Paul says: "I am tired."</p>
                <p class="gloss">Exact words · guillemets · two dots</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Discours indirect</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Paul dit <span class="highlight hl-aux">qu'</span><span class="highlight hl-subject">il</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">est</span> fatigué.</p>
                <p class="gloss">Paul says that he is tired.</p>
                <p class="gloss">No guillemets · <em>que</em> added · pronoun changed</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">🔑 <strong>Three things always change:</strong>
                ① punctuation disappears and <span class="highlight hl-aux">que</span> appears,
                ② the <span class="highlight hl-subject">pronouns</span> shift (je → il),
                ③ the <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">possessives</span> shift (mon → son).</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="disc-dec-2" data-step="Formation">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">2</span> Formation</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">La formule — verbe introducteur + QUE</h2>
            <div class="formula-pipeline">
              <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Verbe introducteur</span><span class="f-value">Il dit</span></div>
              <div class="f-op">+</div>
              <div class="f-box" style="border-color:var(--gold);"><span class="f-label">QUE</span><span class="f-value" style="color:var(--gold);">que / qu'</span></div>
              <div class="f-op">+</div>
              <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Proposition</span><span class="f-value">il est fatigué</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Les pronoms changent</h3>
                <table class="subj-table">
                  <tr><th>Direct</th><th>Indirect</th></tr>
                  <tr><td>« <strong>Je</strong> suis prêt. »</td><td>Il dit qu'<span class="key-form">il</span> est prêt.</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>« <strong>Nous</strong> partons. »</td><td>Ils disent qu'<span class="key-form">ils</span> partent.</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>« <strong>Tu</strong> as raison. »</td><td>Il dit que <span class="key-form">j'</span>ai raison.</td></tr>
                </table>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Les possessifs changent</h3>
                <table class="subj-table">
                  <tr><th>Direct</th><th>Indirect</th></tr>
                  <tr><td>« <strong>Ma</strong> mère est là. »</td><td>Il dit que <span class="key-form">sa</span> mère est là.</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>« <strong>Mon</strong> frère vient. »</td><td>Elle dit que <span class="key-form">son</span> frère vient.</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>« <strong>Nos</strong> amis arrivent. »</td><td>Ils disent que <span class="key-form">leurs</span> amis arrivent.</td></tr>
                </table>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="disc-dec-3" data-step="Exceptions">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">3</span> Exceptions</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Les exceptions — quand le temps ne change pas</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box green content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--green);">Verbe introducteur au PRÉSENT → rien ne change</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Il <span class="highlight hl-verb">dit</span> : « Je pars. »<br>→ Il <span class="highlight hl-verb">dit</span> qu'il <span class="highlight hl-verb">part</span>.</p>
                <p class="gloss">The tense stays exactly as it was.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Elle <span class="highlight hl-verb">affirme</span> : « J'ai fini. »<br>→ Elle affirme qu'elle <span class="highlight hl-verb">a fini</span>.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box red content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--crimson);">Verbe introducteur au PASSÉ → tout change</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Il <span class="highlight hl-aux">a dit</span> : « Je pars. »<br>→ Il a dit qu'il <span class="highlight hl-aux">partait</span>.</p>
                <p class="gloss">présent → imparfait</p>
                <p class="gloss">See sub-topic 4, <em>La concordance des temps</em>, for the full table.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field"><strong>Les verbes introducteurs utiles:</strong>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">dire que</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">déclarer que</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">affirmer que</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">expliquer que</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">répondre que</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">ajouter que</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">annoncer que</span>
                <span class="gloss">— varying them earns marks for style.</span></p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="disc-dec-4" data-step="Pièges">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">4</span> Pièges</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">⚠️ Trap Alert — punctuation and pronouns</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box red content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--crimson);">✗ Wrong</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Il dit que <span class="highlight hl-neg">« il est</span> fatigué ».</p>
                <p class="example-text">Il dit <span class="highlight hl-neg">,</span> qu'il est fatigué.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Il dit que <span class="highlight hl-neg">je</span> suis fatigué. <span class="gloss">(if Paul spoke about himself)</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Il dit que <span class="highlight hl-neg">ma</span> mère est là. <span class="gloss">(Paul's mother)</span></p>
              </div>
              <div class="box green content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--green);">✓ Right</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Il dit qu'il est fatigué. <span class="gloss">no guillemets at all</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Il dit qu'il est fatigué. <span class="gloss">no comma before que</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Il dit qu'<span class="highlight hl-verb">il</span> est fatigué. <span class="gloss">je → il</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Il dit que <span class="highlight hl-verb">sa</span> mère est là. <span class="gloss">ma → sa</span></p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">💡 <strong>Ask yourself: who is speaking, and who am I?</strong> The pronoun shift depends entirely on that.
              If Paul says « <em>Je</em> viens », and I report it, it becomes « <em>il</em> vient ». If Paul says « <em>Tu</em> viens » to me, it becomes « <em>je</em> viens ».</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="disc-dec-5" data-step="Exemples">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">5</span> Exemples travaillés</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Worked examples</h2>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <p class="example-text">Marie dit : « <span class="highlight hl-subject">Je</span> suis contente. »</p>
              <p class="example-text">→ Marie dit <span class="highlight hl-aux">qu'</span><span class="highlight hl-subject">elle</span> est contente.</p>
              <p class="gloss">Marie says that she is happy.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Les élèves disent : « <span class="highlight hl-subject">Nous</span> avons fini <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">nos</span> devoirs. »</p>
              <p class="example-text">→ Les élèves disent <span class="highlight hl-aux">qu'</span><span class="highlight hl-subject">ils</span> ont fini <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">leurs</span> devoirs.</p>
              <p class="gloss">The pupils say that they have finished their homework.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Il me dit : « <span class="highlight hl-subject">Tu</span> as raison. »</p>
              <p class="example-text">→ Il me dit <span class="highlight hl-aux">que</span> <span class="highlight hl-subject">j'</span>ai raison.</p>
              <p class="gloss">He tells me that I am right. — tu → je, because he is speaking to me</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text"><span class="q-tag">CBSE 2024</span>Gilles nous dit : « <span class="highlight hl-subject">Je</span> ne veux pas <span class="highlight hl-subject">vous</span> déranger. »</p>
              <p class="example-text">→ Gilles nous dit <span class="highlight hl-aux">qu'</span><span class="highlight hl-subject">il</span> ne veut pas <span class="highlight hl-subject">nous</span> déranger.</p>
              <p class="gloss">Gilles tells us that he doesn't want to disturb us.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="disc-dec-6" data-step="En contexte">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">6</span> En contexte</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">In context — reporting news</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">L.5 — Les médias</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Le journaliste annonce que la situation s'améliore.</p>
                <p class="gloss">The journalist announces that the situation is improving.</p>
                <h3>L.3 — Chercher du travail</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Le directeur explique qu'il n'y a pas de poste libre.</p>
                <p class="gloss">The director explains that there is no vacancy.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Dans une lettre</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Ma mère dit que tu peux venir chez nous.</p>
                <p class="gloss">My mother says that you can come to our place.</p>
                <h3 style="color:var(--gold);">L.7 — En pleine forme</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Le médecin répond qu'il faut dormir davantage.</p>
                <p class="gloss">The doctor replies that one must sleep more.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">💡 <strong>Letter tip:</strong> passing on someone's message is a natural way to use indirect speech —
              <em>Maman dit qu'elle t'embrasse.</em> <span class="gloss">Mum says she sends you her love.</span></p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="disc-dec-7" data-step="Pratique QCM">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">7</span> Pratique — QCM</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Choose the correct indirect speech</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="qu'il est malade">
                <p class="q-text">1. Paul dit : « Je suis malade. » → Paul dit _____.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">que je suis malade</button><button class="option-btn">qu'il est malade</button><button class="option-btn">qu'il était malade</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="que sa sœur arrive">
                <p class="q-text">2. Elle dit : « Ma sœur arrive. » → Elle dit _____.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">que ma sœur arrive</button><button class="option-btn">que sa sœur arrive</button><button class="option-btn">que leur sœur arrive</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="qu'ils ont fini">
                <p class="q-text">3. Ils disent : « Nous avons fini. » → Ils disent _____.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">qu'ils ont fini</button><button class="option-btn">que nous avons fini</button><button class="option-btn">qu'ils avaient fini</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="que j'ai raison">
                <p class="q-text">4. Il me dit : « Tu as raison. » → Il me dit _____.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">que tu as raison</button><button class="option-btn">que j'ai raison</button><button class="option-btn">qu'il a raison</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="qu'il ne veut pas nous déranger">
                <p class="q-text">5. <span class="q-tag">CBSE 2024</span>Gilles nous dit : « Je ne veux pas vous déranger. » → Gilles nous dit _____.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">qu'il ne veut pas nous déranger</button><button class="option-btn">qu'il ne veut pas vous déranger</button><button class="option-btn">que je ne veux pas vous déranger</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="disc-dec-8" data-step="Pratique — à compléter">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">8</span> Pratique — à compléter</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Mettez au discours indirect</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">1. Il dit : « Je travaille beaucoup. » → Il dit _____ beaucoup.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="qu'il travaille" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">2. Elle dit : « Mon père est médecin. » → Elle dit _____ médecin.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="que son père est" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">3. Ils disent : « Nous sommes prêts. » → Ils disent _____ prêts.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="qu'ils sont" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">4. Tu dis : « J'ai compris. » → Tu dis _____ compris.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="que tu as" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">5. Le prof dit : « L'examen est facile. » → Le prof dit _____ facile.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="que l'examen est" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="accent-bar">
                <span class="ab-label">Accents :</span>
                <button class="accent-key">é</button><button class="accent-key">è</button><button class="accent-key">ê</button>
                <button class="accent-key">à</button><button class="accent-key">ç</button><button class="accent-key">ù</button>
                <button class="accent-key">û</button><button class="accent-key">î</button><button class="accent-key">ô</button>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn fib-check student-only">✓ Vérifier</button>
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </section>

      <!-- ================= 6.2 L'INTERROGATIF ================= -->
      <section data-topic="discours" data-topic-name="Discours Direct / Indirect" data-sub="L'Interrogatif">

        <section data-slide-id="disc-int-1" data-step="Description">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">1</span> Description</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">L'Interrogatif indirect — reporting a question</h2>
            <p class="editable-field">A reported question loses its <strong>question mark</strong> and its <strong>inversion</strong>. It becomes an ordinary subordinate clause.</p>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Question directe</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Il demande : « <span class="highlight hl-verb">Viens-tu</span> ? »</p>
                <p class="gloss">He asks: "Are you coming?"</p>
                <p class="gloss">Inversion · question mark · guillemets</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Question indirecte</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Il demande <span class="highlight hl-aux">si</span> <span class="highlight hl-subject">je</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">viens</span>.</p>
                <p class="gloss">He asks if I am coming.</p>
                <p class="gloss">No inversion · full stop · <em>si</em> added</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">🔑 <strong>Verbes introducteurs:</strong> <em>demander</em>, <em>vouloir savoir</em>, <em>se demander</em>.
              Never <em>dire</em> for a question.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="disc-int-2" data-step="Formation">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">2</span> Formation</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">La formule — trois cas à connaître</h2>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <table class="subj-table">
                <tr><th>Question directe</th><th>Mot de liaison</th><th>Question indirecte</th></tr>
                <tr><td>« Tu viens ? » / « Est-ce que tu viens ? »</td><td class="key-form">si</td><td>Il demande <strong>si</strong> je viens.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>« <strong>Qu'est-ce que</strong> tu fais ? »</td><td class="key-form">ce que</td><td>Il demande <strong>ce que</strong> je fais.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>« <strong>Qu'est-ce qui</strong> se passe ? »</td><td class="key-form">ce qui</td><td>Il demande <strong>ce qui</strong> se passe.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>« <strong>Où</strong> habites-tu ? »</td><td class="key-form">où</td><td>Il demande <strong>où</strong> j'habite.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>« <strong>Quand</strong> pars-tu ? »</td><td class="key-form">quand</td><td>Il demande <strong>quand</strong> je pars.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>« <strong>Pourquoi</strong> pleures-tu ? »</td><td class="key-form">pourquoi</td><td>Il demande <strong>pourquoi</strong> je pleure.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>« <strong>Qui</strong> est là ? »</td><td class="key-form">qui</td><td>Il demande <strong>qui</strong> est là.</td></tr>
              </table>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">🔑 <strong>Only three things to memorise:</strong>
                yes/no question → <span class="highlight hl-aux">si</span> ·
                <em>qu'est-ce que</em> → <span class="highlight hl-aux">ce que</span> ·
                <em>qu'est-ce qui</em> → <span class="highlight hl-aux">ce qui</span>.
                Every other question word stays exactly as it is.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="disc-int-3" data-step="Exceptions">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">3</span> Exceptions</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Les exceptions — SI et l'ordre des mots</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">SI ne s'élide que devant « il / ils »</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Il demande <span class="highlight hl-verb">s'il</span> vient.</p>
                <p class="gloss">s' + il</p>
                <p class="example-text">Il demande <span class="highlight hl-verb">si elle</span> vient.</p>
                <p class="gloss">✗ never <em>s'elle</em></p>
                <p class="example-text">Il demande <span class="highlight hl-verb">si on</span> peut entrer.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Pas d'inversion — jamais</h3>
                <p class="example-text">✗ Il demande où <span class="highlight hl-neg">habites-tu</span>.</p>
                <p class="example-text">✓ Il demande où <span class="highlight hl-verb">tu habites</span>.</p>
                <p class="example-text">✗ Il demande quand <span class="highlight hl-neg">part-elle</span>.</p>
                <p class="example-text">✓ Il demande quand <span class="highlight hl-verb">elle part</span>.</p>
                <p class="gloss">Reported questions use ordinary word order.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field"><strong>Attention à « qui »:</strong> as a person-subject it stays <em>qui</em> —
              <em>« Qui est là ? » → Il demande <span class="highlight hl-aux">qui</span> est là.</em>
              Do not turn it into <em>ce qui</em>, which is only for things.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="disc-int-4" data-step="Pièges">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">4</span> Pièges</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">⚠️ Trap Alert — QUE never survives on its own</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box red content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--crimson);">✗ Wrong</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Il demande <span class="highlight hl-neg">qu'est-ce que</span> je fais.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Il demande <span class="highlight hl-neg">que</span> je fais.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Il demande <span class="highlight hl-neg">si</span> je fais quoi.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Il demande où <span class="highlight hl-neg">vas-tu</span> ?</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box green content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--green);">✓ Right</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Il demande <span class="highlight hl-verb">ce que</span> je fais.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Il demande <span class="highlight hl-verb">ce que</span> je fais.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Il demande <span class="highlight hl-verb">ce que</span> je fais.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Il demande où <span class="highlight hl-verb">tu vas</span>. <span class="gloss">no inversion, no ?</span></p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">🔑 <strong>The two-step routine:</strong> ① Is it a yes/no question? → <em>si</em>.
              ② Does it start with <em>qu'est-ce que / qu'est-ce qui</em>? → <em>ce que / ce qui</em>.
              ③ Anything else (où, quand, comment, pourquoi, combien, qui) → keep it and drop the inversion.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="disc-int-5" data-step="Exemples">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">5</span> Exemples travaillés</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Worked examples</h2>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <p class="example-text">Elle demande : « Est-ce que tu as faim ? »</p>
              <p class="example-text">→ Elle demande <span class="highlight hl-aux">si</span> j'ai faim.</p>
              <p class="gloss">She asks if I am hungry.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Il demande : « Qu'est-ce que tu veux ? »</p>
              <p class="example-text">→ Il demande <span class="highlight hl-aux">ce que</span> je veux.</p>
              <p class="gloss">He asks what I want.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Le prof demande : « Qu'est-ce qui ne va pas ? »</p>
              <p class="example-text">→ Le prof demande <span class="highlight hl-aux">ce qui</span> ne va pas.</p>
              <p class="gloss">The teacher asks what is wrong.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Ma mère demande : « Où vas-tu ? »</p>
              <p class="example-text">→ Ma mère demande <span class="highlight hl-aux">où</span> je vais.</p>
              <p class="gloss">My mother asks where I am going. — question word kept, inversion dropped</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="disc-int-6" data-step="En contexte">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">6</span> En contexte</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">In context — reporting an interview</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">L.3 — Chercher du travail</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Le recruteur demande si j'ai de l'expérience.</p>
                <p class="gloss">The recruiter asks if I have experience.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Il veut savoir pourquoi je veux ce poste.</p>
                <p class="gloss">He wants to know why I want this job.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">L.2 — Après le bac</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Mes parents me demandent ce que je veux étudier.</p>
                <p class="gloss">My parents ask me what I want to study.</p>
                <h3 style="color:var(--gold);">L.7 — En pleine forme</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Le médecin demande depuis quand j'ai mal.</p>
                <p class="gloss">The doctor asks how long I've been in pain.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="disc-int-7" data-step="Pratique QCM">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">7</span> Pratique — QCM</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Choose the correct link word</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="si">
                <p class="q-text">1. « Tu viens ? » → Il demande _____ je viens.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">que</button><button class="option-btn">si</button><button class="option-btn">ce que</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="ce que">
                <p class="q-text">2. « Qu'est-ce que tu manges ? » → Il demande _____ je mange.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">ce que</button><button class="option-btn">ce qui</button><button class="option-btn">que</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="ce qui">
                <p class="q-text">3. « Qu'est-ce qui se passe ? » → Il demande _____ se passe.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">ce que</button><button class="option-btn">ce qui</button><button class="option-btn">qui</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="où tu habites">
                <p class="q-text">4. « Où habites-tu ? » → Il demande _____.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">où habites-tu</button><button class="option-btn">où tu habites</button><button class="option-btn">si tu habites où</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="s'il">
                <p class="q-text">5. « Il vient ? » → Elle demande _____ vient.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">si il</button><button class="option-btn">s'il</button><button class="option-btn">ce qu'il</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="disc-int-8" data-step="Pratique — à compléter">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">8</span> Pratique — à compléter</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Mettez la question au discours indirect</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">1. « Est-ce que tu es prêt ? » → Il demande _____ prêt.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="si je suis" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">2. « Qu'est-ce que vous faites ? » → Elle demande _____ nous faisons.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="ce que" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">3. « Quand pars-tu ? » → Il demande quand _____.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="je pars" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">4. « Qu'est-ce qui t'intéresse ? » → Il demande _____ m'intéresse.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="ce qui" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">5. « Pourquoi es-tu en retard ? » → Elle demande pourquoi _____ en retard.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="je suis" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="accent-bar">
                <span class="ab-label">Accents :</span>
                <button class="accent-key">é</button><button class="accent-key">è</button><button class="accent-key">ê</button>
                <button class="accent-key">à</button><button class="accent-key">ç</button><button class="accent-key">ù</button>
                <button class="accent-key">û</button><button class="accent-key">î</button><button class="accent-key">ô</button>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn fib-check student-only">✓ Vérifier</button>
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </section>

      <!-- ================= 6.3 L'IMPÉRATIF ================= -->
      <section data-topic="discours" data-topic-name="Discours Direct / Indirect" data-sub="L'Impératif rapporté">

        <section data-slide-id="disc-imp-1" data-step="Description">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">1</span> Description</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">L'Impératif rapporté — reporting an order</h2>
            <p class="editable-field">An order or piece of advice becomes <strong>de + infinitif</strong> — not <em>que</em>, and not a conjugated verb.</p>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Ordre direct</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Il me dit : « <span class="highlight hl-verb">Viens</span> ! »</p>
                <p class="gloss">He tells me: "Come!"</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Ordre rapporté</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Il me dit <span class="highlight hl-aux">de</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">venir</span>.</p>
                <p class="gloss">He tells me to come.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field"><strong>Verbes introducteurs pour un ordre:</strong>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">dire de</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">demander de</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">ordonner de</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">conseiller de</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">interdire de</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">prier de</span>
                <span class="gloss">— all followed by <em>de</em> + infinitive.</span></p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="disc-imp-2" data-step="Formation">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">2</span> Formation</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">La formule</h2>
            <div class="formula-pipeline">
              <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Verbe introducteur</span><span class="f-value">Il me dit</span></div>
              <div class="f-op">+</div>
              <div class="f-box" style="border-color:var(--gold);"><span class="f-label">DE</span><span class="f-value" style="color:var(--gold);">de / d'</span></div>
              <div class="f-op">+</div>
              <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Infinitif</span><span class="f-value">venir</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <table class="subj-table">
                <tr><th>Discours direct</th><th>Discours indirect</th></tr>
                <tr><td>« Ferme la porte ! »</td><td>Il me dit <span class="key-form">de fermer</span> la porte.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>« Écoutez bien ! »</td><td>Le prof nous dit <span class="key-form">d'écouter</span> bien.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>« Sois patient ! »</td><td>Elle me dit <span class="key-form">d'être</span> patient.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>« Ne pars pas ! »</td><td>Il me dit <span class="key-form">de ne pas partir</span>.</td></tr>
              </table>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field"><strong>La négation:</strong> both words stay together <strong>before</strong> the infinitive —
              <em>de <span class="highlight hl-neg">ne pas</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">partir</span></em>, never <em>de ne partir pas</em>.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="disc-imp-3" data-step="Exceptions">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">3</span> Exceptions</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Les exceptions — pronoms et temps</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Les pronoms reprennent leur place normale</h3>
                <p class="example-text">« <span class="highlight hl-verb">Donne-moi</span> le livre ! »</p>
                <p class="example-text">→ Il me dit <span class="highlight hl-aux">de</span> <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">lui</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">donner</span> le livre.</p>
                <p class="gloss">The hyphen disappears; the pronoun moves before the infinitive.</p>
                <p class="example-text">« <span class="highlight hl-verb">Lève-toi</span> ! » → Il me dit <span class="highlight hl-aux">de</span> <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">me</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">lever</span>.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Le temps ne change JAMAIS</h3>
                <p>Because the result is an infinitive, there is no concordance to worry about:</p>
                <p class="example-text">Il <span class="highlight hl-verb">dit</span> de venir. <span class="gloss">present</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Il <span class="highlight hl-aux">a dit</span> de venir. <span class="gloss">past — still "de venir"</span></p>
                <p class="gloss">This makes reported orders the easiest of the three types.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="disc-imp-4" data-step="Pièges">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">4</span> Pièges</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">⚠️ Trap Alert — never use QUE for an order</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box red content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--crimson);">✗ Wrong</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Il me dit <span class="highlight hl-neg">que je viens</span>.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Il me dit <span class="highlight hl-neg">que venir</span>.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Il me dit de <span class="highlight hl-neg">ne partir pas</span>.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Il me dit de <span class="highlight hl-neg">donne-moi</span> le livre.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box green content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--green);">✓ Right</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Il me dit <span class="highlight hl-verb">de venir</span>. <span class="gloss">de + infinitive</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Il me dit <span class="highlight hl-verb">de venir</span>.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Il me dit de <span class="highlight hl-verb">ne pas partir</span>.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Il me dit de <span class="highlight hl-verb">lui donner</span> le livre.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">🔑 <strong>Three sentence types, three structures:</strong><br>
                Statement → <span class="highlight hl-aux">que</span> + conjugated verb ·
                Question → <span class="highlight hl-aux">si / ce que / ce qui</span> + conjugated verb ·
                Order → <span class="highlight hl-aux">de</span> + <strong>infinitive</strong>.<br>
                Identify the type <em>first</em>; the structure follows automatically.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="disc-imp-5" data-step="Exemples">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">5</span> Exemples travaillés</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Worked examples</h2>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <p class="example-text">Le prof dit : « Ouvrez vos livres ! »</p>
              <p class="example-text">→ Le prof nous dit <span class="highlight hl-aux">d'</span><span class="highlight hl-verb">ouvrir</span> nos livres.</p>
              <p class="gloss">The teacher tells us to open our books.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text"><span class="q-tag">CBSE 2024</span>Son père lui dit : « Ne va pas seul. »</p>
              <p class="example-text">→ Son père lui dit <span class="highlight hl-aux">de</span> <span class="highlight hl-neg">ne pas</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">aller</span> seul.</p>
              <p class="gloss">His father tells him not to go alone.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Elle me dit : « Téléphone-moi ce soir ! »</p>
              <p class="example-text">→ Elle me dit <span class="highlight hl-aux">de</span> <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">lui</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">téléphoner</span> le soir.</p>
              <p class="gloss">She tells me to phone her in the evening.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Le médecin conseille : « Reposez-vous ! »</p>
              <p class="example-text">→ Le médecin lui conseille <span class="highlight hl-aux">de</span> <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">se</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">reposer</span>.</p>
              <p class="gloss">The doctor advises him to rest.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="disc-imp-6" data-step="En contexte">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">6</span> En contexte</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">In context — passing on advice</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">L.7 — En pleine forme</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Le médecin me dit de faire plus de sport.</p>
                <p class="gloss">The doctor tells me to do more sport.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Il me conseille de ne pas manger trop de sucre.</p>
                <p class="gloss">He advises me not to eat too much sugar.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">L.8 — L'environnement</h3>
                <p class="example-text">On nous demande de recycler nos déchets.</p>
                <p class="gloss">We are asked to recycle our waste.</p>
                <h3 style="color:var(--gold);">L.2 — Après le bac</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Mes parents me disent de bien réfléchir avant de choisir.</p>
                <p class="gloss">My parents tell me to think carefully before choosing.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">💡 <strong>Letter tip:</strong> reporting advice you received is a natural way to fill an informal letter —
              <em>Mon prof m'a dit de travailler davantage.</em> One sentence, one structure, marks earned.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="disc-imp-7" data-step="Pratique QCM">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">7</span> Pratique — QCM</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Report the order correctly</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="de fermer">
                <p class="q-text">1. « Ferme la fenêtre ! » → Il me dit _____ la fenêtre.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">que je ferme</button><button class="option-btn">de fermer</button><button class="option-btn">de je ferme</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="de ne pas aller">
                <p class="q-text">2. <span class="q-tag">CBSE 2024</span>« Ne va pas seul. » → Son père lui dit _____ seul.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">de ne aller pas</button><button class="option-btn">de ne pas aller</button><button class="option-btn">qu'il ne va pas</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="d'être">
                <p class="q-text">3. « Sois sage ! » → Elle lui dit _____ sage.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">d'être</button><button class="option-btn">qu'il soit</button><button class="option-btn">de sois</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="de lui donner">
                <p class="q-text">4. « Donne-moi ton stylo ! » → Il me dit _____ mon stylo.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">de donne-moi</button><button class="option-btn">de lui donner</button><button class="option-btn">de me donner</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="de se reposer">
                <p class="q-text">5. « Repose-toi ! » → Le médecin lui dit _____.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">de se reposer</button><button class="option-btn">de te reposer</button><button class="option-btn">qu'il se repose</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="disc-imp-8" data-step="Pratique — à compléter">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">8</span> Pratique — à compléter</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Rapportez l'ordre</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">1. « Travaillez bien ! » → Le prof nous dit _____ bien.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="de travailler" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">2. « Ne fumez pas ! » → Le médecin lui dit _____.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="de ne pas fumer" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">3. « Attends-moi ! » → Elle me demande _____.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="de l'attendre" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">4. « Prends ton parapluie ! » → Ma mère me dit _____ mon parapluie.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="de prendre" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">5. « Ayez du courage ! » → Il nous dit _____ du courage.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="d'avoir" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="accent-bar">
                <span class="ab-label">Accents :</span>
                <button class="accent-key">é</button><button class="accent-key">è</button><button class="accent-key">ê</button>
                <button class="accent-key">à</button><button class="accent-key">ç</button><button class="accent-key">ù</button>
                <button class="accent-key">û</button><button class="accent-key">î</button><button class="accent-key">ô</button>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn fib-check student-only">✓ Vérifier</button>
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </section>
      <!-- ================= 6.4 LA CONCORDANCE DES TEMPS ================= -->
      <section data-topic="discours" data-topic-name="Discours Direct / Indirect" data-sub="La Concordance des Temps">

        <section data-slide-id="disc-conc-1" data-step="Description">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">1</span> Description</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">La Concordance des Temps — the tense shift</h2>
            <p class="editable-field">When the reporting verb is in the <strong>past</strong>, every tense inside the quotation moves <strong>one step further back</strong> in time.</p>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box green content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--green);">Verbe introducteur au PRÉSENT</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Il <span class="highlight hl-verb">dit</span> : « Je suis fatigué. »</p>
                <p class="example-text">→ Il <span class="highlight hl-verb">dit</span> qu'il <span class="highlight hl-verb">est</span> fatigué.</p>
                <p class="gloss">✅ No change at all.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box red content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--crimson);">Verbe introducteur au PASSÉ</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Il <span class="highlight hl-aux">a dit</span> : « Je suis fatigué. »</p>
                <p class="example-text">→ Il <span class="highlight hl-aux">a dit</span> qu'il <span class="highlight hl-aux">était</span> fatigué.</p>
                <p class="gloss">⚠️ présent → imparfait.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">🔑 <strong>Always check the reporting verb first.</strong> <em>dit / demande</em> → nothing changes.
              <em>a dit / disait / a demandé</em> → apply the shift table on the next slide.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="disc-conc-2" data-step="Formation">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">2</span> Formation</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Le tableau de la concordance</h2>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <table class="subj-table">
                <tr><th>Discours direct</th><th>→</th><th>Discours indirect (passé)</th></tr>
                <tr><td>Présent — <em>je suis</em></td><td>→</td><td class="key-form">Imparfait — j'étais</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Passé composé — <em>j'ai fini</em></td><td>→</td><td class="key-form">Plus-que-parfait — j'avais fini</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Futur simple — <em>je viendrai</em></td><td>→</td><td class="key-form">Conditionnel présent — je viendrais</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Futur antérieur — <em>j'aurai fini</em></td><td>→</td><td class="key-form">Conditionnel passé — j'aurais fini</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Futur proche — <em>je vais partir</em></td><td>→</td><td class="key-form">j'allais partir</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Imparfait — <em>j'étais</em></td><td>→</td><td class="key-form">Imparfait (inchangé)</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Plus-que-parfait — <em>j'avais vu</em></td><td>→</td><td class="key-form">Plus-que-parfait (inchangé)</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Impératif — <em>Viens !</em></td><td>→</td><td class="key-form">de + infinitif — de venir</td></tr>
              </table>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">💡 <strong>Notice the logic:</strong> each tense moves back one notch —
              present becomes past, past becomes further past, future becomes conditional.
              The two tenses that are <strong>already</strong> as far back as possible (imparfait, plus-que-parfait) simply stay put.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="disc-conc-3" data-step="Exceptions">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">3</span> Exceptions</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Les exceptions — la vérité générale</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Vérité toujours valable → présent conservé</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Le prof a dit que la Terre <span class="highlight hl-verb">tourne</span> autour du Soleil.</p>
                <p class="gloss">The teacher said that the Earth goes round the Sun. — still true today</p>
                <p class="example-text">Il a dit que l'eau <span class="highlight hl-verb">bout</span> à 100 degrés.</p>
                <p class="gloss">A permanent fact keeps the présent.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Situation encore vraie</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Il a dit qu'il <span class="highlight hl-verb">habite</span> à Paris.</p>
                <p class="gloss">He said he lives in Paris — and he still does.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Il a dit qu'il <span class="highlight hl-aux">habitait</span> à Paris.</p>
                <p class="gloss">He said he lived in Paris — perhaps no longer.</p>
                <p class="gloss">Both are correct; the meaning differs slightly.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">⚠️ <strong>In the exam</strong>, unless the sentence is an obvious universal truth, <strong>apply the shift</strong>.
              That is what the marking scheme expects.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="disc-conc-4" data-step="Pièges">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">4</span> Pièges</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">⚠️ Trap Alert — futur → conditionnel, not imparfait</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box red content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--crimson);">✗ Wrong</h3>
                <p class="example-text">« Je viendrai. » → Il a dit qu'il <span class="highlight hl-neg">venait</span>.</p>
                <p class="example-text">« J'ai fini. » → Il a dit qu'il <span class="highlight hl-neg">finissait</span>.</p>
                <p class="example-text">« J'étais malade. » → Il a dit qu'il <span class="highlight hl-neg">avait été</span> malade.</p>
                <p class="example-text">« Je suis prêt. » → Il a dit qu'il <span class="highlight hl-neg">est</span> prêt.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box green content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--green);">✓ Right</h3>
                <p class="example-text">→ Il a dit qu'il <span class="highlight hl-verb">viendrait</span>. <span class="gloss">futur → conditionnel</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">→ Il a dit qu'il <span class="highlight hl-verb">avait fini</span>. <span class="gloss">PC → plus-que-parfait</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">→ Il a dit qu'il <span class="highlight hl-verb">était</span> malade. <span class="gloss">imparfait unchanged</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">→ Il a dit qu'il <span class="highlight hl-verb">était</span> prêt. <span class="gloss">présent → imparfait</span></p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">🔑 <strong>The trap:</strong> <em>viendrai</em> (futur) and <em>viendrais</em> (conditionnel) differ by <strong>one letter</strong>.
              In reported past speech the answer is nearly always the one <strong>with the s</strong>.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="disc-conc-5" data-step="Exemples">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">5</span> Exemples travaillés</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Worked examples</h2>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <p class="example-text">Il a dit : « Je <span class="highlight hl-verb">travaille</span> beaucoup. »</p>
              <p class="example-text">→ Il a dit qu'il <span class="highlight hl-aux">travaillait</span> beaucoup.</p>
              <p class="gloss">présent → imparfait</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Elle a répondu : « J'<span class="highlight hl-verb">ai vu</span> ce film. »</p>
              <p class="example-text">→ Elle a répondu qu'elle <span class="highlight hl-aux">avait vu</span> ce film.</p>
              <p class="gloss">passé composé → plus-que-parfait</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Il m'a promis : « Je te <span class="highlight hl-verb">téléphonerai</span>. »</p>
              <p class="example-text">→ Il m'a promis qu'il me <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">téléphonerait</span>.</p>
              <p class="gloss">futur → conditionnel présent</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Elle a dit : « Quand j'<span class="highlight hl-verb">étais</span> jeune, je <span class="highlight hl-verb">jouais</span> du piano. »</p>
              <p class="example-text">→ Elle a dit que quand elle <span class="highlight hl-aux">était</span> jeune, elle <span class="highlight hl-aux">jouait</span> du piano.</p>
              <p class="gloss">imparfait → imparfait (no change)</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="disc-conc-6" data-step="En contexte">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">6</span> En contexte</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">In context — telling a story</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">L.3 — Chercher du travail</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Le directeur m'a dit que le poste était déjà pris.</p>
                <p class="gloss">The director told me that the post was already taken.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Il a ajouté qu'il me rappellerait.</p>
                <p class="gloss">He added that he would call me back. — conditionnel</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">L.5 — Les médias</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Le présentateur a annoncé qu'il y avait eu un accident.</p>
                <p class="gloss">The presenter announced that there had been an accident.</p>
                <h3 style="color:var(--gold);">L.2 — Après le bac</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Mon frère a dit qu'il choisirait la médecine.</p>
                <p class="gloss">My brother said he would choose medicine.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">💡 <strong>Recognise the link:</strong> the plus-que-parfait you learned in <em>Les Verbes</em> is exactly what the passé composé becomes here.
              Reported speech is where all your tenses come together.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="disc-conc-7" data-step="Pratique QCM">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">7</span> Pratique — QCM</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Apply the tense shift</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="était">
                <p class="q-text">1. « Je suis content. » → Il a dit qu'il _____ content.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">est</button><button class="option-btn">était</button><button class="option-btn">sera</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="avait fini">
                <p class="q-text">2. « J'ai fini mon travail. » → Elle a dit qu'elle _____ son travail.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">a fini</button><button class="option-btn">avait fini</button><button class="option-btn">finissait</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="viendrait">
                <p class="q-text">3. « Je viendrai demain. » → Il a dit qu'il _____ le lendemain.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">viendra</button><button class="option-btn">venait</button><button class="option-btn">viendrait</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="était">
                <p class="q-text">4. « J'étais malade. » → Il a dit qu'il _____ malade.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">était</button><button class="option-btn">avait été</button><button class="option-btn">est</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="est">
                <p class="q-text">5. « Je suis fatigué. » → Il dit qu'il _____ fatigué. <span class="gloss">(présent !)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">était</button><button class="option-btn">est</button><button class="option-btn">serait</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="disc-conc-8" data-step="Pratique — à compléter">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">8</span> Pratique — à compléter</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Appliquez la concordance</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">1. « Je pars. » → Il a dit qu'il _____.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="partait" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">2. « Nous avons gagné. » → Ils ont dit qu'ils _____.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="avaient gagné" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">3. « Je te verrai. » → Elle a dit qu'elle me _____.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="verrait" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">4. « Il fait beau. » → Il a remarqué qu'il _____ beau.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="faisait" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">5. « Je vais sortir. » → Il a dit qu'il _____ sortir.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="allait" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="accent-bar">
                <span class="ab-label">Accents :</span>
                <button class="accent-key">é</button><button class="accent-key">è</button><button class="accent-key">ê</button>
                <button class="accent-key">à</button><button class="accent-key">ç</button><button class="accent-key">ù</button>
                <button class="accent-key">û</button><button class="accent-key">î</button><button class="accent-key">ô</button>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn fib-check student-only">✓ Vérifier</button>
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </section>

      <!-- ================= 6.5 LES MARQUEURS DE TEMPS ================= -->
      <section data-topic="discours" data-topic-name="Discours Direct / Indirect" data-sub="Les Marqueurs de Temps">

        <section data-slide-id="disc-marq-1" data-step="Description">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">1</span> Description</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Les Marqueurs de Temps — words that move too</h2>
            <p class="editable-field">If the reporting happens <strong>later</strong>, words like <em>aujourd'hui</em> and <em>demain</em> no longer make sense. They must be re-anchored.</p>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <p class="example-text">Lundi, il a dit : « Je pars <span class="highlight hl-aux">demain</span>. »</p>
              <p class="gloss">On Monday he said: "I'm leaving tomorrow."</p>
              <p class="example-text">→ Il a dit qu'il partait <span class="highlight hl-aux">le lendemain</span>.</p>
              <p class="gloss">He said he was leaving the next day.</p>
              <p class="gloss">If I report this on Friday, "demain" would mean Saturday — which is wrong. Hence <em>le lendemain</em>.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">🔑 These changes apply <strong>only</strong> when the reporting verb is in the past — exactly like the tense shift.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="disc-marq-2" data-step="Formation">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">2</span> Formation</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Le tableau des marqueurs</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Le temps</h3>
                <table class="subj-table">
                  <tr><th>Direct</th><th>Indirect</th></tr>
                  <tr><td>aujourd'hui</td><td class="key-form">ce jour-là</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>hier</td><td class="key-form">la veille</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>avant-hier</td><td class="key-form">l'avant-veille</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>demain</td><td class="key-form">le lendemain</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>après-demain</td><td class="key-form">le surlendemain</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>maintenant</td><td class="key-form">à ce moment-là</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>ce matin</td><td class="key-form">ce matin-là</td></tr>
                </table>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Les périodes et le lieu</h3>
                <table class="subj-table">
                  <tr><th>Direct</th><th>Indirect</th></tr>
                  <tr><td>la semaine prochaine</td><td class="key-form">la semaine suivante</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>la semaine dernière</td><td class="key-form">la semaine précédente</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>l'année prochaine</td><td class="key-form">l'année suivante</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>l'année dernière</td><td class="key-form">l'année précédente</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>ici</td><td class="key-form">là</td></tr>
                </table>
                <p class="gloss">Pattern: <em>prochain</em> → <em>suivant</em>, <em>dernier</em> → <em>précédent</em>.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="disc-marq-3" data-step="Exceptions">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">3</span> Exceptions</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Les exceptions — quand rien ne change</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box green content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--green);">Verbe introducteur au présent</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Il dit : « Je pars demain. »</p>
                <p class="example-text">→ Il dit qu'il part <span class="highlight hl-verb">demain</span>.</p>
                <p class="gloss">Nothing changes — the moment of speaking is still now.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Rapport le jour même</h3>
                <p class="example-text">If you report on the <strong>same day</strong>, the original words still work:</p>
                <p class="example-text">Ce matin il a dit : « Je pars demain. »</p>
                <p class="example-text">→ Il a dit qu'il partait <span class="highlight hl-verb">demain</span>. ✓</p>
                <p class="gloss">Because "tomorrow" is still tomorrow for both of us.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">⚠️ <strong>In the exam</strong>, the expected answer is almost always the <strong>shifted</strong> form
              (<em>le lendemain, la veille, ce jour-là</em>), because the exercise assumes reporting at a later date. Use the table unless told otherwise.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="disc-marq-4" data-step="Pièges">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">4</span> Pièges</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">⚠️ Trap Alert — forgetting the time words entirely</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box red content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--crimson);">✗ Incomplet</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Il a dit qu'il partait <span class="highlight hl-neg">demain</span>.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Elle a dit qu'elle était venue <span class="highlight hl-neg">hier</span>.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Il a dit qu'il était malade <span class="highlight hl-neg">aujourd'hui</span>.</p>
                <p class="gloss">The tense was shifted but the time word was left behind — half marks lost.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box green content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--green);">✓ Complet</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Il a dit qu'il partait <span class="highlight hl-verb">le lendemain</span>.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Elle a dit qu'elle était venue <span class="highlight hl-verb">la veille</span>.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Il a dit qu'il était malade <span class="highlight hl-verb">ce jour-là</span>.</p>
                <p class="gloss">Tense AND time word both shifted.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">🔑 <strong>Four checks for every reported sentence:</strong>
                ① the <span class="highlight hl-aux">link word</span> (que / si / ce que / de),
                ② the <span class="highlight hl-subject">pronouns</span>,
                ③ the <span class="highlight hl-verb">tense</span>,
                ④ the <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">time words</span>. Students routinely do the first three and forget the fourth.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="disc-marq-5" data-step="Exemples">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">5</span> Exemples travaillés</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Worked examples — all four changes at once</h2>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <p class="example-text">Il a dit : « <span class="highlight hl-subject">Je</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">pars</span> <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">demain</span>. »</p>
              <p class="example-text">→ Il a dit <span class="highlight hl-aux">qu'</span><span class="highlight hl-subject">il</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">partait</span> <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">le lendemain</span>.</p>
              <p class="gloss">que · il · partait · le lendemain — four changes.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Elle a dit : « J'<span class="highlight hl-verb">ai vu</span> ce film <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">hier</span>. »</p>
              <p class="example-text">→ Elle a dit qu'elle <span class="highlight hl-verb">avait vu</span> ce film <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">la veille</span>.</p>
              <p class="gloss">passé composé → plus-que-parfait, hier → la veille.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Il a promis : « Je te <span class="highlight hl-verb">rendrai</span> ton livre <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">la semaine prochaine</span>. »</p>
              <p class="example-text">→ Il a promis qu'il me <span class="highlight hl-verb">rendrait</span> mon livre <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">la semaine suivante</span>.</p>
              <p class="gloss">futur → conditionnel, prochaine → suivante.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Elle a demandé : « <span class="highlight hl-verb">Es-tu</span> libre <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">aujourd'hui</span> ? »</p>
              <p class="example-text">→ Elle a demandé <span class="highlight hl-aux">si</span> j'<span class="highlight hl-verb">étais</span> libre <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">ce jour-là</span>.</p>
              <p class="gloss">A question: si · no inversion · imparfait · ce jour-là.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="disc-marq-6" data-step="En contexte">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">6</span> En contexte</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">In context — recounting a conversation</h2>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Une conversation rapportée</h3>
              <p class="example-text">Hier, mon ami m'a dit qu'il avait reçu ses résultats <strong>la veille</strong> et qu'il partirait en France <strong>la semaine suivante</strong>. Il m'a demandé si je voulais l'accompagner et m'a conseillé de préparer mon passeport.</p>
              <p class="gloss">Yesterday my friend told me that he had received his results the day before and that he would leave for France the following week. He asked me whether I wanted to go with him and advised me to get my passport ready.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">Notice all three sentence types in one paragraph:
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">que</span> for the statements,
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">si</span> for the question,
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">de</span> + infinitive for the advice —
                plus the tense shifts and <em>la veille / la semaine suivante</em>.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="disc-marq-7" data-step="Pratique QCM">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">7</span> Pratique — QCM</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Choose the correct time marker</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="le lendemain">
                <p class="q-text">1. « Je pars demain. » → Il a dit qu'il partait _____.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">demain</button><button class="option-btn">le lendemain</button><button class="option-btn">la veille</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="la veille">
                <p class="q-text">2. « Je l'ai vu hier. » → Elle a dit qu'elle l'avait vu _____.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">hier</button><button class="option-btn">la veille</button><button class="option-btn">ce jour-là</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="ce jour-là">
                <p class="q-text">3. « Je suis occupé aujourd'hui. » → Il a dit qu'il était occupé _____.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">aujourd'hui</button><button class="option-btn">ce jour-là</button><button class="option-btn">le lendemain</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="la semaine suivante">
                <p class="q-text">4. « Je viendrai la semaine prochaine. » → Il a dit qu'il viendrait _____.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">la semaine prochaine</button><button class="option-btn">la semaine suivante</button><button class="option-btn">la semaine précédente</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="demain">
                <p class="q-text">5. « Je pars demain. » → Il dit qu'il part _____. <span class="gloss">(présent !)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">le lendemain</button><button class="option-btn">demain</button><button class="option-btn">ce jour-là</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="disc-marq-8" data-step="Pratique — à compléter">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">8</span> Pratique — à compléter</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Transformez complètement</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">1. « Je viendrai demain. » → Il a dit qu'il viendrait _____.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="le lendemain" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">2. « J'ai fini hier. » → Elle a dit qu'elle avait fini _____.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="la veille" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">3. « Je suis ici. » → Il a dit qu'il était _____.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="là" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">4. « Je pars maintenant. » → Il a dit qu'il partait _____.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="à ce moment-là" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">5. « Je l'ai acheté l'année dernière. » → Il a dit qu'il l'avait acheté _____.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="l'année précédente" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="accent-bar">
                <span class="ab-label">Accents :</span>
                <button class="accent-key">é</button><button class="accent-key">è</button><button class="accent-key">ê</button>
                <button class="accent-key">à</button><button class="accent-key">ç</button><button class="accent-key">ù</button>
                <button class="accent-key">û</button><button class="accent-key">î</button><button class="accent-key">ô</button>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn fib-check student-only">✓ Vérifier</button>
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </section>

      <!-- ================= TOPIC 6 CLOSER ================= -->
      <section data-topic="discours" data-topic-name="Discours Direct / Indirect" data-sub="Synthèse &amp; Examen">

        <section data-slide-id="disc-fin-1" data-step="Tableau de référence">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">📊 Tableau de référence — les 4 changements</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">① Le mot de liaison</h3>
                <p>Déclaration → <span class="key-form">que</span></p>
                <p>Question oui/non → <span class="key-form">si</span></p>
                <p>Qu'est-ce que → <span class="key-form">ce que</span></p>
                <p>Qu'est-ce qui → <span class="key-form">ce qui</span></p>
                <p>Ordre → <span class="key-form">de + infinitif</span></p>
                <h3>② Les pronoms</h3>
                <p>je → il · nous → ils · mon → son · notre → leur</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">③ Les temps (si le verbe introducteur est au passé)</h3>
                <p>présent → <span class="key-form">imparfait</span></p>
                <p>passé composé → <span class="key-form">plus-que-parfait</span></p>
                <p>futur → <span class="key-form">conditionnel</span></p>
                <p>imparfait → <span class="key-form">imparfait</span></p>
                <h3 style="color:var(--gold);">④ Les marqueurs</h3>
                <p>demain → <span class="key-form">le lendemain</span> · hier → <span class="key-form">la veille</span> · aujourd'hui → <span class="key-form">ce jour-là</span></p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="disc-fin-2" data-step="Examen CBSE">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">📝 Examen blanc — Discours Indirect</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text"><span class="q-tag">CBSE 2024</span>1. Son père lui dit : « Ne va pas seul. » → Son père lui dit _____ seul.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="de ne pas aller" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text"><span class="q-tag">CBSE 2024</span>2. Gilles nous dit : « Je ne veux pas vous déranger. » → Gilles nous dit _____ déranger.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="qu'il ne veut pas nous" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">3. Elle a dit : « J'ai perdu mes clés. » → Elle a dit qu'elle _____ ses clés.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="avait perdu" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">4. Il demande : « Est-ce que tu viens ? » → Il demande _____.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="si je viens" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">5. Il a dit : « Je te téléphonerai demain. » → Il a dit qu'il me téléphonerait _____.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="le lendemain" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">6. Elle demande : « Qu'est-ce que tu lis ? » → Elle demande _____ je lis.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="ce que" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="accent-bar">
                <span class="ab-label">Accents :</span>
                <button class="accent-key">é</button><button class="accent-key">è</button><button class="accent-key">ê</button>
                <button class="accent-key">à</button><button class="accent-key">ç</button><button class="accent-key">ù</button>
                <button class="accent-key">û</button><button class="accent-key">î</button><button class="accent-key">ô</button>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn fib-check student-only">✓ Vérifier</button>
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 6</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="disc-fin-3" data-step="Check-list">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">✅ Check-list — Le Discours Indirect</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <p>☐ What <strong>type</strong> of sentence is it — statement, question or order?</p>
                <p>☐ Did I remove the <strong>guillemets</strong>, the colon and the question mark?</p>
                <p>☐ Did I use the right link word — <em>que / si / ce que / ce qui / de</em>?</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <p>☐ Did I change the <strong>pronouns and possessives</strong>?</p>
                <p>☐ Is the reporting verb <strong>past</strong>? Then shift the tense.</p>
                <p>☐ Did I also shift the <strong>time markers</strong>? (the most forgotten step)</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">🎯 <strong>Exam note:</strong> Le Discours Direct et Indirect is 5 marks in Section C.
              Questions usually mix all three sentence types, so identify the type <strong>before</strong> you start writing.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </section>
      <!-- ==================================================================
           TOPIC 7 — TROUVEZ LA QUESTION
           =================================================================== -->
      <section data-topic="question" data-topic-name="Trouvez la Question" data-sub="Est-ce que">

        <section data-slide-id="q-esk-1" data-step="Description">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">1</span> Description</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Est-ce que — the safest question form</h2>
            <p class="editable-field">The exam task <em>« Trouvez la question »</em> gives you an answer and asks you to write the question that produced it. <strong>Est-ce que</strong> is the form that never fails.</p>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <p class="editable-field">French has three ways to ask the same yes/no question:</p>
              <table class="subj-table">
                <tr><td>① Intonation</td><td class="key-form">Tu viens ?</td><td class="gloss">informal, spoken</td></tr>
                <tr><td>② Est-ce que</td><td class="key-form">Est-ce que tu viens ?</td><td class="gloss">neutral — always correct</td></tr>
                <tr><td>③ Inversion</td><td class="key-form">Viens-tu ?</td><td class="gloss">formal, written</td></tr>
              </table>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">💡 <strong>Exam strategy:</strong> unless the question specifically asks for inversion, <em>est-ce que</em> is accepted and is far harder to get wrong — no hyphens, no <em>-t-</em>, no word-order changes.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="q-esk-2" data-step="Formation">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">2</span> Formation</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">La formule — rien ne bouge après « est-ce que »</h2>
            <div class="formula-pipeline">
              <div class="f-box" style="border-color:var(--gold);"><span class="f-label">Est-ce que</span><span class="f-value" style="color:var(--gold);">Est-ce que</span></div>
              <div class="f-op">+</div>
              <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Sujet</span><span class="f-value">tu</span></div>
              <div class="f-op">+</div>
              <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Verbe</span><span class="f-value">viens ?</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Question totale (oui / non)</h3>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-aux">Est-ce que</span> tu aimes le français ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">Do you like French? — answer: oui / non</p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-aux">Est-ce qu'</span>il est arrivé ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">Has he arrived? — <em>qu'</em> before a vowel</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Avec un mot interrogatif</h3>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-subject">Où</span> <span class="highlight hl-aux">est-ce que</span> tu vas ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">Where are you going?</p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-subject">Quand</span> <span class="highlight hl-aux">est-ce qu'</span>il part ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">When is he leaving?</p>
                <p class="gloss">Pattern: question word + est-ce que + subject + verb.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="q-esk-3" data-step="Exceptions">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">3</span> Exceptions</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Les exceptions — l'élision et les formes longues</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Est-ce qu' devant voyelle</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Est-ce qu'<span class="highlight hl-verb">il</span> vient ?</p>
                <p class="example-text">Est-ce qu'<span class="highlight hl-verb">elle</span> a compris ?</p>
                <p class="example-text">Est-ce qu'<span class="highlight hl-verb">on</span> peut entrer ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">But: Est-ce <strong>que</strong> tu… / Est-ce <strong>que</strong> nous… — no elision before a consonant.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Les formes longues</h3>
                <p><strong>Qu'est-ce que</strong> = what (object)</p>
                <p class="example-text">Qu'est-ce que tu manges ? <span class="gloss">What are you eating?</span></p>
                <p><strong>Qu'est-ce qui</strong> = what (subject)</p>
                <p class="example-text">Qu'est-ce qui se passe ? <span class="gloss">What is happening?</span></p>
                <p><strong>Qui est-ce que</strong> = whom</p>
                <p class="example-text">Qui est-ce que tu vois ? <span class="gloss">Whom do you see?</span></p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="q-esk-4" data-step="Pièges">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">4</span> Pièges</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">⚠️ Trap Alert — never invert after « est-ce que »</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box red content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--crimson);">✗ Wrong</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Est-ce que <span class="highlight hl-neg">viens-tu</span> ?</p>
                <p class="example-text">Est-ce que <span class="highlight hl-neg">il</span> vient ?</p>
                <p class="example-text">Où <span class="highlight hl-neg">est-ce que vas-tu</span> ?</p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-neg">Que est-ce que</span> tu fais ?</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box green content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--green);">✓ Right</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Est-ce que <span class="highlight hl-verb">tu viens</span> ? <span class="gloss">normal order</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Est-ce <span class="highlight hl-verb">qu'il</span> vient ? <span class="gloss">elision</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Où est-ce que <span class="highlight hl-verb">tu vas</span> ?</p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-verb">Qu'est-ce que</span> tu fais ?</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">🔑 <strong>Choose one method, not two.</strong> <em>Est-ce que</em> already marks the sentence as a question,
              so the rest of the sentence stays exactly as it would in a statement.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="q-esk-5" data-step="Exemples">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">5</span> Exemples travaillés</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Worked examples — from answer to question</h2>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <p class="example-text">Réponse : <em>Oui, j'aime le chocolat.</em></p>
              <p class="example-text">→ Question : <span class="highlight hl-aux">Est-ce que</span> tu aimes le chocolat ?</p>
              <p class="gloss">A yes/no answer → a yes/no question.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Réponse : <em>Non, il n'est pas encore arrivé.</em></p>
              <p class="example-text">→ Question : <span class="highlight hl-aux">Est-ce qu'</span>il est arrivé ?</p>
              <p class="gloss">Note the elision before <em>il</em>.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Réponse : <em>Je vais à la bibliothèque.</em></p>
              <p class="example-text">→ Question : <span class="highlight hl-subject">Où</span> <span class="highlight hl-aux">est-ce que</span> tu vas ?</p>
              <p class="gloss">The answer gives a place → ask <em>où</em>.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Réponse : <em>Je mange une pomme.</em></p>
              <p class="example-text">→ Question : <span class="highlight hl-aux">Qu'est-ce que</span> tu manges ?</p>
              <p class="gloss">The answer gives a thing (object) → <em>qu'est-ce que</em>.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="q-esk-6" data-step="En contexte">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">6</span> En contexte</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">In context — everyday questions</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">L.8 — Faire des achats</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Est-ce que vous avez cette robe en bleu ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">Do you have this dress in blue?</p>
                <h3>L.5 — Les médias</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Est-ce que tu regardes souvent la télévision ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">Do you often watch television?</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">L.2 — Après le bac</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Qu'est-ce que tu veux faire après le bac ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">What do you want to do after school?</p>
                <h3 style="color:var(--gold);">L.7 — En pleine forme</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Est-ce que tu fais du sport régulièrement ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">Do you play sport regularly?</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="q-esk-7" data-step="Pratique QCM">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">7</span> Pratique — QCM</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Find the correct question</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="Est-ce que tu viens ?">
                <p class="q-text">1. <em>Oui, je viens.</em> → _____</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">Est-ce que tu viens ?</button><button class="option-btn">Est-ce que viens-tu ?</button><button class="option-btn">Est-ce tu viens ?</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="Est-ce qu'elle travaille ?">
                <p class="q-text">2. <em>Oui, elle travaille.</em> → _____</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">Est-ce que elle travaille ?</button><button class="option-btn">Est-ce qu'elle travaille ?</button><button class="option-btn">Est-ce qu'elle travaille-t-elle ?</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="Qu'est-ce que tu lis ?">
                <p class="q-text">3. <em>Je lis un roman.</em> → _____</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">Que est-ce que tu lis ?</button><button class="option-btn">Qu'est-ce que tu lis ?</button><button class="option-btn">Qu'est-ce qui tu lis ?</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="Où est-ce qu'ils habitent ?">
                <p class="q-text">4. <em>Ils habitent à Lyon.</em> → _____</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">Où est-ce qu'ils habitent ?</button><button class="option-btn">Où est-ce que habitent-ils ?</button><button class="option-btn">Où ils habitent est-ce que ?</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="Qu'est-ce qui se passe ?">
                <p class="q-text">5. <em>Un accident se passe.</em> → _____</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">Qu'est-ce que se passe ?</button><button class="option-btn">Qu'est-ce qui se passe ?</button><button class="option-btn">Qui est-ce que se passe ?</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="q-esk-8" data-step="Pratique — à compléter">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">8</span> Pratique — à compléter</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Complétez la question</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">1. <em>Oui, j'ai compris.</em> → _____ tu as compris ?</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="est-ce que" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">2. <em>Il mange du pain.</em> → _____ il mange ?</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="qu'est-ce qu'" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">3. <em>Nous partons à huit heures.</em> → _____ vous partez ?</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="quand est-ce que" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">4. <em>Le bruit me dérange.</em> → _____ te dérange ?</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="qu'est-ce qui" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">5. <em>Oui, elle est prête.</em> → _____ elle est prête ?</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="est-ce qu'" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="accent-bar">
                <span class="ab-label">Accents :</span>
                <button class="accent-key">é</button><button class="accent-key">è</button><button class="accent-key">ê</button>
                <button class="accent-key">à</button><button class="accent-key">ç</button><button class="accent-key">ù</button>
                <button class="accent-key">û</button><button class="accent-key">î</button><button class="accent-key">ô</button>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn fib-check student-only">✓ Vérifier</button>
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </section>

      <!-- ================= 7.2 L'INVERSION ================= -->
      <section data-topic="question" data-topic-name="Trouvez la Question" data-sub="L'Inversion">

        <section data-slide-id="q-inv-1" data-step="Description">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">1</span> Description</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">L'Inversion — the formal question</h2>
            <p class="editable-field">The verb and its subject pronoun swap places and are joined by a <strong>hyphen</strong>. This is the written, formal register — the one examiners like to see.</p>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Affirmation → Question</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Tu viens. → <span class="highlight hl-verb">Viens-tu</span> ?</p>
                <p class="example-text">Vous parlez. → <span class="highlight hl-verb">Parlez-vous</span> ?</p>
                <p class="example-text">Elle habite ici. → <span class="highlight hl-verb">Habite-t-elle</span> ici ?</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Le trait d'union est obligatoire</h3>
                <p class="example-text">✓ Viens<span class="highlight hl-aux">-</span>tu ?</p>
                <p class="example-text">✗ Viens tu ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">Without the hyphen it is not a question — it is a mistake.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="q-inv-2" data-step="Formation">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">2</span> Formation</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">La formule — verbe + trait d'union + pronom</h2>
            <div class="formula-pipeline">
              <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Verbe</span><span class="f-value">Viens</span></div>
              <div class="f-op">-</div>
              <div class="f-box" style="border-color:var(--purple);"><span class="f-label">Pronom sujet</span><span class="f-value" style="color:var(--purple);">tu</span></div>
              <div class="f-op">?</div>
              <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Question</span><span class="f-value">Viens-tu ?</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Temps composé — on inverse l'AUXILIAIRE</h3>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-aux">As-tu</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">compris</span> ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">Have you understood?</p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-aux">Est-elle</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">partie</span> ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">Has she left?</p>
                <p class="gloss">✗ never <em>« Compris as-tu ? »</em></p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Avec un nom sujet</h3>
                <p>Keep the noun, then add the matching pronoun:</p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-subject">Paul</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">vient-il</span> ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">Is Paul coming?</p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-subject">Tes parents</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">sont-ils</span> là ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">Are your parents there?</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="q-inv-3" data-step="Exceptions">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">3</span> Exceptions</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Le « -t- » euphonique</h2>
            <p class="editable-field">When the verb ends in a <strong>vowel</strong> and the pronoun is <em>il, elle</em> or <em>on</em>, French inserts <strong>-t-</strong> so the words don't clash.</p>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Il faut un -t-</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Il a → <span class="highlight hl-verb">A-t-il</span> ?</p>
                <p class="example-text">Elle va → <span class="highlight hl-verb">Va-t-elle</span> ?</p>
                <p class="example-text">Il parle → <span class="highlight hl-verb">Parle-t-il</span> ?</p>
                <p class="example-text">On mange → <span class="highlight hl-verb">Mange-t-on</span> ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">Verb ends in <strong>-a</strong> or <strong>-e</strong> → add -t-.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Pas de -t- nécessaire</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Il est → <span class="highlight hl-verb">Est-il</span> ? <span class="gloss">already ends in -t</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Il fait → <span class="highlight hl-verb">Fait-il</span> ? <span class="gloss">ends in -t</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Il prend → <span class="highlight hl-verb">Prend-il</span> ? <span class="gloss">ends in -d</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Tu viens → <span class="highlight hl-verb">Viens-tu</span> ? <span class="gloss">not il/elle/on</span></p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box red content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">⚠️ <strong>« Je » est particulier:</strong> inversion with <em>je</em> is rare and literary.
              Say <em>Est-ce que je peux…?</em> rather than <em>Puis-je…?</em> — except in the fixed polite form
              <span class="highlight hl-verb">Puis-je</span> <span class="gloss">May I?</span></p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="q-inv-4" data-step="Pièges">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">4</span> Pièges</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">⚠️ Trap Alert — hyphen, -t-, and negation</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box red content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--crimson);">✗ Wrong</h3>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-neg">A il</span> compris ?</p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-neg">Va-elle</span> à Paris ?</p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-neg">Compris as-tu</span> ?</p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-neg">Ne viens-tu</span> pas ? <span class="gloss">order of ne…pas</span></p>
              </div>
              <div class="box green content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--green);">✓ Right</h3>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-verb">A-t-il</span> compris ? <span class="gloss">-t- + hyphens</span></p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-verb">Va-t-elle</span> à Paris ?</p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-verb">As-tu</span> compris ? <span class="gloss">invert the auxiliary</span></p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-verb">Ne viens-tu pas</span> ? <span class="gloss">ne … pas wraps the inverted block</span></p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">🔑 <strong>Two-second check:</strong> does the verb end in a <strong>vowel</strong> AND is the pronoun <em>il/elle/on</em>?
              If yes → insert <strong>-t-</strong> with hyphens on both sides. Otherwise one hyphen is enough.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="q-inv-5" data-step="Exemples">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">5</span> Exemples travaillés</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Worked examples</h2>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <p class="example-text">Réponse : <em>Oui, je parle français.</em> → <span class="highlight hl-verb">Parlez-vous</span> français ?</p>
              <p class="gloss">Do you speak French?</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Réponse : <em>Il a vingt ans.</em> → Quel âge <span class="highlight hl-verb">a-t-il</span> ?</p>
              <p class="gloss">How old is he? — verb ends in a vowel + il → -t-</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Réponse : <em>Nous sommes arrivés hier.</em> → Quand <span class="highlight hl-verb">êtes-vous</span> arrivés ?</p>
              <p class="gloss">When did you arrive? — auxiliary inverted</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Réponse : <em>Marie habite à Paris.</em> → Où <span class="highlight hl-subject">Marie</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">habite-t-elle</span> ?</p>
              <p class="gloss">Where does Marie live? — noun subject kept + pronoun added</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="q-inv-6" data-step="En contexte">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">6</span> En contexte</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">In context — formal situations</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">L.3 — Chercher du travail</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Avez-vous de l'expérience dans ce domaine ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">Do you have experience in this field?</p>
                <p class="example-text">Pourquoi souhaitez-vous ce poste ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">Why do you want this job?</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">L.8 — Faire des achats</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Combien coûte-t-il ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">How much does it cost?</p>
                <h3 style="color:var(--gold);">Lettre formelle</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Pourriez-vous m'envoyer les documents ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">Could you send me the documents?</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">💡 <strong>Register matters:</strong> inversion in a job interview or formal letter sounds right;
              in a text message to a friend it sounds stiff. In the exam, formal contexts reward inversion.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="q-inv-7" data-step="Pratique QCM">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">7</span> Pratique — QCM</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Choose the correct inversion</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="A-t-il">
                <p class="q-text">1. <em>Il a un frère.</em> → _____ un frère ?</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">A-il</button><button class="option-btn">A-t-il</button><button class="option-btn">At-il</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="Est-elle">
                <p class="q-text">2. <em>Elle est française.</em> → _____ française ?</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">Est-t-elle</button><button class="option-btn">Est-elle</button><button class="option-btn">Est elle</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="Avez-vous fini">
                <p class="q-text">3. <em>Nous avons fini.</em> → _____ ?</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">Fini avez-vous</button><button class="option-btn">Avez-vous fini</button><button class="option-btn">Avez fini-vous</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="Va-t-elle">
                <p class="q-text">4. <em>Elle va au marché.</em> → Où _____ ?</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">va-elle</button><button class="option-btn">va-t-elle</button><button class="option-btn">vas-t-elle</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="Paul vient-il">
                <p class="q-text">5. <em>Paul vient ce soir.</em> → _____ ce soir ?</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">Vient Paul</button><button class="option-btn">Paul vient-il</button><button class="option-btn">Vient-Paul</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="q-inv-8" data-step="Pratique — à compléter">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">8</span> Pratique — à compléter</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Écrivez la question avec l'inversion</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">1. <em>Oui, je viens.</em> → _____ ? <span class="gloss">(venir — tu)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="viens-tu" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">2. <em>Il travaille à Paris.</em> → Où _____ ? <span class="gloss">(travailler — il)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="travaille-t-il" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">3. <em>Oui, elle a compris.</em> → _____ compris ? <span class="gloss">(avoir — elle)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="a-t-elle" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">4. <em>Nous partons demain.</em> → Quand _____ ? <span class="gloss">(partir — vous)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="partez-vous" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">5. <em>Ils sont arrivés.</em> → _____ arrivés ? <span class="gloss">(être — ils)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="sont-ils" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="accent-bar">
                <span class="ab-label">Accents :</span>
                <button class="accent-key">é</button><button class="accent-key">è</button><button class="accent-key">ê</button>
                <button class="accent-key">à</button><button class="accent-key">ç</button><button class="accent-key">ù</button>
                <button class="accent-key">û</button><button class="accent-key">î</button><button class="accent-key">ô</button>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn fib-check student-only">✓ Vérifier</button>
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </section>

      <!-- ================= 7.3 QUI / QUE INTERROGATIFS ================= -->
      <section data-topic="question" data-topic-name="Trouvez la Question" data-sub="QUI / QUE interrogatifs">

        <section data-slide-id="q-quique-1" data-step="Description">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">1</span> Description</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">QUI / QUE — asking about people and things</h2>
            <p class="editable-field">Two questions decide the form: is it a <strong>person</strong> or a <strong>thing</strong>? Is it the <strong>subject</strong> or the <strong>object</strong>?</p>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <table class="subj-table">
                <tr><th></th><th>Sujet (qui fait ?)</th><th>Objet (fait quoi ?)</th></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Personne</strong></td><td class="key-form">Qui …?</td><td class="key-form">Qui est-ce que …?</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Chose</strong></td><td class="key-form">Qu'est-ce qui …?</td><td class="key-form">Qu'est-ce que …? / Que …?</td></tr>
              </table>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">🔑 <strong>Memory hook:</strong> a form beginning with <span class="highlight hl-subject">QUI</span> asks about a <strong>person</strong>;
              a form beginning with <span class="highlight hl-verb">QU'</span> asks about a <strong>thing</strong>.
              The ending <em>-ci/-que</em> tells you subject or object.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="q-quique-2" data-step="Formation">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">2</span> Formation</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Les quatre formes en action</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Personnes</h3>
                <p><strong>Sujet</strong> — <span class="highlight hl-subject">Qui</span> parle ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">Who is speaking? — answer: Paul.</p>
                <p><strong>Objet</strong> — <span class="highlight hl-subject">Qui est-ce que</span> tu vois ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">Whom do you see? — answer: I see Paul.</p>
                <p class="gloss">Formal alternative: <em>Qui vois-tu ?</em></p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Choses</h3>
                <p><strong>Sujet</strong> — <span class="highlight hl-verb">Qu'est-ce qui</span> se passe ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">What is happening? — answer: An accident.</p>
                <p><strong>Objet</strong> — <span class="highlight hl-verb">Qu'est-ce que</span> tu fais ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">What are you doing? — answer: I'm reading.</p>
                <p class="gloss">Formal alternative: <em>Que fais-tu ?</em></p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field"><strong>Après une préposition, on utilise « qui » pour les personnes et « quoi » pour les choses:</strong><br>
                <em>Avec <span class="highlight hl-subject">qui</span> parles-tu ?</em> <span class="gloss">Who are you talking to?</span> ·
                <em>De <span class="highlight hl-verb">quoi</span> parles-tu ?</em> <span class="gloss">What are you talking about?</span></p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="q-quique-3" data-step="Exceptions">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">3</span> Exceptions</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Les exceptions — QUE et QUOI</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">QUE exige l'inversion</h3>
                <p class="example-text">✓ <span class="highlight hl-verb">Que</span> fais-tu ? <span class="gloss">inversion required</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">✗ <em>Que tu fais ?</em></p>
                <p class="example-text">✓ <span class="highlight hl-verb">Qu'est-ce que</span> tu fais ? <span class="gloss">no inversion</span></p>
                <p class="gloss">Short <em>que</em> is formal and always inverts; <em>qu'est-ce que</em> never does.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">QUOI — après préposition ou seul</h3>
                <p class="example-text">À <span class="highlight hl-verb">quoi</span> penses-tu ? <span class="gloss">What are you thinking about?</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">De <span class="highlight hl-verb">quoi</span> as-tu besoin ? <span class="gloss">What do you need?</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Tu fais <span class="highlight hl-verb">quoi</span> ? <span class="gloss">informal, spoken only</span></p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field"><strong>« Qui » ne s'élide jamais:</strong> <em>Qui est là ?</em> ✓ — never <em>Qu'est là ?</em>
              But <em>que</em> does elide: <em>Qu'as-tu ?</em> <span class="gloss">What's the matter with you?</span></p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="q-quique-4" data-step="Pièges">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">4</span> Pièges</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">⚠️ Trap Alert — <em>qu'est-ce qui</em> vs <em>qu'est-ce que</em></h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">QU'EST-CE QUI + verbe</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Qu'est-ce qui <span class="highlight hl-verb">se passe</span> ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">What is happening? — nothing between it and the verb</p>
                <p class="example-text">Qu'est-ce qui <span class="highlight hl-verb">t'intéresse</span> ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">What interests you?</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">QU'EST-CE QUE + sujet + verbe</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Qu'est-ce que <span class="highlight hl-subject">tu</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">fais</span> ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">What are you doing? — a subject follows</p>
                <p class="example-text">Qu'est-ce que <span class="highlight hl-subject">Paul</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">veut</span> ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">What does Paul want?</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box red content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">🔑 <strong>Exactly the same test as the relative pronouns:</strong>
                <span class="highlight hl-verb">…QUI</span> + verb · <span class="highlight hl-verb">…QUE</span> + subject + verb.
                If you can do <em>qui/que</em> in relatives, you already know this.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="q-quique-5" data-step="Exemples">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">5</span> Exemples travaillés</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Worked examples — from answer to question</h2>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <p class="example-text">Réponse : <em><span class="highlight hl-subject">Paul</span> a téléphoné.</em></p>
              <p class="example-text">→ <span class="highlight hl-subject">Qui</span> a téléphoné ?</p>
              <p class="gloss">The answer is a person doing the action → qui.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Réponse : <em>Je vois <span class="highlight hl-subject">Marie</span>.</em></p>
              <p class="example-text">→ <span class="highlight hl-subject">Qui est-ce que</span> tu vois ?</p>
              <p class="gloss">A person receiving the action → qui est-ce que.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Réponse : <em>Je lis <span class="highlight hl-verb">un livre</span>.</em></p>
              <p class="example-text">→ <span class="highlight hl-verb">Qu'est-ce que</span> tu lis ?</p>
              <p class="gloss">A thing receiving the action → qu'est-ce que.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Réponse : <em><span class="highlight hl-verb">Le bruit</span> me dérange.</em></p>
              <p class="example-text">→ <span class="highlight hl-verb">Qu'est-ce qui</span> te dérange ?</p>
              <p class="gloss">A thing doing the action → qu'est-ce qui.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="q-quique-6" data-step="En contexte">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">6</span> En contexte</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">In context — natural questions</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">L.6 — Chacun ses goûts</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Qu'est-ce que tu aimes comme musique ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">What kind of music do you like?</p>
                <p class="example-text">Qui est ton chanteur préféré ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">Who is your favourite singer?</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">L.2 — Après le bac</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Qu'est-ce qui t'intéresse le plus ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">What interests you most?</p>
                <h3 style="color:var(--gold);">L.1 — La famille</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Avec qui habites-tu ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">Who do you live with?</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="q-quique-7" data-step="Pratique QCM">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">7</span> Pratique — QCM</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Find the correct question word</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="Qui">
                <p class="q-text">1. <em>Marie a gagné.</em> → _____ a gagné ?</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">Qui</button><button class="option-btn">Qu'est-ce qui</button><button class="option-btn">Qui est-ce que</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="Qu'est-ce que">
                <p class="q-text">2. <em>Je mange une pomme.</em> → _____ tu manges ?</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">Qu'est-ce qui</button><button class="option-btn">Qu'est-ce que</button><button class="option-btn">Qui est-ce que</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="Qu'est-ce qui">
                <p class="q-text">3. <em>La musique me détend.</em> → _____ te détend ?</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">Qu'est-ce que</button><button class="option-btn">Qu'est-ce qui</button><button class="option-btn">Qui</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="Qui est-ce que">
                <p class="q-text">4. <em>J'attends mon frère.</em> → _____ tu attends ?</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">Qu'est-ce que</button><button class="option-btn">Qui est-ce que</button><button class="option-btn">Qu'est-ce qui</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="De quoi">
                <p class="q-text">5. <em>Je parle de mon voyage.</em> → _____ parles-tu ?</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">De qui</button><button class="option-btn">De quoi</button><button class="option-btn">Que</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="q-quique-8" data-step="Pratique — à compléter">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">8</span> Pratique — à compléter</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Trouvez le mot interrogatif</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">1. <em>Mon père a préparé le dîner.</em> → _____ a préparé le dîner ?</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="qui" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">2. <em>Elle regarde un film.</em> → _____ elle regarde ?</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="qu'est-ce qu'" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">3. <em>Le vent m'empêche de dormir.</em> → _____ t'empêche de dormir ?</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="qu'est-ce qui" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">4. <em>Je pense à mes examens.</em> → À _____ penses-tu ?</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="quoi" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">5. <em>Je sors avec mes amis.</em> → Avec _____ sors-tu ?</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="qui" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="accent-bar">
                <span class="ab-label">Accents :</span>
                <button class="accent-key">é</button><button class="accent-key">è</button><button class="accent-key">ê</button>
                <button class="accent-key">à</button><button class="accent-key">ç</button><button class="accent-key">ù</button>
                <button class="accent-key">û</button><button class="accent-key">î</button><button class="accent-key">ô</button>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn fib-check student-only">✓ Vérifier</button>
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </section>
      <!-- ================= 7.4 OÙ / QUAND / COMMENT / POURQUOI ================= -->
      <section data-topic="question" data-topic-name="Trouvez la Question" data-sub="Où · Quand · Comment · Pourquoi">

        <section data-slide-id="q-adv-1" data-step="Description">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">1</span> Description</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Les adverbes interrogatifs</h2>
            <p class="editable-field">These four ask about <strong>circumstances</strong>. In « Trouvez la question », the underlined part of the answer tells you which one to use.</p>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <table class="subj-table">
                <tr><th>Mot</th><th>Demande</th><th>La réponse contient…</th></tr>
                <tr><td class="key-form">Où ?</td><td class="gloss">where</td><td>un lieu — à Paris, chez moi, au marché</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="key-form">Quand ?</td><td class="gloss">when</td><td>un temps — demain, à huit heures, en été</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="key-form">Comment ?</td><td class="gloss">how</td><td>une manière — en bus, bien, lentement</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="key-form">Pourquoi ?</td><td class="gloss">why</td><td>une cause — parce que…, pour…</td></tr>
              </table>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">🔑 <strong>Method for the exam:</strong> look at what is <u>underlined</u> in the answer.
              A place → <em>où</em> · a time → <em>quand</em> · a manner → <em>comment</em> · a reason (<em>parce que</em>) → <em>pourquoi</em>.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="q-adv-2" data-step="Formation">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">2</span> Formation</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">La formule — deux constructions possibles</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Avec est-ce que</h3>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-subject">Où</span> <span class="highlight hl-aux">est-ce que</span> tu habites ?</p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-subject">Quand</span> <span class="highlight hl-aux">est-ce qu'</span>il part ?</p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-subject">Pourquoi</span> <span class="highlight hl-aux">est-ce que</span> tu pleures ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">Word order stays normal.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Avec l'inversion</h3>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-subject">Où</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">habites-tu</span> ?</p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-subject">Quand</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">part-il</span> ?</p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-subject">Pourquoi</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">pleures-tu</span> ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">More formal — both are correct.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field"><strong>Composés avec « où »:</strong>
                <em>D'où viens-tu ?</em> <span class="gloss">Where do you come from?</span> ·
                <em>Par où passes-tu ?</em> <span class="gloss">Which way do you go?</span> ·
                <em>Jusqu'où vas-tu ?</em> <span class="gloss">How far are you going?</span></p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="q-adv-3" data-step="Exceptions">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">3</span> Exceptions</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Les exceptions — pourquoi et la réponse attendue</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">POURQUOI → PARCE QUE</h3>
                <p class="example-text">— <span class="highlight hl-subject">Pourquoi</span> es-tu en retard ?</p>
                <p class="example-text">— <span class="highlight hl-verb">Parce que</span> le bus était en retard.</p>
                <p class="gloss">Why are you late? — Because the bus was late.</p>
                <p class="gloss">⚠️ Two words: <em>parce que</em>. Never <em>« par ce que »</em>.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">COMMENT — plusieurs sens</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Comment vas-tu ? <span class="gloss">How are you?</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Comment y vas-tu ? <span class="gloss">How do you get there? — by what means</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Comment est ta sœur ? <span class="gloss">What is your sister like? — description</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Comment t'appelles-tu ? <span class="gloss">What's your name?</span></p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field"><strong>« Quand » vs « à quelle heure »:</strong>
                <em>Quand pars-tu ?</em> <span class="gloss">a day or period — demain, lundi</span> ·
                <em>À quelle heure pars-tu ?</em> <span class="gloss">a clock time — à huit heures</span><br>
                If the answer contains a clock time, prefer <strong>à quelle heure</strong>.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="q-adv-4" data-step="Pièges">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">4</span> Pièges</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">⚠️ Trap Alert — choosing the wrong question word</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box red content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--crimson);">✗ Ne correspond pas</h3>
                <p class="example-text"><em>Je vais à Paris.</em> → <span class="highlight hl-neg">Quand</span> vas-tu ?</p>
                <p class="example-text"><em>Il vient en bus.</em> → <span class="highlight hl-neg">Où</span> vient-il ?</p>
                <p class="example-text"><em>Parce que je suis malade.</em> → <span class="highlight hl-neg">Comment</span> …?</p>
                <p class="example-text"><em>Elle habite à Lyon.</em> → <span class="highlight hl-neg">Où est-ce que habite-t-elle</span> ?</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box green content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--green);">✓ Correspond</h3>
                <p class="example-text">→ <span class="highlight hl-verb">Où</span> vas-tu ? <span class="gloss">place</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">→ <span class="highlight hl-verb">Comment</span> vient-il ? <span class="gloss">manner</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">→ <span class="highlight hl-verb">Pourquoi</span> …? <span class="gloss">reason</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">→ <span class="highlight hl-verb">Où est-ce qu'elle habite</span> ? <span class="gloss">one method only</span></p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">💡 <strong>Check your work:</strong> read your question, then read the given answer.
              If the answer would actually answer your question, it is right. This one-second check catches nearly every error.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="q-adv-5" data-step="Exemples">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">5</span> Exemples travaillés</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Worked examples</h2>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <p class="example-text"><span class="q-tag">CBSE 2019</span>Réponse : <em>Miriam arrive <u>demain</u>.</em></p>
              <p class="example-text">→ <span class="highlight hl-subject">Quand</span> est-ce que Miriam arrive ?</p>
              <p class="gloss">The underlined part is a time → quand.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Réponse : <em>Je vais à l'école <u>en bus</u>.</em></p>
              <p class="example-text">→ <span class="highlight hl-subject">Comment</span> est-ce que tu vas à l'école ?</p>
              <p class="gloss">A means of transport → comment.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Réponse : <em>Elle est absente <u>parce qu'elle est malade</u>.</em></p>
              <p class="example-text">→ <span class="highlight hl-subject">Pourquoi</span> est-elle absente ?</p>
              <p class="gloss">A cause → pourquoi.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Réponse : <em>Nous dînons <u>à huit heures</u>.</em></p>
              <p class="example-text">→ <span class="highlight hl-subject">À quelle heure</span> dînez-vous ?</p>
              <p class="gloss">A clock time → à quelle heure.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="q-adv-6" data-step="En contexte">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">6</span> En contexte</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">In context — an interview</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">L.3 — Chercher du travail</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Où avez-vous travaillé auparavant ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">Where have you worked before?</p>
                <p class="example-text">Pourquoi voulez-vous changer d'emploi ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">Why do you want to change jobs?</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">L.5 — Les voyages</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Quand partez-vous en vacances ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">When are you going on holiday?</p>
                <p class="example-text">Comment voyagez-vous — en train ou en avion ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">How do you travel — by train or by plane?</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="q-adv-7" data-step="Pratique QCM">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">7</span> Pratique — QCM</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Choose the right question word</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="Où">
                <p class="q-text">1. <em>Il habite <u>à Delhi</u>.</em> → _____ habite-t-il ?</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">Quand</button><button class="option-btn">Où</button><button class="option-btn">Comment</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="Quand">
                <p class="q-text">2. <em>Nous partons <u>lundi</u>.</em> → _____ partez-vous ?</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">Quand</button><button class="option-btn">Où</button><button class="option-btn">Pourquoi</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="Comment">
                <p class="q-text">3. <em>Je viens <u>à pied</u>.</em> → _____ viens-tu ?</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">Où</button><button class="option-btn">Comment</button><button class="option-btn">Quand</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="Pourquoi">
                <p class="q-text">4. <em>Je suis fatigué <u>parce que j'ai mal dormi</u>.</em> → _____ es-tu fatigué ?</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">Comment</button><button class="option-btn">Pourquoi</button><button class="option-btn">Quand</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="À quelle heure">
                <p class="q-text">5. <em>Le train part <u>à 7 h 30</u>.</em> → _____ part le train ?</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">Quand</button><button class="option-btn">À quelle heure</button><button class="option-btn">Comment</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="q-adv-8" data-step="Pratique — à compléter">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">8</span> Pratique — à compléter</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Trouvez la question</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">1. <em>Je vais <u>au marché</u>.</em> → _____ est-ce que tu vas ?</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="où" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">2. <em>Elle arrive <u>ce soir</u>.</em> → _____ est-ce qu'elle arrive ?</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="quand" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">3. <em>Il va bien.</em> → _____ va-t-il ?</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="comment" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">4. <em>Je pleure <u>parce que je suis triste</u>.</em> → _____ pleures-tu ?</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="pourquoi" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">5. <em>Je viens <u>de Mumbai</u>.</em> → _____ viens-tu ?</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="d'où" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="accent-bar">
                <span class="ab-label">Accents :</span>
                <button class="accent-key">é</button><button class="accent-key">è</button><button class="accent-key">ê</button>
                <button class="accent-key">à</button><button class="accent-key">ç</button><button class="accent-key">ù</button>
                <button class="accent-key">û</button><button class="accent-key">î</button><button class="accent-key">ô</button>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn fib-check student-only">✓ Vérifier</button>
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </section>

      <!-- ================= 7.5 QUEL(LE)(S) ================= -->
      <section data-topic="question" data-topic-name="Trouvez la Question" data-sub="QUEL(LE)(S)">

        <section data-slide-id="q-quel-1" data-step="Description">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">1</span> Description</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">QUEL — the interrogative adjective</h2>
            <p class="editable-field"><em>Quel</em> is an <strong>adjective</strong>: it always accompanies a noun and <strong>agrees</strong> with it. English "which" or "what".</p>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <table class="subj-table">
                <tr><th></th><th>Masculin</th><th>Féminin</th></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Singulier</strong></td><td class="key-form">quel</td><td class="key-form">quelle</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Pluriel</strong></td><td class="key-form">quels</td><td class="key-form">quelles</td></tr>
              </table>
              <p class="gloss" style="margin-top:8px;">All four are pronounced the same — only the spelling changes, and only the spelling is marked.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-subject">Quel</span> âge as-tu ? <span class="gloss">How old are you? — âge is masculine</span></p>
              <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-subject">Quelle</span> heure est-il ? <span class="gloss">What time is it? — heure is feminine</span></p>
              <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-subject">Quels</span> livres préfères-tu ? <span class="gloss">Which books do you prefer?</span></p>
              <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-subject">Quelles</span> matières étudies-tu ? <span class="gloss">Which subjects do you study?</span></p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="q-quel-2" data-step="Formation">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">2</span> Formation</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">La formule — deux constructions</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">① Quel + nom</h3>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-subject">Quel film</span> as-tu vu ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">Which film did you see?</p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-subject">Quelle robe</span> préfères-tu ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">Which dress do you prefer?</p>
                <p class="gloss">The noun follows immediately.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">② Quel + être + nom</h3>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-subject">Quel est</span> ton nom ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">What is your name?</p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-subject">Quelle est</span> ta matière préférée ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">What is your favourite subject?</p>
                <p class="gloss">Agreement is with the noun that follows <em>être</em>.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field"><strong>Avec une préposition:</strong>
                <em>À <span class="highlight hl-subject">quelle</span> heure pars-tu ?</em> ·
                <em>Dans <span class="highlight hl-subject">quel</span> pays habites-tu ?</em> ·
                <em>De <span class="highlight hl-subject">quelle</span> couleur est ta voiture ?</em></p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="q-quel-3" data-step="Exceptions">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">3</span> Exceptions</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">QUEL vs LEQUEL vs QU'EST-CE QUE</h2>
            <div class="three-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">QUEL + nom</h3>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-subject">Quel</span> livre veux-tu ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">Which book do you want? — a noun follows</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">LEQUEL — sans nom</h3>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-pronoun">Lequel</span> veux-tu ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">Which one do you want? — replaces the noun</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box green content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--green);">QU'EST-CE QUE</h3>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-verb">Qu'est-ce que</span> tu veux ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">What do you want? — no noun at all</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field"><strong>Exclamations aussi:</strong> <em>quel</em> is also used to exclaim —
                <em><span class="highlight hl-subject">Quelle</span> belle journée !</em> <span class="gloss">What a beautiful day!</span> ·
                <em><span class="highlight hl-subject">Quel</span> dommage !</em> <span class="gloss">What a pity!</span>
                Note there is no article: never <em>« quel une belle journée »</em>.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="q-quel-4" data-step="Pièges">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">4</span> Pièges</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">⚠️ Trap Alert — the agreement is invisible when spoken</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box red content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--crimson);">✗ Wrong</h3>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-neg">Quel</span> heure est-il ?</p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-neg">Quelle</span> âge as-tu ?</p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-neg">Quel</span> matières étudies-tu ?</p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-neg">Qu'est-ce que</span> âge as-tu ?</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box green content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--green);">✓ Right</h3>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-verb">Quelle</span> heure est-il ? <span class="gloss">une heure — fem.</span></p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-verb">Quel</span> âge as-tu ? <span class="gloss">un âge — masc.</span></p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-verb">Quelles</span> matières étudies-tu ? <span class="gloss">fem. plural</span></p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-verb">Quel</span> âge as-tu ? <span class="gloss">a noun follows → quel</span></p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">🔑 <strong>Always find the noun first</strong>, then decide the gender and number, then write <em>quel / quelle / quels / quelles</em>.
              The four forms sound identical, so only careful writing earns the mark.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="q-quel-5" data-step="Exemples">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">5</span> Exemples travaillés</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Worked examples</h2>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <p class="example-text">Réponse : <em>J'ai <u>quinze ans</u>.</em> → <span class="highlight hl-subject">Quel</span> âge as-tu ?</p>
              <p class="gloss">How old are you? — <em>âge</em> masculine singular</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Réponse : <em>Ma matière préférée est <u>le français</u>.</em> → <span class="highlight hl-subject">Quelle</span> est ta matière préférée ?</p>
              <p class="gloss"><em>matière</em> feminine singular</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Réponse : <em>J'aime <u>les films d'action</u>.</em> → <span class="highlight hl-subject">Quels</span> films aimes-tu ?</p>
              <p class="gloss"><em>films</em> masculine plural</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Réponse : <em>Je pars <u>à six heures</u>.</em> → À <span class="highlight hl-subject">quelle</span> heure pars-tu ?</p>
              <p class="gloss">Preposition + quelle + heure</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="q-quel-6" data-step="En contexte">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">6</span> En contexte</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">In context — filling in a form</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Questions personnelles</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Quel est ton nom ? / Quelle est ton adresse ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">What is your name? / What is your address?</p>
                <p class="example-text">Quelle est ta nationalité ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">What is your nationality?</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">L.2 — Après le bac</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Quelles études veux-tu faire ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">What studies do you want to do?</p>
                <h3 style="color:var(--gold);">L.6 — Chacun ses goûts</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Quel genre de musique préfères-tu ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">What kind of music do you prefer?</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="q-quel-7" data-step="Pratique QCM">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">7</span> Pratique — QCM</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Choose the correct form of « quel »</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="Quelle">
                <p class="q-text">1. _____ heure est-il ?</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">Quel</button><button class="option-btn">Quelle</button><button class="option-btn">Quels</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="Quel">
                <p class="q-text">2. _____ âge as-tu ?</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">Quel</button><button class="option-btn">Quelle</button><button class="option-btn">Quels</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="Quelles">
                <p class="q-text">3. _____ langues parles-tu ?</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">Quels</button><button class="option-btn">Quelles</button><button class="option-btn">Quelle</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="Quel est">
                <p class="q-text">4. _____ ton sport préféré ?</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">Quel est</button><button class="option-btn">Quelle est</button><button class="option-btn">Qu'est-ce que</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="Lequel">
                <p class="q-text">5. Voici deux livres. _____ préfères-tu ? <span class="gloss">(sans nom)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">Quel</button><button class="option-btn">Lequel</button><button class="option-btn">Qu'est-ce que</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="q-quel-8" data-step="Pratique — à compléter">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">8</span> Pratique — à compléter</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Complétez avec quel / quelle / quels / quelles</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">1. _____ est ton adresse ?</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="quelle" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">2. _____ films as-tu vus cette année ?</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="quels" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">3. Dans _____ ville habites-tu ?</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="quelle" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">4. _____ sont tes projets pour l'été ?</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="quels" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">5. _____ jour sommes-nous ?</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="quel" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="accent-bar">
                <span class="ab-label">Accents :</span>
                <button class="accent-key">é</button><button class="accent-key">è</button><button class="accent-key">ê</button>
                <button class="accent-key">à</button><button class="accent-key">ç</button><button class="accent-key">ù</button>
                <button class="accent-key">û</button><button class="accent-key">î</button><button class="accent-key">ô</button>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn fib-check student-only">✓ Vérifier</button>
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </section>

      <!-- ================= 7.6 COMBIEN ================= -->
      <section data-topic="question" data-topic-name="Trouvez la Question" data-sub="COMBIEN">

        <section data-slide-id="q-comb-1" data-step="Description">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">1</span> Description</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">COMBIEN — asking about quantity</h2>
            <p class="editable-field">Use <em>combien</em> when the answer contains a <strong>number, a price or an amount</strong>.</p>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">COMBIEN DE + nom</h3>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-subject">Combien de</span> frères as-tu ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">How many brothers do you have? — J'ai deux frères.</p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-subject">Combien d'</span>élèves y a-t-il ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">How many pupils are there?</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">COMBIEN seul</h3>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-subject">Combien</span> coûte ce livre ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">How much does this book cost?</p>
                <p class="example-text">Ça fait <span class="highlight hl-subject">combien</span> ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">How much is it?</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">⚠️ <strong>Toujours « de », jamais « du / des »:</strong>
                ✓ <em>combien <span class="highlight hl-verb">de</span> livres</em> ·
                ✗ <em>combien <span class="highlight hl-neg">des</span> livres</em>. Before a vowel: <em>combien <span class="highlight hl-verb">d'</span>amis</em>.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="q-comb-2" data-step="Formation">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">2</span> Formation</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">La formule</h2>
            <div class="formula-pipeline">
              <div class="f-box" style="border-color:var(--gold);"><span class="f-label">Combien de</span><span class="f-value" style="color:var(--gold);">Combien de</span></div>
              <div class="f-op">+</div>
              <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Nom</span><span class="f-value">frères</span></div>
              <div class="f-op">+</div>
              <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Verbe + sujet</span><span class="f-value">as-tu ?</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Avec est-ce que</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Combien de livres <span class="highlight hl-aux">est-ce que</span> tu as ?</p>
                <p class="example-text">Combien <span class="highlight hl-aux">est-ce que</span> ça coûte ?</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Avec l'inversion</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Combien de livres <span class="highlight hl-verb">as-tu</span> ?</p>
                <p class="example-text">Combien <span class="highlight hl-verb">coûte-t-il</span> ?</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field"><strong>Expressions de temps courantes:</strong>
                <em>Combien de temps ?</em> <span class="gloss">How long?</span> ·
                <em>Depuis combien de temps ?</em> <span class="gloss">For how long?</span> ·
                <em>Combien de fois ?</em> <span class="gloss">How many times?</span></p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="q-comb-3" data-step="Exceptions">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">3</span> Exceptions</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Les exceptions — combien vs quel</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Un nombre → COMBIEN</h3>
                <p class="example-text">— <span class="highlight hl-subject">Combien de</span> frères as-tu ?<br>— J'ai <strong>trois</strong> frères.</p>
                <p class="gloss">A countable quantity.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Un âge → QUEL</h3>
                <p class="example-text">— <span class="highlight hl-subject">Quel</span> âge as-tu ?<br>— J'ai <strong>quinze ans</strong>.</p>
                <p class="gloss">Although the answer is a number, French asks <em>quel âge</em>, never <em>combien d'ans</em>.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Same for time: <em><span class="highlight hl-subject">Quelle</span> heure est-il ?</em></p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field"><strong>Le prix — deux formulations:</strong>
                <em><span class="highlight hl-subject">Combien</span> coûte ce livre ?</em> ·
                <em><span class="highlight hl-subject">Quel</span> est le prix de ce livre ?</em> — both correct.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="q-comb-4" data-step="Pièges">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">4</span> Pièges</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">⚠️ Trap Alert — « de » and the age exception</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box red content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--crimson);">✗ Wrong</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Combien <span class="highlight hl-neg">des</span> livres as-tu ?</p>
                <p class="example-text">Combien <span class="highlight hl-neg">d'ans</span> as-tu ?</p>
                <p class="example-text">Combien <span class="highlight hl-neg">de</span> coûte ce stylo ?</p>
                <p class="example-text">Combien <span class="highlight hl-neg">du</span> temps ?</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box green content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--green);">✓ Right</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Combien <span class="highlight hl-verb">de</span> livres as-tu ?</p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-verb">Quel âge</span> as-tu ? <span class="gloss">fixed expression</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Combien coûte ce stylo ? <span class="gloss">no <em>de</em> before a verb</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Combien <span class="highlight hl-verb">de</span> temps ?</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">🔑 <strong>Simple rule:</strong> <em>combien</em> + <strong>de</strong> only when a <strong>noun</strong> follows.
              If a verb follows, use <em>combien</em> alone.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="q-comb-5" data-step="Exemples">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">5</span> Exemples travaillés</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Worked examples</h2>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <p class="example-text">Réponse : <em>J'ai <u>deux sœurs</u>.</em> → <span class="highlight hl-subject">Combien de</span> sœurs as-tu ?</p>
              <p class="gloss">How many sisters do you have?</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Réponse : <em>Ce livre coûte <u>15 euros</u>.</em> → <span class="highlight hl-subject">Combien</span> coûte ce livre ?</p>
              <p class="gloss">How much does this book cost? — a verb follows, so no <em>de</em></p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Réponse : <em>J'étudie le français <u>depuis trois ans</u>.</em> → <span class="highlight hl-subject">Depuis combien de temps</span> étudies-tu le français ?</p>
              <p class="gloss">How long have you been studying French?</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Réponse : <em>Il y a <u>trente élèves</u> dans ma classe.</em> → <span class="highlight hl-subject">Combien d'</span>élèves y a-t-il dans ta classe ?</p>
              <p class="gloss">How many pupils are there in your class? — <em>d'</em> before a vowel</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="q-comb-6" data-step="En contexte">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">6</span> En contexte</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">In context — shopping and daily life</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">L.8 — Faire des achats</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Combien coûtent ces chaussures ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">How much do these shoes cost?</p>
                <p class="example-text">Combien de kilos voulez-vous ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">How many kilos would you like?</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">L.7 — En pleine forme</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Combien d'heures dors-tu par nuit ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">How many hours do you sleep a night?</p>
                <h3 style="color:var(--gold);">L.1 — La famille</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Combien de personnes y a-t-il dans ta famille ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">How many people are there in your family?</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="q-comb-7" data-step="Pratique QCM">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">7</span> Pratique — QCM</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Choose the correct question</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="Combien de">
                <p class="q-text">1. <em>J'ai trois chats.</em> → _____ chats as-tu ?</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">Combien de</button><button class="option-btn">Combien des</button><button class="option-btn">Quel</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="Combien">
                <p class="q-text">2. <em>Ça coûte 20 euros.</em> → _____ ça coûte ?</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">Combien de</button><button class="option-btn">Combien</button><button class="option-btn">Quelle</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="Quel âge">
                <p class="q-text">3. <em>J'ai seize ans.</em> → _____ as-tu ?</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">Combien d'ans</button><button class="option-btn">Quel âge</button><button class="option-btn">Combien d'âge</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="Combien d'">
                <p class="q-text">4. <em>Il y a vingt élèves.</em> → _____ élèves y a-t-il ?</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">Combien de</button><button class="option-btn">Combien d'</button><button class="option-btn">Combien des</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="Depuis combien de temps">
                <p class="q-text">5. <em>J'habite ici depuis cinq ans.</em> → _____ habites-tu ici ?</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">Depuis combien de temps</button><button class="option-btn">Combien de temps depuis</button><button class="option-btn">Quel temps</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="q-comb-8" data-step="Pratique — à compléter">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">8</span> Pratique — à compléter</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Trouvez la question</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">1. <em>J'ai deux frères.</em> → _____ frères as-tu ?</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="combien de" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">2. <em>Le billet coûte 50 roupies.</em> → _____ coûte le billet ?</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="combien" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">3. <em>J'ai quatorze ans.</em> → _____ as-tu ?</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="quel âge" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">4. <em>Je bois deux litres d'eau.</em> → _____ eau bois-tu ?</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="combien d'" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">5. <em>Le film dure deux heures.</em> → _____ dure le film ?</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="combien de temps" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="accent-bar">
                <span class="ab-label">Accents :</span>
                <button class="accent-key">é</button><button class="accent-key">è</button><button class="accent-key">ê</button>
                <button class="accent-key">à</button><button class="accent-key">ç</button><button class="accent-key">ù</button>
                <button class="accent-key">û</button><button class="accent-key">î</button><button class="accent-key">ô</button>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn fib-check student-only">✓ Vérifier</button>
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </section>

      <!-- ================= TOPIC 7 CLOSER ================= -->
      <section data-topic="question" data-topic-name="Trouvez la Question" data-sub="Synthèse &amp; Examen">

        <section data-slide-id="q-fin-1" data-step="Tableau de référence">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">📊 Tableau — la réponse vous donne la question</h2>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <table class="subj-table">
                <tr><th>Si la réponse contient…</th><th>Posez la question avec…</th><th>Exemple</th></tr>
                <tr><td>oui / non</td><td class="key-form">Est-ce que…?</td><td>Est-ce que tu viens ?</td></tr>
                <tr><td>une personne (sujet)</td><td class="key-form">Qui…?</td><td>Qui a téléphoné ?</td></tr>
                <tr><td>une personne (objet)</td><td class="key-form">Qui est-ce que…?</td><td>Qui est-ce que tu vois ?</td></tr>
                <tr><td>une chose (objet)</td><td class="key-form">Qu'est-ce que…?</td><td>Qu'est-ce que tu fais ?</td></tr>
                <tr><td>une chose (sujet)</td><td class="key-form">Qu'est-ce qui…?</td><td>Qu'est-ce qui se passe ?</td></tr>
                <tr><td>un lieu</td><td class="key-form">Où…?</td><td>Où habites-tu ?</td></tr>
                <tr><td>un moment</td><td class="key-form">Quand…?</td><td>Quand pars-tu ?</td></tr>
                <tr><td>une heure précise</td><td class="key-form">À quelle heure…?</td><td>À quelle heure pars-tu ?</td></tr>
                <tr><td>une manière</td><td class="key-form">Comment…?</td><td>Comment viens-tu ?</td></tr>
                <tr><td>une cause (parce que)</td><td class="key-form">Pourquoi…?</td><td>Pourquoi pleures-tu ?</td></tr>
                <tr><td>un nombre / un prix</td><td class="key-form">Combien (de)…?</td><td>Combien de frères as-tu ?</td></tr>
                <tr><td>un choix + nom</td><td class="key-form">Quel(le)(s)…?</td><td>Quel film as-tu vu ?</td></tr>
              </table>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="q-fin-2" data-step="Examen CBSE">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">📝 Examen blanc — Trouvez la question</h2>
            <p class="editable-field gloss">Écrivez la question qui correspond à la partie soulignée.</p>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text"><span class="q-tag">CBSE 2019</span>1. <em>Miriam arrive <u>demain</u>.</em> → _____ est-ce que Miriam arrive ?</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="quand" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text"><span class="q-tag">CBSE 2019</span>2. <em>Les magasins sont <u>fermés</u>.</em> → _____ sont les magasins ?</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="comment" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">3. <em><u>Mon père</u> a préparé le repas.</em> → _____ a préparé le repas ?</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="qui" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">4. <em>Elle habite <u>à Chennai</u>.</em> → _____ est-ce qu'elle habite ?</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="où" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">5. <em>J'ai <u>trois</u> cousins.</em> → _____ cousins as-tu ?</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="combien de" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">6. <em>Je lis <u>un roman policier</u>.</em> → _____ tu lis ?</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="qu'est-ce que" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="accent-bar">
                <span class="ab-label">Accents :</span>
                <button class="accent-key">é</button><button class="accent-key">è</button><button class="accent-key">ê</button>
                <button class="accent-key">à</button><button class="accent-key">ç</button><button class="accent-key">ù</button>
                <button class="accent-key">û</button><button class="accent-key">î</button><button class="accent-key">ô</button>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn fib-check student-only">✓ Vérifier</button>
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 6</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="q-fin-3" data-step="Check-list">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">✅ Check-list — Trouvez la Question</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <p>☐ What exactly is <strong>underlined</strong> in the answer? That is what the question must ask about.</p>
                <p>☐ Person or thing? Subject or object? → qui / qu'est-ce qui / qu'est-ce que</p>
                <p>☐ Does a <strong>noun</strong> follow? → quel(le)(s), and check the agreement.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <p>☐ Did I use <strong>one</strong> method — est-ce que <em>or</em> inversion, never both?</p>
                <p>☐ Inversion: is the <strong>hyphen</strong> there, and is <strong>-t-</strong> needed?</p>
                <p>☐ Did I finish with a <strong>question mark</strong>?</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">🎯 <strong>Exam note:</strong> « Trouvez la question » is 5 marks. The safest strategy is
              <strong>est-ce que</strong> plus the correct question word — it avoids every inversion trap and is always accepted.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </section>
      <!-- ==================================================================
           TOPIC 8 — LES POSSESSIFS
           =================================================================== -->
      <section data-topic="possessifs" data-topic-name="Les Possessifs" data-sub="Adjectifs Possessifs">

        <section data-slide-id="poss-adj-1" data-step="Description">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">1</span> Description</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Les Adjectifs Possessifs — mon, ma, mes…</h2>
            <p class="editable-field">A possessive adjective shows <strong>who owns</strong> something. In French it agrees with the <strong>thing owned</strong> — not with the owner.</p>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <table class="subj-table">
                <tr><th>Possesseur</th><th>Masc. sing.</th><th>Fém. sing.</th><th>Pluriel</th></tr>
                <tr><td>je</td><td class="key-form">mon</td><td class="key-form">ma</td><td class="key-form">mes</td></tr>
                <tr><td>tu</td><td class="key-form">ton</td><td class="key-form">ta</td><td class="key-form">tes</td></tr>
                <tr><td>il / elle</td><td class="key-form">son</td><td class="key-form">sa</td><td class="key-form">ses</td></tr>
                <tr><td>nous</td><td class="key-form">notre</td><td class="key-form">notre</td><td class="key-form">nos</td></tr>
                <tr><td>vous</td><td class="key-form">votre</td><td class="key-form">votre</td><td class="key-form">vos</td></tr>
                <tr><td>ils / elles</td><td class="key-form">leur</td><td class="key-form">leur</td><td class="key-form">leurs</td></tr>
              </table>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">🔑 <strong>The big difference from English:</strong> <em>son livre</em> can mean "his book" <strong>or</strong> "her book".
              What decides <em>son / sa</em> is the gender of <strong>livre</strong>, not of the owner.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="poss-adj-2" data-step="Formation">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">2</span> Formation</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">La formule — accord avec l'objet possédé</h2>
            <div class="formula-pipeline">
              <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Possesseur</span><span class="f-value">je</span></div>
              <div class="f-op">+</div>
              <div class="f-box" style="border-color:var(--purple);"><span class="f-label">Genre / nombre du NOM</span><span class="f-value" style="color:var(--purple);">livre (m.)</span></div>
              <div class="f-op">=</div>
              <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Adjectif</span><span class="f-value">mon livre</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Le même possesseur, trois formes</h3>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-pronoun">mon</span> frère <span class="gloss">my brother — masc.</span></p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-pronoun">ma</span> sœur <span class="gloss">my sister — fem.</span></p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-pronoun">mes</span> parents <span class="gloss">my parents — plural</span></p>
                <p class="gloss">The owner never changes — only the noun does.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Nous / vous / ils — plus simple</h3>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-pronoun">notre</span> maison · <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">notre</span> jardin</p>
                <p class="gloss">One form for both genders in the singular.</p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-pronoun">nos</span> amis · <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">vos</span> livres · <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">leurs</span> enfants</p>
                <p class="gloss">One plural form each.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="poss-adj-3" data-step="Exceptions">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">3</span> Exceptions</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">L'exception majeure — MON devant une voyelle</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Nom féminin commençant par une voyelle</h3>
                <p>French avoids <em>ma amie</em> because two vowels clash. It uses the masculine form instead:</p>
                <p class="example-text">✗ <em>ma amie</em> → ✓ <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">mon</span> amie</p>
                <p class="example-text">✗ <em>ta école</em> → ✓ <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">ton</span> école</p>
                <p class="example-text">✗ <em>sa histoire</em> → ✓ <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">son</span> histoire</p>
                <p class="gloss">The noun is still feminine — only the possessive changes shape.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">LEUR / LEURS — attention au -s</h3>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-pronoun">leur</span> maison <span class="gloss">their house — one house</span></p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-pronoun">leurs</span> maisons <span class="gloss">their houses — several</span></p>
                <p class="gloss">The -s depends on the number of <strong>objects</strong>, not owners.</p>
                <p class="gloss">⚠️ Don't confuse with the pronoun <em>leur</em> (to them), which never takes -s.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="poss-adj-4" data-step="Pièges">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">4</span> Pièges</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">⚠️ Trap Alert — thinking in English</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box red content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--crimson);">✗ Wrong</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Marie et <span class="highlight hl-neg">sa</span> frère.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Paul et <span class="highlight hl-neg">sa</span> livre.</p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-neg">Ma</span> amie s'appelle Léa.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Ils ont vendu <span class="highlight hl-neg">leur</span> voitures.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box green content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--green);">✓ Right</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Marie et <span class="highlight hl-verb">son</span> frère. <span class="gloss">frère is masculine</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Paul et <span class="highlight hl-verb">son</span> livre. <span class="gloss">livre is masculine</span></p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-verb">Mon</span> amie s'appelle Léa. <span class="gloss">vowel rule</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Ils ont vendu <span class="highlight hl-verb">leurs</span> voitures. <span class="gloss">several cars</span></p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">🔑 <strong>Never ask "is the owner male or female?"</strong> — that is the English habit and it is always wrong here.
              Ask instead: <em>is the <strong>noun</strong> masculine, feminine or plural?</em></p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="poss-adj-5" data-step="Exemples">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">5</span> Exemples travaillés</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Worked examples</h2>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-pronoun">Ma</span> sœur habite avec <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">ses</span> amis.</p>
              <p class="gloss">My sister lives with her friends. — sœur fem. sing., amis plural</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Paul a oublié <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">son</span> cahier et <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">sa</span> trousse.</p>
              <p class="gloss">Paul forgot his exercise book and his pencil case. — cahier m., trousse f.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-pronoun">Mon</span> école est près de <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">notre</span> maison.</p>
              <p class="gloss">My school is near our house. — école is feminine but starts with a vowel</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Les élèves ont apporté <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">leurs</span> livres et <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">leur</span> professeur est content.</p>
              <p class="gloss">The pupils brought their books and their teacher is happy. — many books, one teacher</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="poss-adj-6" data-step="En contexte">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">6</span> En contexte</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">In context — talking about family and school</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">L.1 — La famille</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Mon père est ingénieur et ma mère est professeur.</p>
                <p class="gloss">My father is an engineer and my mother is a teacher.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Mes grands-parents habitent avec nous.</p>
                <p class="gloss">My grandparents live with us.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">L.2 — Au lycée / Après le bac</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Notre classe a trente élèves et notre professeur est très gentil.</p>
                <p class="gloss">Our class has thirty pupils and our teacher is very kind.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Quelles sont vos matières préférées ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">What are your favourite subjects?</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">💡 <strong>Letter tip:</strong> informal letters are full of possessives —
              <em>Comment vont <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">tes</span> parents ? <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">Ma</span> famille va bien.</em>
              Get the agreement right and the whole letter reads better.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="poss-adj-7" data-step="Pratique QCM">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">7</span> Pratique — QCM</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Choose the correct possessive adjective</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="son">
                <p class="q-text">1. Marie parle avec _____ frère. <span class="gloss">(le frère de Marie)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">sa</button><button class="option-btn">son</button><button class="option-btn">ses</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="mon">
                <p class="q-text">2. _____ amie s'appelle Sonia.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">ma</button><button class="option-btn">mon</button><button class="option-btn">mes</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="leurs">
                <p class="q-text">3. Les enfants ont rangé _____ jouets.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">leur</button><button class="option-btn">leurs</button><button class="option-btn">ses</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="notre">
                <p class="q-text">4. Nous aimons _____ maison.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">nos</button><button class="option-btn">notre</button><button class="option-btn">nôtre</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="ta">
                <p class="q-text">5. <span class="q-tag">CBSE 2024</span>Peux-tu me prêter _____ trousse ?</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">ton</button><button class="option-btn">ta</button><button class="option-btn">tes</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="poss-adj-8" data-step="Pratique — à compléter">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">8</span> Pratique — à compléter</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Complétez avec l'adjectif possessif</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">1. J'aime beaucoup _____ nouvelle école. <span class="gloss">(je)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="ma" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">2. Il a perdu _____ clés. <span class="gloss">(il)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="ses" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">3. Vous avez oublié _____ parapluie. <span class="gloss">(vous)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="votre" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">4. Elles adorent _____ professeur de français. <span class="gloss">(elles)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="leur" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">5. C'est _____ histoire préférée. <span class="gloss">(tu — histoire est féminin)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="ton" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="accent-bar">
                <span class="ab-label">Accents :</span>
                <button class="accent-key">é</button><button class="accent-key">è</button><button class="accent-key">ê</button>
                <button class="accent-key">à</button><button class="accent-key">ç</button><button class="accent-key">ù</button>
                <button class="accent-key">û</button><button class="accent-key">î</button><button class="accent-key">ô</button>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn fib-check student-only">✓ Vérifier</button>
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </section>

      <!-- ================= 8.2 PRONOMS POSSESSIFS ================= -->
      <section data-topic="possessifs" data-topic-name="Les Possessifs" data-sub="Pronoms Possessifs">

        <section data-slide-id="poss-pro-1" data-step="Description">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">1</span> Description</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Les Pronoms Possessifs — le mien, le tien…</h2>
            <p class="editable-field">A possessive <strong>pronoun</strong> replaces the noun entirely: "mine", "yours", "his". It always carries an <strong>article</strong>.</p>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <p class="example-text">C'est <span class="highlight hl-aux">mon</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">livre</span>. → C'est <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">le mien</span>.</p>
              <p class="gloss">It's my book. → It's mine.</p>
              <table class="subj-table" style="margin-top:8px;">
                <tr><th>Possesseur</th><th>Masc. sing.</th><th>Fém. sing.</th><th>Masc. plur.</th><th>Fém. plur.</th></tr>
                <tr><td>je</td><td class="key-form">le mien</td><td class="key-form">la mienne</td><td>les miens</td><td>les miennes</td></tr>
                <tr><td>tu</td><td class="key-form">le tien</td><td class="key-form">la tienne</td><td>les tiens</td><td>les tiennes</td></tr>
                <tr><td>il/elle</td><td class="key-form">le sien</td><td class="key-form">la sienne</td><td>les siens</td><td>les siennes</td></tr>
                <tr><td>nous</td><td class="key-form">le nôtre</td><td class="key-form">la nôtre</td><td colspan="2">les nôtres</td></tr>
                <tr><td>vous</td><td class="key-form">le vôtre</td><td class="key-form">la vôtre</td><td colspan="2">les vôtres</td></tr>
                <tr><td>ils/elles</td><td class="key-form">le leur</td><td class="key-form">la leur</td><td colspan="2">les leurs</td></tr>
              </table>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="poss-pro-2" data-step="Formation">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">2</span> Formation</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">La formule — article + forme possessive</h2>
            <div class="formula-pipeline">
              <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Article</span><span class="f-value">le / la / les</span></div>
              <div class="f-op">+</div>
              <div class="f-box" style="border-color:var(--purple);"><span class="f-label">Forme</span><span class="f-value" style="color:var(--purple);">mien(ne)(s)</span></div>
              <div class="f-op">=</div>
              <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Pronom</span><span class="f-value">le mien</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">L'accord suit le nom remplacé</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Mon <span class="highlight hl-verb">stylo</span> → <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">le mien</span> <span class="gloss">masc. sing.</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Ma <span class="highlight hl-verb">trousse</span> → <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">la mienne</span> <span class="gloss">fem. sing.</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Mes <span class="highlight hl-verb">livres</span> → <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">les miens</span> <span class="gloss">masc. plur.</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Mes <span class="highlight hl-verb">clés</span> → <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">les miennes</span> <span class="gloss">fem. plur.</span></p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Contractions avec à et de</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Je pense <span class="highlight hl-aux">au</span> mien. <span class="gloss">à + le → au</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Je parle <span class="highlight hl-aux">du</span> tien. <span class="gloss">de + le → du</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Je m'occupe <span class="highlight hl-aux">des</span> miens. <span class="gloss">de + les → des</span></p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="poss-pro-3" data-step="Exceptions">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">3</span> Exceptions</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">L'accent circonflexe — nôtre / vôtre</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Adjectif — SANS accent</h3>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-verb">notre</span> maison</p>
                <p class="gloss">our house</p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-verb">votre</span> voiture</p>
                <p class="gloss">your car</p>
                <p class="gloss">A noun follows.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Pronom — AVEC accent</h3>
                <p class="example-text">C'est <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">la nôtre</span>.</p>
                <p class="gloss">It's ours.</p>
                <p class="example-text">C'est <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">le vôtre</span>.</p>
                <p class="gloss">It's yours.</p>
                <p class="gloss">No noun follows — and the ô is compulsory.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field"><strong>Autre façon d'exprimer la possession:</strong> <em>être à</em> + pronom tonique —
                <em>Ce livre est <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">à moi</span>.</em> <span class="gloss">This book is mine.</span>
                It means the same as <em>C'est le mien</em> but is simpler to write.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="poss-pro-4" data-step="Pièges">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">4</span> Pièges</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">⚠️ Trap Alert — adjective or pronoun?</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box red content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--crimson);">✗ Wrong</h3>
                <p class="example-text">C'est <span class="highlight hl-neg">mien</span>. <span class="gloss">missing article</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">C'est <span class="highlight hl-neg">le mon</span>. <span class="gloss">adjective used as pronoun</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">C'est <span class="highlight hl-neg">la notre</span>. <span class="gloss">missing accent</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">J'ai perdu <span class="highlight hl-neg">le mien</span> trousse. <span class="gloss">pronoun + noun</span></p>
              </div>
              <div class="box green content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--green);">✓ Right</h3>
                <p class="example-text">C'est <span class="highlight hl-verb">le mien</span>.</p>
                <p class="example-text">C'est <span class="highlight hl-verb">le mien</span>.</p>
                <p class="example-text">C'est <span class="highlight hl-verb">la nôtre</span>.</p>
                <p class="example-text">J'ai perdu <span class="highlight hl-verb">ma</span> trousse. <span class="gloss">adjective + noun</span></p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">🔑 <strong>One-second test:</strong> is there a <strong>noun</strong> straight after?
              Yes → adjective (<em>mon, ma, mes</em>). No → pronoun (<em>le mien, la mienne</em>), and it needs an article.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="poss-pro-5" data-step="Exemples">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">5</span> Exemples travaillés</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Worked examples</h2>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <p class="example-text">Ton stylo écrit bien ; <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">le mien</span> ne marche plus.</p>
              <p class="gloss">Your pen writes well; mine doesn't work any more.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text"><span class="q-tag">CBSE 2024</span>Peux-tu me prêter <span class="highlight hl-aux">ta</span> trousse ? Je ne trouve pas <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">la mienne</span>.</p>
              <p class="gloss">Can you lend me your pencil case? I can't find mine.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">J'ai fait <span class="highlight hl-aux">mes</span> devoirs. Et toi, as-tu fait <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">les tiens</span> ?</p>
              <p class="gloss">I've done my homework. And you, have you done yours?</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Notre maison est petite mais <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">la vôtre</span> est immense.</p>
              <p class="gloss">Our house is small but yours is huge. — note the circumflex</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="poss-pro-6" data-step="En contexte">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">6</span> En contexte</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">In context — comparing</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">En classe</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Mon cahier est bleu, le tien est rouge.</p>
                <p class="gloss">My exercise book is blue, yours is red.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Ses notes sont meilleures que les miennes.</p>
                <p class="gloss">His/her marks are better than mine.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">L.1 — La famille</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Ma famille est nombreuse ; la sienne est petite.</p>
                <p class="gloss">My family is large; his/hers is small.</p>
                <h3 style="color:var(--gold);">L.6 — Chacun ses goûts</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Tes goûts et les miens sont très différents.</p>
                <p class="gloss">Your tastes and mine are very different.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">💡 <strong>Why it matters:</strong> possessive pronouns let you <strong>compare</strong> without repeating the noun.
              That is exactly the structure the exam tests: one sentence with the adjective, one with the pronoun.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="poss-pro-7" data-step="Pratique QCM">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">7</span> Pratique — QCM</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Choose the correct possessive pronoun</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="la mienne">
                <p class="q-text">1. <span class="q-tag">CBSE 2024</span>Je ne trouve pas _____. <span class="gloss">(ma trousse)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">le mien</button><button class="option-btn">la mienne</button><button class="option-btn">les miennes</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="les tiens">
                <p class="q-text">2. J'ai fait mes devoirs. As-tu fait _____ ?</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">les tiens</button><button class="option-btn">le tien</button><button class="option-btn">les tiennes</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="la nôtre">
                <p class="q-text">3. Votre voiture est neuve ; _____ est vieille.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">la notre</button><button class="option-btn">la nôtre</button><button class="option-btn">le nôtre</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="le sien">
                <p class="q-text">4. Mon vélo est cassé, mais _____ marche bien. <span class="gloss">(le vélo de Paul)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">le sien</button><button class="option-btn">la sienne</button><button class="option-btn">les siens</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="les leurs">
                <p class="q-text">5. Nos résultats sont bons ; _____ aussi. <span class="gloss">(les résultats des autres)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">le leur</button><button class="option-btn">les leurs</button><button class="option-btn">leurs</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="poss-pro-8" data-step="Pratique — à compléter">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">8</span> Pratique — à compléter</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Remplacez par un pronom possessif</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">1. C'est <u>mon livre</u>. → C'est _____.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="le mien" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">2. Ce sont <u>tes clés</u>. → Ce sont _____.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="les tiennes" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">3. C'est <u>sa maison</u>. → C'est _____.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="la sienne" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">4. C'est <u>notre classe</u>. → C'est _____.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="la nôtre" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">5. Ce sont <u>leurs affaires</u>. → Ce sont _____.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="les leurs" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="accent-bar">
                <span class="ab-label">Accents :</span>
                <button class="accent-key">é</button><button class="accent-key">è</button><button class="accent-key">ê</button>
                <button class="accent-key">à</button><button class="accent-key">ç</button><button class="accent-key">ù</button>
                <button class="accent-key">û</button><button class="accent-key">î</button><button class="accent-key">ô</button>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn fib-check student-only">✓ Vérifier</button>
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </section>

      <!-- ================= TOPIC 8 CLOSER ================= -->
      <section data-topic="possessifs" data-topic-name="Les Possessifs" data-sub="Synthèse &amp; Examen">

        <section data-slide-id="poss-fin-1" data-step="Tableau de référence">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">📊 Tableau — adjectif ou pronom ?</h2>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <table class="subj-table">
                <tr><th>Possesseur</th><th>Adjectif (+ nom)</th><th>Pronom (sans nom)</th></tr>
                <tr><td>je</td><td>mon / ma / mes</td><td class="key-form">le mien · la mienne · les miens · les miennes</td></tr>
                <tr><td>tu</td><td>ton / ta / tes</td><td class="key-form">le tien · la tienne · les tiens · les tiennes</td></tr>
                <tr><td>il / elle</td><td>son / sa / ses</td><td class="key-form">le sien · la sienne · les siens · les siennes</td></tr>
                <tr><td>nous</td><td>notre / nos</td><td class="key-form">le nôtre · la nôtre · les nôtres</td></tr>
                <tr><td>vous</td><td>votre / vos</td><td class="key-form">le vôtre · la vôtre · les vôtres</td></tr>
                <tr><td>ils / elles</td><td>leur / leurs</td><td class="key-form">le leur · la leur · les leurs</td></tr>
              </table>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">🔑 <strong>Two rules cover everything:</strong>
                ① agreement follows the <strong>object possessed</strong>, never the owner;
                ② a pronoun always carries its <strong>article</strong> — and <em>nôtre / vôtre</em> take a circumflex.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="poss-fin-2" data-step="Examen CBSE">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">📝 Examen blanc — Les Possessifs</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text"><span class="q-tag">CBSE 2024</span>1. Peux-tu me prêter _____ trousse ? <span class="gloss">(adjectif — tu)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="ta" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text"><span class="q-tag">CBSE 2024</span>2. Je ne trouve pas _____. <span class="gloss">(pronom — ma trousse)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="la mienne" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">3. J'ai fait _____ devoirs. <span class="gloss">(adjectif — je)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="mes" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">4. Et toi, as-tu fait _____ ? <span class="gloss">(pronom — tes devoirs)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="les tiens" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">5. Les élèves ont apporté _____ cahiers. <span class="gloss">(adjectif — ils)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="leurs" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">6. Notre équipe a gagné, mais _____ a perdu. <span class="gloss">(pronom — votre équipe)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="la vôtre" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="accent-bar">
                <span class="ab-label">Accents :</span>
                <button class="accent-key">é</button><button class="accent-key">è</button><button class="accent-key">ê</button>
                <button class="accent-key">à</button><button class="accent-key">ç</button><button class="accent-key">ù</button>
                <button class="accent-key">û</button><button class="accent-key">î</button><button class="accent-key">ô</button>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn fib-check student-only">✓ Vérifier</button>
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 6</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="poss-fin-3" data-step="Check-list">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">✅ Check-list — Les Possessifs</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <p>☐ Is there a <strong>noun</strong> after the gap? → adjective. No noun? → pronoun.</p>
                <p>☐ Did I check the <strong>gender and number of the noun</strong>, not the owner?</p>
                <p>☐ Feminine noun starting with a vowel? → <strong>mon / ton / son</strong>.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <p>☐ Pronoun: did I include the <strong>article</strong> (le / la / les)?</p>
                <p>☐ <em>nôtre / vôtre</em> as pronouns — is the <strong>circumflex</strong> there?</p>
                <p>☐ <em>leur</em> or <em>leurs</em> — how many <strong>objects</strong> are there?</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">🎯 <strong>Exam note:</strong> "Adjectifs et pronoms possessifs" is 5 marks and is usually set as a
              <strong>pair</strong> of gaps — one adjective, one pronoun — often with a word bank. Decide which is which before you choose.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </section>
      <!-- ==================================================================
           TOPIC 9 — LES DÉMONSTRATIFS
           =================================================================== -->
      <section data-topic="demonstratifs" data-topic-name="Les Démonstratifs" data-sub="Adjectifs Démonstratifs">

        <section data-slide-id="dem-adj-1" data-step="Description">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">1</span> Description</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Les Adjectifs Démonstratifs — ce, cet, cette, ces</h2>
            <p class="editable-field">These point at something: "this", "that", "these", "those". They replace the article and always sit <strong>before a noun</strong>.</p>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <table class="subj-table">
                <tr><th>Forme</th><th>Emploi</th><th>Exemple</th></tr>
                <tr><td class="key-form">ce</td><td>masculin + consonne</td><td>ce livre <span class="gloss">this book</span></td></tr>
                <tr><td class="key-form">cet</td><td>masculin + voyelle / h muet</td><td>cet arbre · cet homme</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="key-form">cette</td><td>féminin singulier</td><td>cette maison <span class="gloss">this house</span></td></tr>
                <tr><td class="key-form">ces</td><td>pluriel (m. et f.)</td><td>ces enfants · ces filles</td></tr>
              </table>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">🔑 <strong>French does not distinguish "this" and "that":</strong> <em>ce livre</em> covers both.
              To insist on the difference, add <span class="highlight hl-aux">-ci</span> (here) or <span class="highlight hl-aux">-là</span> (there) — see sub-topic 3.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="dem-adj-2" data-step="Formation">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">2</span> Formation</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">La formule — l'article disparaît</h2>
            <div class="formula-pipeline">
              <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Article</span><span class="f-value">le livre</span></div>
              <div class="f-op">→</div>
              <div class="f-box" style="border-color:var(--purple);"><span class="f-label">Démonstratif</span><span class="f-value" style="color:var(--purple);">ce livre</span></div>
              <div class="f-op">=</div>
              <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Sens</span><span class="f-value">this / that book</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Du défini au démonstratif</h3>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-aux">le</span> garçon → <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">ce</span> garçon</p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-aux">l'</span>ami → <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">cet</span> ami</p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-aux">la</span> fille → <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">cette</span> fille</p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-aux">les</span> livres → <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">ces</span> livres</p>
                <p class="gloss">Never write <em>« ce le livre »</em> — one determiner only.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">CET — uniquement au masculin</h3>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-pronoun">cet</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">homme</span> <span class="gloss">masc., silent h</span></p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-pronoun">cet</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">été</span> <span class="gloss">masc., vowel</span></p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-pronoun">cette</span> <span class="highlight hl-verb">école</span> <span class="gloss">fem. + vowel → still cette</span></p>
                <p class="gloss">⚠️ <em>cet</em> and <em>cette</em> sound the same but are not interchangeable.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="dem-adj-3" data-step="Exceptions">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">3</span> Exceptions</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Les exceptions — expressions de temps</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Le temps proche</h3>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-pronoun">ce</span> matin <span class="gloss">this morning</span></p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-pronoun">cet</span> après-midi <span class="gloss">this afternoon</span></p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-pronoun">ce</span> soir <span class="gloss">this evening</span></p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-pronoun">cette</span> nuit <span class="gloss">tonight / last night</span></p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-pronoun">cette</span> semaine · <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">cette</span> année</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Ne pas confondre CE avec…</h3>
                <p><strong>ce</strong> (démonstratif) + nom :<br>
                  <em><span class="highlight hl-pronoun">ce</span> livre</em> <span class="gloss">this book</span></p>
                <p><strong>ce</strong> (pronom) + être :<br>
                  <em><span class="highlight hl-verb">c'est</span> un livre</em> <span class="gloss">it's a book</span></p>
                <p><strong>se</strong> (pronom réfléchi) :<br>
                  <em>il <span class="highlight hl-neg">se</span> lave</em> <span class="gloss">he washes himself</span></p>
                <p class="gloss">All pronounced alike — a frequent spelling trap.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="dem-adj-4" data-step="Pièges">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">4</span> Pièges</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">⚠️ Trap Alert — CET vs CETTE</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box red content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--crimson);">✗ Wrong</h3>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-neg">Ce</span> homme est mon oncle.</p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-neg">Cette</span> arbre est grand.</p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-neg">Cet</span> école est nouvelle.</p>
                <p class="example-text">J'aime <span class="highlight hl-neg">ce les</span> fleurs.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box green content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--green);">✓ Right</h3>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-verb">Cet</span> homme est mon oncle. <span class="gloss">masc. + silent h</span></p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-verb">Cet</span> arbre est grand. <span class="gloss">arbre is masculine</span></p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-verb">Cette</span> école est nouvelle. <span class="gloss">école is feminine</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">J'aime <span class="highlight hl-verb">ces</span> fleurs. <span class="gloss">one determiner</span></p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">🔑 <strong>Decide in two steps:</strong> ① Is the noun <strong>masculine or feminine</strong>?
              ② If masculine, does it start with a <strong>vowel or silent h</strong>? Only then use <em>cet</em>.
              Feminine is always <em>cette</em>, vowel or not.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="dem-adj-5" data-step="Exemples">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">5</span> Exemples travaillés</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Worked examples</h2>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-pronoun">Ce</span> livre est très intéressant.</p>
              <p class="gloss">This book is very interesting. — livre masc. + consonant</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-pronoun">Cet</span> hôtel est près de la gare.</p>
              <p class="gloss">This hotel is near the station. — hôtel masc. + silent h</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-pronoun">Cette</span> histoire me fait peur.</p>
              <p class="gloss">This story frightens me. — histoire is feminine</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-pronoun">Ces</span> exercices sont difficiles, mais <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">cette</span> leçon est facile.</p>
              <p class="gloss">These exercises are difficult, but this lesson is easy.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="dem-adj-6" data-step="En contexte">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">6</span> En contexte</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">In context — pointing things out</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">L.8 — Faire des achats</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Je voudrais essayer cette robe et ce pantalon.</p>
                <p class="gloss">I'd like to try this dress and these trousers.</p>
                <h3>L.4 — Le plaisir de lire</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Cet auteur écrit très bien.</p>
                <p class="gloss">This author writes very well.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">L.8 — L'environnement</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Ce problème concerne toute la planète.</p>
                <p class="gloss">This problem concerns the whole planet.</p>
                <h3 style="color:var(--gold);">Expressions de temps</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Ce matin, j'ai raté le bus. Ce soir, je resterai à la maison.</p>
                <p class="gloss">This morning I missed the bus. This evening I'll stay at home.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="dem-adj-7" data-step="Pratique QCM">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">7</span> Pratique — QCM</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Choose ce, cet, cette or ces</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="Cet">
                <p class="q-text">1. _____ homme travaille ici.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">Ce</button><button class="option-btn">Cet</button><button class="option-btn">Cette</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="Cette">
                <p class="q-text">2. _____ école est très ancienne.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">Cet</button><button class="option-btn">Cette</button><button class="option-btn">Ces</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="Ces">
                <p class="q-text">3. _____ enfants jouent dans le parc.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">Ce</button><button class="option-btn">Cet</button><button class="option-btn">Ces</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="Ce">
                <p class="q-text">4. _____ garçon est mon cousin.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">Ce</button><button class="option-btn">Cet</button><button class="option-btn">Cette</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="cet">
                <p class="q-text">5. Je pars _____ après-midi.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">ce</button><button class="option-btn">cet</button><button class="option-btn">cette</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="dem-adj-8" data-step="Pratique — à compléter">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">8</span> Pratique — à compléter</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Complétez avec l'adjectif démonstratif</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">1. _____ film est excellent. <span class="gloss">(film — masc.)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="ce" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">2. _____ actrice est célèbre. <span class="gloss">(actrice — fém.)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="cette" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">3. _____ ordinateur ne marche pas. <span class="gloss">(ordinateur — masc., voyelle)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="cet" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">4. _____ fleurs sentent bon. <span class="gloss">(pluriel)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="ces" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">5. <span class="q-tag">CBSE 2024</span>Melissa prend _____ lunettes. <span class="gloss">(pluriel)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="ces" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="accent-bar">
                <span class="ab-label">Accents :</span>
                <button class="accent-key">é</button><button class="accent-key">è</button><button class="accent-key">ê</button>
                <button class="accent-key">à</button><button class="accent-key">ç</button><button class="accent-key">ù</button>
                <button class="accent-key">û</button><button class="accent-key">î</button><button class="accent-key">ô</button>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn fib-check student-only">✓ Vérifier</button>
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </section>

      <!-- ================= 9.2 PRONOMS DÉMONSTRATIFS SIMPLES ================= -->
      <section data-topic="demonstratifs" data-topic-name="Les Démonstratifs" data-sub="Pronoms Simples">

        <section data-slide-id="dem-pro-1" data-step="Description">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">1</span> Description</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Les Pronoms Démonstratifs — celui, celle, ceux, celles</h2>
            <p class="editable-field">These <strong>replace</strong> the noun: "the one", "the ones". They are never used alone — they must be followed by <em>de</em>, a relative pronoun, or <em>-ci / -là</em>.</p>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <table class="subj-table">
                <tr><th></th><th>Masculin</th><th>Féminin</th></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Singulier</strong></td><td class="key-form">celui</td><td class="key-form">celle</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Pluriel</strong></td><td class="key-form">ceux</td><td class="key-form">celles</td></tr>
              </table>
              <p class="example-text" style="margin-top:8px;">Quel livre ? <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">Celui</span> de Paul.</p>
              <p class="gloss">Which book? Paul's one.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">⚠️ <strong>Never alone:</strong> ✗ <em>Je préfère celui.</em> — you must add something:
                <em>celui <span class="highlight hl-aux">de</span> Paul</em> · <em>celui <span class="highlight hl-aux">qui</span> est rouge</em> · <em>celui-<span class="highlight hl-aux">ci</span></em>.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="dem-pro-2" data-step="Formation">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">2</span> Formation</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">La formule — trois continuations possibles</h2>
            <div class="three-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">① + DE (possession)</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Mon livre et <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">celui de</span> Paul.</p>
                <p class="gloss">My book and Paul's.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Ma voiture et <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">celle de</span> ma sœur.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">② + QUI / QUE</h3>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-pronoun">Celui qui</span> parle est mon frère.</p>
                <p class="gloss">The one who is speaking is my brother.</p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-pronoun">Celle que</span> j'ai vue était belle.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box green content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--green);">③ + -CI / -LÀ</h3>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-pronoun">Celui-ci</span> ou <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">celui-là</span> ?</p>
                <p class="gloss">This one or that one?</p>
                <p class="gloss">See sub-topic 3.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field"><strong>L'accord suit le nom remplacé:</strong>
                <em>le livre → <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">celui</span></em> ·
                <em>la robe → <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">celle</span></em> ·
                <em>les livres → <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">ceux</span></em> ·
                <em>les robes → <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">celles</span></em></p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="dem-pro-3" data-step="Exceptions">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">3</span> Exceptions</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Les formes neutres — ce, ceci, cela, ça</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Pour une idée, pas un nom précis</h3>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-pronoun">Ce</span> qui m'intéresse, c'est la musique.</p>
                <p class="gloss">What interests me is music.</p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-pronoun">Ce</span> que tu dis est vrai.</p>
                <p class="gloss">What you say is true.</p>
                <p class="gloss">Neutral <em>ce</em> has no gender — it refers to a whole idea.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">CECI / CELA / ÇA</h3>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-pronoun">Cela</span> m'étonne. <span class="gloss">That surprises me.</span></p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-pronoun">Ça</span> va ? <span class="gloss">How's it going? — informal</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Prends <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">ceci</span>, pas <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">cela</span>.</p>
                <p class="gloss">Take this, not that.</p>
                <p class="gloss"><em>ça</em> is the spoken form of <em>cela</em>.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="dem-pro-4" data-step="Pièges">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">4</span> Pièges</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">⚠️ Trap Alert — adjectif ou pronom ?</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box red content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--crimson);">✗ Wrong</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Je préfère <span class="highlight hl-neg">celui</span>. <span class="gloss">nothing follows</span></p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-neg">Ce</span> de Paul est meilleur.</p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-neg">Celui</span> livre est à moi.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Ma robe et <span class="highlight hl-neg">celui</span> de Marie.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box green content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--green);">✓ Right</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Je préfère <span class="highlight hl-verb">celui-ci</span>. <span class="gloss">-ci added</span></p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-verb">Celui</span> de Paul est meilleur.</p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-verb">Ce</span> livre est à moi. <span class="gloss">adjective + noun</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Ma robe et <span class="highlight hl-verb">celle</span> de Marie. <span class="gloss">robe is feminine</span></p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">🔑 <strong>The distinction:</strong>
                <span class="highlight hl-verb">ce / cet / cette / ces</span> come <strong>before a noun</strong>;
                <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">celui / celle / ceux / celles</span> come <strong>instead of a noun</strong> —
                and are always followed by <em>de</em>, <em>qui/que</em>, or <em>-ci/-là</em>.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="dem-pro-5" data-step="Exemples">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">5</span> Exemples travaillés</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Worked examples</h2>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <p class="example-text">Mon vélo est vieux ; <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">celui de</span> mon frère est neuf.</p>
              <p class="gloss">My bike is old; my brother's is new.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-pronoun">Celles qui</span> veulent participer doivent s'inscrire.</p>
              <p class="gloss">Those (girls) who want to take part must register.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">Parmi tous ces livres, je choisis <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">ceux que</span> tu m'as conseillés.</p>
              <p class="gloss">Among all these books, I choose the ones you recommended.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text"><span class="q-tag">CBSE 2024</span>Melissa prend <span class="highlight hl-aux">ses</span> lunettes. Elle laisse <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">celles</span>-là pour sa sœur.</p>
              <p class="gloss">Melissa takes her glasses. She leaves those ones for her sister.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="dem-pro-6" data-step="En contexte">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">6</span> En contexte</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">In context — comparing and choosing</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">L.8 — Faire des achats</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Cette chemise est jolie, mais celle de la vitrine est moins chère.</p>
                <p class="gloss">This shirt is pretty, but the one in the window is cheaper.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">L.4 — Le plaisir de lire</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Les romans que je préfère sont ceux qui racontent une histoire vraie.</p>
                <p class="gloss">The novels I prefer are the ones that tell a true story.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">💡 <strong>Style tip:</strong> <em>celui de / celle de</em> is how French avoids repeating a noun when comparing —
              <em>ma maison et <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">celle de</span> mon oncle</em> rather than <em>ma maison et la maison de mon oncle</em>.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="dem-pro-7" data-step="Pratique QCM">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">7</span> Pratique — QCM</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Choose the correct demonstrative pronoun</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="celle">
                <p class="q-text">1. Ma voiture et _____ de Paul. <span class="gloss">(voiture — fém.)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">celui</button><button class="option-btn">celle</button><button class="option-btn">ceux</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="ceux">
                <p class="q-text">2. Mes livres et _____ de mon frère. <span class="gloss">(livres — masc. plur.)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">celles</button><button class="option-btn">ceux</button><button class="option-btn">celui</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="Celui qui">
                <p class="q-text">3. _____ chante bien, c'est mon cousin.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">Celui qui</button><button class="option-btn">Celui que</button><button class="option-btn">Ce qui</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="Ce que">
                <p class="q-text">4. _____ tu dis est intéressant. <span class="gloss">(une idée)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">Celui que</button><button class="option-btn">Ce que</button><button class="option-btn">Celle que</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="celles">
                <p class="q-text">5. <span class="q-tag">CBSE 2024</span>Elle laisse _____-là pour sa sœur. <span class="gloss">(les lunettes)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">ceux</button><button class="option-btn">celles</button><button class="option-btn">celle</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="dem-pro-8" data-step="Pratique — à compléter">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">8</span> Pratique — à compléter</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Complétez avec celui / celle / ceux / celles</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">1. Mon stylo et _____ de Marie. <span class="gloss">(stylo — masc.)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="celui" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">2. Ta maison et _____ de tes parents. <span class="gloss">(maison — fém.)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="celle" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">3. _____ qui travaillent réussissent. <span class="gloss">(les élèves — masc. plur.)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="ceux" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">4. Ces photos sont plus belles que _____ de l'année dernière.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="celles" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">5. _____ que j'ai acheté est très bon. <span class="gloss">(le gâteau)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="celui" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="accent-bar">
                <span class="ab-label">Accents :</span>
                <button class="accent-key">é</button><button class="accent-key">è</button><button class="accent-key">ê</button>
                <button class="accent-key">à</button><button class="accent-key">ç</button><button class="accent-key">ù</button>
                <button class="accent-key">û</button><button class="accent-key">î</button><button class="accent-key">ô</button>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn fib-check student-only">✓ Vérifier</button>
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </section>

      <!-- ================= 9.3 PRONOMS COMPOSÉS -CI / -LÀ ================= -->
      <section data-topic="demonstratifs" data-topic-name="Les Démonstratifs" data-sub="Pronoms Composés (-ci / -là)">

        <section data-slide-id="dem-comp-1" data-step="Description">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">1</span> Description</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Les Pronoms Composés — celui-ci, celui-là</h2>
            <p class="editable-field">Adding <strong>-ci</strong> or <strong>-là</strong> creates a contrast between what is <strong>near</strong> and what is <strong>far</strong> — "this one" vs "that one".</p>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <table class="subj-table">
                <tr><th></th><th>Ici (-ci)</th><th>Là-bas (-là)</th></tr>
                <tr><td>masc. sing.</td><td class="key-form">celui-ci</td><td class="key-form">celui-là</td></tr>
                <tr><td>fém. sing.</td><td class="key-form">celle-ci</td><td class="key-form">celle-là</td></tr>
                <tr><td>masc. plur.</td><td class="key-form">ceux-ci</td><td class="key-form">ceux-là</td></tr>
                <tr><td>fém. plur.</td><td class="key-form">celles-ci</td><td class="key-form">celles-là</td></tr>
              </table>
              <p class="example-text" style="margin-top:8px;">Quelle robe préfères-tu ? <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">Celle-ci</span> ou <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">celle-là</span> ?</p>
              <p class="gloss">Which dress do you prefer? This one or that one?</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="dem-comp-2" data-step="Formation">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">2</span> Formation</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">La formule — pronom + trait d'union + ci/là</h2>
            <div class="formula-pipeline">
              <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Pronom</span><span class="f-value">celui</span></div>
              <div class="f-op">-</div>
              <div class="f-box" style="border-color:var(--purple);"><span class="f-label">ci / là</span><span class="f-value" style="color:var(--purple);">ci</span></div>
              <div class="f-op">=</div>
              <div class="f-box"><span class="f-label">Composé</span><span class="f-value">celui-ci</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Avec l'adjectif aussi</h3>
                <p>The same <em>-ci / -là</em> can be attached to a noun preceded by a demonstrative adjective:</p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-pronoun">ce</span> livre-<span class="highlight hl-aux">ci</span> <span class="gloss">this book (here)</span></p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-pronoun">cette</span> robe-<span class="highlight hl-aux">là</span> <span class="gloss">that dress (there)</span></p>
                <p class="gloss">The hyphen goes after the <strong>noun</strong>, not the adjective.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Le trait d'union est obligatoire</h3>
                <p class="example-text">✓ celui<span class="highlight hl-aux">-</span>ci &nbsp;·&nbsp; ✗ <em>celui ci</em></p>
                <p class="example-text">✓ ce livre<span class="highlight hl-aux">-</span>là &nbsp;·&nbsp; ✗ <em>ce livre là</em></p>
                <p class="gloss">Without the hyphen it is simply wrong.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="dem-comp-3" data-step="Exceptions">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">3</span> Exceptions</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Les emplois particuliers</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">« Le dernier » et « le premier »</h3>
                <p>In a sentence naming two things, <em>celui-ci</em> refers to the <strong>last mentioned</strong> and <em>celui-là</em> to the <strong>first</strong>:</p>
                <p class="example-text">Paul et Marc sont venus ; <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">celui-ci</span> est resté, <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">celui-là</span> est parti.</p>
                <p class="gloss">Paul and Marc came; the latter (Marc) stayed, the former (Paul) left.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">En pratique, « -là » domine</h3>
                <p>In everyday French, <em>-là</em> is used far more than <em>-ci</em>, even for near objects:</p>
                <p class="example-text">Je prends <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">celui-là</span>.</p>
                <p class="gloss">I'll take that one.</p>
                <p class="gloss">Use <em>-ci</em> mainly when you explicitly contrast two items.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field"><strong>Neutre:</strong> <em>ceci</em> and <em>cela</em> are the neutral equivalents —
              <em>Prends <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">ceci</span>, laisse <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">cela</span>.</em> Note they are written as <strong>one word</strong>, with no hyphen.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="dem-comp-4" data-step="Pièges">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">4</span> Pièges</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">⚠️ Trap Alert — agreement and hyphen</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box red content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--crimson);">✗ Wrong</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Ces robes ? Je préfère <span class="highlight hl-neg">celui-ci</span>.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Je prends <span class="highlight hl-neg">celui ci</span>.</p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-neg">Ce-ci</span> livre est à moi.</p>
                <p class="example-text">Elle laisse <span class="highlight hl-neg">ceux</span>-là. <span class="gloss">(les lunettes = fém.)</span></p>
              </div>
              <div class="box green content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--green);">✓ Right</h3>
                <p class="example-text">Ces robes ? Je préfère <span class="highlight hl-verb">celles-ci</span>. <span class="gloss">fem. plural</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Je prends <span class="highlight hl-verb">celui-ci</span>. <span class="gloss">hyphen</span></p>
                <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-verb">Ce livre-ci</span> est à moi. <span class="gloss">-ci after the noun</span></p>
                <p class="example-text">Elle laisse <span class="highlight hl-verb">celles</span>-là. <span class="gloss">lunettes is feminine plural</span></p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">🔑 <strong>Three checks:</strong> ① what noun is replaced, ② its <strong>gender and number</strong>,
              ③ the <strong>hyphen</strong> before ci/là. Watch out for nouns that are plural in French: <em>les lunettes</em> (f. pl.), <em>les vacances</em> (f. pl.).</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="dem-comp-5" data-step="Exemples">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">5</span> Exemples travaillés</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Worked examples</h2>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <p class="example-text">Ces deux livres sont bien. <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">Celui-ci</span> est plus court que <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">celui-là</span>.</p>
              <p class="gloss">These two books are good. This one is shorter than that one.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text">— Quelles chaussures veux-tu ? — <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">Celles-là</span>, s'il vous plaît.</p>
              <p class="gloss">— Which shoes do you want? — Those ones, please.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text"><span class="highlight hl-pronoun">Ce</span> gâteau-<span class="highlight hl-aux">ci</span> est au chocolat ; <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">ce</span> gâteau-<span class="highlight hl-aux">là</span> est à la vanille.</p>
              <p class="gloss">This cake is chocolate; that cake is vanilla. — adjective + noun + ci/là</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="example-text"><span class="q-tag">CBSE 2024</span>Melissa prend ses lunettes. Elle laisse <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">celles-là</span> pour sa sœur.</p>
              <p class="gloss">Melissa takes her glasses. She leaves those ones for her sister.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="dem-comp-6" data-step="En contexte">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">6</span> En contexte</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">In context — making a choice in a shop</h2>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <h3 style="margin-top:0;">L.8 — Faire des achats</h3>
              <p class="example-text">— Bonjour, je cherche une écharpe.<br>
                 — Nous avons <strong>celle-ci</strong> en laine et <strong>celle-là</strong> en soie.<br>
                 — Je préfère <strong>celle-ci</strong>. Combien coûte-t-elle ?</p>
              <p class="gloss">— Hello, I'm looking for a scarf. — We have this one in wool and that one in silk. — I prefer this one. How much is it?</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">💡 <strong>Role-play tip:</strong> shop dialogues are a standard CBSE short-composition task.
              <em>celui-ci / celle-là</em> plus <em>combien coûte…?</em> gives you a natural, correct exchange in two lines.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="dem-comp-7" data-step="Pratique QCM">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">7</span> Pratique — QCM</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Choose the correct compound form</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="celle-ci">
                <p class="q-text">1. Quelle robe ? _____ ou celle-là ? <span class="gloss">(robe — fém.)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">celui-ci</button><button class="option-btn">celle-ci</button><button class="option-btn">celles-ci</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="ceux-là">
                <p class="q-text">2. Ces gâteaux ? Je prends _____. <span class="gloss">(masc. plur.)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">celles-là</button><button class="option-btn">ceux-là</button><button class="option-btn">celui-là</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="celles-là">
                <p class="q-text">3. <span class="q-tag">CBSE 2024</span>Elle laisse _____ pour sa sœur. <span class="gloss">(les lunettes — fém. plur.)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">ceux-là</button><button class="option-btn">celles-là</button><button class="option-btn">celle-là</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="ce livre-ci">
                <p class="q-text">4. Je préfère _____ à celui-là.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">ce-ci livre</button><button class="option-btn">ce livre-ci</button><button class="option-btn">celui livre-ci</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="celui-ci">
                <p class="q-text">5. Deux stylos : _____ écrit mieux que celui-là.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">celui-ci</button><button class="option-btn">celle-ci</button><button class="option-btn">ceci</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="dem-comp-8" data-step="Pratique — à compléter">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <div class="step-ribbon"><span class="sr-n">8</span> Pratique — à compléter</div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">Complétez avec un pronom composé</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">1. Quel pull ? _____ ou celui-là ? <span class="gloss">(masc. sing., ici)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="celui-ci" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">2. Ces fleurs sont belles ; je prends _____. <span class="gloss">(fém. plur., ici)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="celles-ci" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">3. Ces exercices ? Faites _____. <span class="gloss">(masc. plur., là)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="ceux-là" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">4. Cette maison-ci est neuve ; _____ est ancienne. <span class="gloss">(fém. sing., là)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="celle-là" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">5. Prends _____, laisse cela. <span class="gloss">(neutre, ici)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="ceci" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="accent-bar">
                <span class="ab-label">Accents :</span>
                <button class="accent-key">é</button><button class="accent-key">è</button><button class="accent-key">ê</button>
                <button class="accent-key">à</button><button class="accent-key">ç</button><button class="accent-key">ù</button>
                <button class="accent-key">û</button><button class="accent-key">î</button><button class="accent-key">ô</button>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn fib-check student-only">✓ Vérifier</button>
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 5</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </section>

      <!-- ================= TOPIC 9 CLOSER ================= -->
      <section data-topic="demonstratifs" data-topic-name="Les Démonstratifs" data-sub="Synthèse &amp; Examen">

        <section data-slide-id="dem-fin-1" data-step="Tableau de référence">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">📊 Tableau — adjectifs et pronoms démonstratifs</h2>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <table class="subj-table">
                <tr><th></th><th>Adjectif (+ nom)</th><th>Pronom simple</th><th>Pronom composé</th></tr>
                <tr><td>masc. sing.</td><td class="key-form">ce (cet)</td><td class="key-form">celui</td><td class="key-form">celui-ci / celui-là</td></tr>
                <tr><td>fém. sing.</td><td class="key-form">cette</td><td class="key-form">celle</td><td class="key-form">celle-ci / celle-là</td></tr>
                <tr><td>masc. plur.</td><td class="key-form">ces</td><td class="key-form">ceux</td><td class="key-form">ceux-ci / ceux-là</td></tr>
                <tr><td>fém. plur.</td><td class="key-form">ces</td><td class="key-form">celles</td><td class="key-form">celles-ci / celles-là</td></tr>
                <tr><td>neutre</td><td>—</td><td class="key-form">ce (ce qui / ce que)</td><td class="key-form">ceci / cela / ça</td></tr>
              </table>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">🔑 <strong>Trois règles:</strong>
                ① <em>cet</em> only before a masculine noun starting with a vowel or silent h;
                ② a simple pronoun is never alone — add <em>de</em>, <em>qui/que</em> or <em>-ci/-là</em>;
                ③ everything agrees with the noun being replaced.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="dem-fin-2" data-step="Examen CBSE">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">📝 Examen blanc — Les Démonstratifs</h2>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text"><span class="q-tag">CBSE 2024</span>1. Melissa prend _____ lunettes. <span class="gloss">(adjectif possessif — elle)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="ses" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text"><span class="q-tag">CBSE 2024</span>2. Elle laisse _____-là pour sa sœur. <span class="gloss">(pronom démonstratif)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="celles" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">3. _____ homme est mon professeur.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="cet" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">4. _____ école est très grande.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="cette" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">5. Mon vélo et _____ de mon frère sont neufs.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="celui" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">6. Ces deux robes : je préfère _____. <span class="gloss">(fém. sing., ici)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="celle-ci" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="accent-bar">
                <span class="ab-label">Accents :</span>
                <button class="accent-key">é</button><button class="accent-key">è</button><button class="accent-key">ê</button>
                <button class="accent-key">à</button><button class="accent-key">ç</button><button class="accent-key">ù</button>
                <button class="accent-key">û</button><button class="accent-key">î</button><button class="accent-key">ô</button>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn fib-check student-only">✓ Vérifier</button>
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 6</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="dem-fin-3" data-step="Check-list">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">✅ Check-list — Les Démonstratifs</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <p>☐ Is there a <strong>noun</strong> after the gap? → adjective (ce / cet / cette / ces).</p>
                <p>☐ Masculine noun starting with a <strong>vowel or silent h</strong>? → <strong>cet</strong>.</p>
                <p>☐ Feminine, vowel or not? → always <strong>cette</strong>.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <p>☐ No noun? → pronoun (celui / celle / ceux / celles).</p>
                <p>☐ Is the pronoun <strong>followed by something</strong> — de, qui/que, or -ci/-là?</p>
                <p>☐ Compound form: is the <strong>hyphen</strong> there, and does it agree?</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">🎯 <strong>Exam note:</strong> "Adjectifs et pronoms démonstratifs" is 5 marks and, like the possessives,
              is usually set as a <strong>pair</strong> — one adjective, one pronoun, in consecutive sentences.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </section>
      <!-- ==================================================================
           RÉVISION MIXTE — interleaved practice across all 9 topics
           =================================================================== -->
      <section data-topic="revision" data-topic-name="Révision Mixte" data-sub="Entraînement Final">

        <section data-slide-id="rev-1" data-step="Pourquoi mélanger">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <svg class="svg-badge" viewBox="0 0 100 100" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
              <circle cx="50" cy="50" r="45" fill="#002395" stroke="#ED2939" stroke-width="4"/>
              <path d="M30 45 L50 25 L70 45 L50 75 Z" fill="#ffffff"/>
            </svg>
            <h2 class="editable-field">🎯 Révision Mixte — why mixing matters</h2>
            <p class="editable-field">Until now every exercise told you which rule to apply. <strong>The board exam does not.</strong> This section removes the labels.</p>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box red content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--crimson);">Practising one topic at a time</h3>
                <p>Feels easy — you already know the answer is a subjunctive, so you only have to conjugate.</p>
                <p class="gloss">This is <strong>blocked practice</strong>. It builds confidence but hides the hardest skill.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box green content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--green);">Practising everything mixed up</h3>
                <p>Feels harder — you must first <strong>identify</strong> what is being tested, then apply the rule.</p>
                <p class="gloss">This is <strong>interleaved practice</strong>. It feels worse and works better, because it trains the exact skill the exam measures.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">🔑 <strong>The two-step habit:</strong> ① <em>What is this question testing?</em> ② <em>What is the rule?</em><br>
              Students who skip step ① lose marks even when they know the grammar perfectly.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="rev-2" data-step="Identifier le sujet">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">🔍 Step 1 — recognise the topic from the clue</h2>
            <div class="box blue content-box">
              <table class="subj-table">
                <tr><th>Ce que vous voyez</th><th>Le sujet testé</th></tr>
                <tr><td>un infinitif entre parenthèses — <em>(aller)</em></td><td class="key-form">Les Verbes</td></tr>
                <tr><td><em>il faut que · bien que · je veux que</em></td><td class="key-form">Le Subjonctif</td></tr>
                <tr><td>« mettez à la forme négative »</td><td class="key-form">La Négation</td></tr>
                <tr><td>un mot souligné à remplacer</td><td class="key-form">Les Pronoms</td></tr>
                <tr><td>deux phrases à relier</td><td class="key-form">Les Pronoms Relatifs</td></tr>
                <tr><td>des guillemets « … »</td><td class="key-form">Le Discours Indirect</td></tr>
                <tr><td>une réponse donnée, il manque la question</td><td class="key-form">Trouvez la Question</td></tr>
                <tr><td>un trou devant un nom (mon/ma/ton…)</td><td class="key-form">Les Possessifs</td></tr>
                <tr><td>ce · cet · cette · celui · celle</td><td class="key-form">Les Démonstratifs</td></tr>
              </table>
            </div>
            <div class="box gold content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">💡 Spend <strong>five seconds</strong> identifying the topic before you write anything. It is the cheapest mark on the paper.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="rev-3" data-step="Mélange 1 — QCM">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">🎲 Mélange 1 — nine topics, no labels</h2>
            <p class="editable-field gloss">Each question tests a different topic. Identify it first, then answer.</p>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="soit">
                <p class="q-text">1. Il faut que tu _____ à l'heure.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">es</button><button class="option-btn">soit</button><button class="option-btn">sois</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="qui">
                <p class="q-text">2. La femme _____ chante est ma tante.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">qui</button><button class="option-btn">que</button><button class="option-btn">dont</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="n'ai vu personne">
                <p class="q-text">3. Je _____ à la fête.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">n'ai personne vu</button><button class="option-btn">n'ai vu personne</button><button class="option-btn">n'ai rien vu personne</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="lui">
                <p class="q-text">4. Je téléphone à ma mère. → Je _____ téléphone.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">la</button><button class="option-btn">lui</button><button class="option-btn">y</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="Cet">
                <p class="q-text">5. _____ homme travaille avec mon père.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">Ce</button><button class="option-btn">Cet</button><button class="option-btn">Cette</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="de ne pas partir">
                <p class="q-text">6. « Ne pars pas ! » → Il me dit _____.</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">que je ne pars pas</button><button class="option-btn">de ne pas partir</button><button class="option-btn">de ne partir pas</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="achèteront">
                <p class="q-text">7. Mes parents _____ une voiture le mois prochain. <span class="gloss">(acheter)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">acheteront</button><button class="option-btn">achèteront</button><button class="option-btn">achetaient</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="la mienne">
                <p class="q-text">8. Je ne trouve pas _____. <span class="gloss">(ma trousse)</span></p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">le mien</button><button class="option-btn">la mienne</button><button class="option-btn">les miennes</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row" data-answer="Combien de">
                <p class="q-text">9. <em>J'ai deux frères.</em> → _____ frères as-tu ?</p>
                <div class="options"><button class="option-btn">Combien de</button><button class="option-btn">Combien des</button><button class="option-btn">Quel</button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 9</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="rev-4" data-step="Mélange 2 — à compléter">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">🎲 Mélange 2 — écrivez la réponse</h2>
            <p class="editable-field gloss">Authentic CBSE questions, deliberately shuffled across topics.</p>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text"><span class="q-tag">CBSE 2022</span>1. En 2021, nous _____ (étudier) souvent en ligne.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="étudiions" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text"><span class="q-tag">CBSE 2024</span>2. Elle a bien réussi au contrôle _____ elle avait fait bien attention.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="auquel" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text"><span class="q-tag">CBSE 2024</span>3. Tout le monde sait nager ? → _____ sait nager. <span class="gloss">(personne)</span></p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="personne ne" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text"><span class="q-tag">CBSE 2024</span>4. Il est important que nous _____ (pouvoir) assister à cette fête.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="puissions" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text"><span class="q-tag">CBSE 2022</span>5. Dès que l'acteur _____ (revenir), le réalisateur racontera l'histoire.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="sera revenu" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text"><span class="q-tag">CBSE 2019</span>6. <em>Miriam arrive <u>demain</u>.</em> → _____ est-ce que Miriam arrive ?</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="quand" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text"><span class="q-tag">CBSE 2024</span>7. Son père lui dit : « Ne va pas seul. » → Son père lui dit _____ seul.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="de ne pas aller" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text"><span class="q-tag">CBSE 2024</span>8. Melissa prend ses lunettes. Elle laisse _____-là pour sa sœur.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="celles" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text"><span class="q-tag">CBSE 2022</span>9. L'année dernière, elles _____ (se rencontrer) dans la rue.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="se sont rencontrées" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">10. Je vais <u>au marché</u>. → J'_____ vais.</p>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="y" placeholder="votre réponse"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="accent-bar">
                <span class="ab-label">Accents :</span>
                <button class="accent-key">é</button><button class="accent-key">è</button><button class="accent-key">ê</button>
                <button class="accent-key">à</button><button class="accent-key">ç</button><button class="accent-key">ù</button>
                <button class="accent-key">û</button><button class="accent-key">î</button><button class="accent-key">ô</button>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn fib-check student-only">✓ Vérifier</button>
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Afficher les réponses</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Recommencer</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 10</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="rev-5" data-step="Les pièges les plus coûteux">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">⚠️ The nine traps that cost the most marks</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box red content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--crimson);">Verbes &amp; Subjonctif</h3>
                <p>① <strong>être ou avoir ?</strong> — et l'accord du participe après <em>être</em>.</p>
                <p>② <strong>Si + imparfait → conditionnel</strong> — jamais <em>si j'aurais</em>.</p>
                <p>③ <strong>espérer que</strong> → indicatif, pas subjonctif.</p>
                <p>④ <strong>quand + futur</strong> en français, présent en anglais.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">Pronoms, négation, démonstratifs</h3>
                <p>⑤ <strong>rien</strong> avant le participe, <strong>personne</strong> après.</p>
                <p>⑥ <strong>ne… que</strong> garde l'article ; <strong>ni… ni</strong> le supprime.</p>
                <p>⑦ <strong>qui</strong> + verbe · <strong>que</strong> + sujet + verbe.</p>
                <p>⑧ <strong>cet</strong> (masc. + voyelle) vs <strong>cette</strong> (fém.).</p>
                <p>⑨ Le possessif s'accorde avec <strong>l'objet</strong>, pas le possesseur.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">💡 <strong>Revision method:</strong> go back through the topics and re-read only the
              <span class="step-ribbon" style="margin:0; padding:2px 8px;"><span class="sr-n">4</span> Pièges</span> slides.
              Nine slides, and they cover the errors that actually lose marks.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="rev-6" data-step="Stratégie de l'examen">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">📋 Section C — how the 30 marks are won</h2>
            <div class="two-columns">
              <div class="box blue content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0;">La structure</h3>
                <p><strong>Les Verbes — OBLIGATOIRE</strong> · 5 marks</p>
                <p class="gloss">You cannot avoid this question. It is worth a sixth of the section on its own.</p>
                <p><strong>Puis 5 sujets sur 6 restants</strong> · 25 marks</p>
                <p class="gloss">Négation · Pronoms · Relatifs · Discours · Trouvez la question · Possessifs · Démonstratifs · Subjonctif</p>
                <p><strong>Total : 30 marks</strong></p>
              </div>
              <div class="box gold content-box">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0; color:var(--gold);">La stratégie</h3>
                <p>① <strong>Do the verbs first</strong> — it is compulsory and you have practised it most.</p>
                <p>② <strong>Read all the optional questions</strong> before choosing. Pick the five you are surest of.</p>
                <p>③ <strong>Leave the hardest for last</strong>, but attempt it — partial marks exist.</p>
                <p>④ <strong>Re-read every answer</strong> for accents and agreement. That is where two or three marks hide.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="box green content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">🎯 <strong>Le calcul:</strong> Section C is <strong>30 of 80 marks</strong> — more than reading and more than culture.
              It is also the most <strong>predictable</strong> section, because the rules never change. Marks here are the easiest to secure in the whole paper.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- CBSE clue-word mixed tenses — no tense named; deduce from the highlighted clue -->
        <section data-slide-id="rev-clue-1" data-step="Mixed Tenses — clue words (1)">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">🕵️ Mettez les verbes au temps convenable</h2>
            <p class="editable-field gloss">Exactly like the board: <strong>no tense is named</strong>. Read the <span class="clue">highlighted clue word</span>, decide the tense, then conjugate. Stuck? Press <strong>💡 Hint</strong>.</p>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">1. <span class="clue">Hier</span>, il _____ (finir) ses devoirs. <button class="hint-btn" type="button">💡 Hint</button></p>
                <div class="hint-box" hidden><strong>hier</strong> = yesterday → one finished past action → use the <strong>Passé Composé</strong>.</div>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="a fini" placeholder="your answer"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">2. <span class="clue">Demain</span>, nous _____ (partir) en voyage. <button class="hint-btn" type="button">💡 Hint</button></p>
                <div class="hint-box" hidden><strong>demain</strong> = tomorrow → a future plan → use the <strong>Futur Simple</strong>.</div>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="partirons" placeholder="your answer"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">3. <span class="clue">Quand j'étais petit</span>, je _____ (jouer) au foot. <button class="hint-btn" type="button">💡 Hint</button></p>
                <div class="hint-box" hidden><strong>quand j'étais petit</strong> = a repeated past habit / background → use the <strong>Imparfait</strong>.</div>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="jouais" placeholder="your answer"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">4. <span class="clue">Tous les jours</span>, elle _____ (prendre) le bus. <button class="hint-btn" type="button">💡 Hint</button></p>
                <div class="hint-box" hidden><strong>tous les jours</strong> = a habit true now (no past marker) → use the <strong>Présent</strong>.</div>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="prend" placeholder="your answer"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">5. <span class="clue">Dès qu'</span>il _____ (finir), il sortira. <button class="hint-btn" type="button">💡 Hint</button></p>
                <div class="hint-box" hidden><strong>dès que</strong> + an action completed <em>before</em> another future action → use the <strong>Futur Antérieur</strong> (aura + participle).</div>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="aura fini" placeholder="your answer"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">6. <span class="clue">Si</span> j'<span class="clue">avais</span> de l'argent, je _____ (voyager). <button class="hint-btn" type="button">💡 Hint</button></p>
                <div class="hint-box" hidden><strong>si + imparfait</strong> → the main clause takes the <strong>Conditionnel présent</strong> (never <em>si j'aurais</em>).</div>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="voyagerais" placeholder="your answer"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="accent-bar">
                <span class="ab-label">Accents :</span>
                <button class="accent-key">é</button><button class="accent-key">è</button><button class="accent-key">ê</button>
                <button class="accent-key">à</button><button class="accent-key">ç</button><button class="accent-key">ù</button>
                <button class="accent-key">û</button><button class="accent-key">î</button><button class="accent-key">ô</button>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn fib-check student-only">✓ Check</button>
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Show answers</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Retry</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 6</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="rev-clue-2" data-step="Mixed Tenses — clue words (2)">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <h2 class="editable-field">🕵️ Mettez les verbes au temps convenable</h2>
            <p class="editable-field gloss">Same drill — spot the <span class="clue">clue</span>, deduce the tense, conjugate. These mix past, present, future, plus-que-parfait and subjunctive.</p>
            <div class="quiz-container">
              <div class="quiz-progress-bar"><div class="quiz-progress-fill"></div></div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">1. <span class="clue">En ce moment</span>, les enfants _____ (dormir). <button class="hint-btn" type="button">💡 Hint</button></p>
                <div class="hint-box" hidden><strong>en ce moment</strong> = right now → use the <strong>Présent</strong>.</div>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="dorment" placeholder="your answer"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">2. <span class="clue">La semaine dernière</span>, nous _____ (visiter) le musée. <button class="hint-btn" type="button">💡 Hint</button></p>
                <div class="hint-box" hidden><strong>la semaine dernière</strong> = last week, finished → use the <strong>Passé Composé</strong>.</div>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="avons visité" placeholder="your answer"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">3. <span class="clue">Autrefois</span>, les gens _____ (écrire) des lettres. <button class="hint-btn" type="button">💡 Hint</button></p>
                <div class="hint-box" hidden><strong>autrefois</strong> = in the old days, habitually → use the <strong>Imparfait</strong>.</div>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="écrivaient" placeholder="your answer"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">4. Quand je suis arrivé, il _____ <span class="clue">déjà</span> (partir). <button class="hint-btn" type="button">💡 Hint</button></p>
                <div class="hint-box" hidden><strong>déjà</strong> + an action finished <em>before</em> another past action → use the <strong>Plus-que-parfait</strong> (était + participle). Remember <em>partir</em> takes <em>être</em>.</div>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="était déjà parti" placeholder="your answer"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">5. <span class="clue">Si</span> tu <span class="clue">viens</span>, je _____ (être) content. <button class="hint-btn" type="button">💡 Hint</button></p>
                <div class="hint-box" hidden><strong>si + présent</strong> → the main clause takes the <strong>Futur Simple</strong>.</div>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="serai" placeholder="your answer"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="question-row">
                <p class="q-text">6. <span class="clue">Il faut que</span> tu _____ (être) à l'heure. <button class="hint-btn" type="button">💡 Hint</button></p>
                <div class="hint-box" hidden><strong>il faut que</strong> is a subjunctive trigger → use the <strong>Subjonctif</strong> (être → sois).</div>
                <input class="fib-input" data-answer="sois" placeholder="your answer"><span class="fib-verdict"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="accent-bar">
                <span class="ab-label">Accents :</span>
                <button class="accent-key">é</button><button class="accent-key">è</button><button class="accent-key">ê</button>
                <button class="accent-key">à</button><button class="accent-key">ç</button><button class="accent-key">ù</button>
                <button class="accent-key">û</button><button class="accent-key">î</button><button class="accent-key">ô</button>
              </div>
              <div class="fib-actions">
                <button class="tb-btn fib-check student-only">✓ Check</button>
                <button class="tb-btn reveal-answers teacher-only">👁️ Show answers</button>
                <button class="retry-btn student-only">🔄 Retry</button>
                <span class="score-display">Score : 0 / 6</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section data-slide-id="rev-7" data-step="Bonne chance">
          <div class="slide-card">
            <div class="flag-stripe"></div>
            <svg class="svg-badge" viewBox="0 0 100 100" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
              <circle cx="50" cy="50" r="45" fill="#002395" stroke="#ED2939" stroke-width="4"/>
              <path d="M30 45 L50 25 L70 45 L50 75 Z" fill="#ffffff"/>
            </svg>
            <h1 class="editable-field">Bonne chance ! 🇫🇷</h1>
            <div class="box gold content-box">
              <p class="editable-field" style="font-weight:800; color:var(--heading-color);">Vous avez travaillé :</p>
              <div style="display:flex; gap:7px; justify-content:center; flex-wrap:wrap; margin:8px 0;">
                <span class="highlight hl-verb">Les Verbes</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">Le Subjonctif</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-neg">La Négation</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-pronoun">Les Pronoms</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-subject">Les Relatifs</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">Le Discours</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-subject">L'Interrogation</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-verb">Les Possessifs</span>
                <span class="highlight hl-aux">Les Démonstratifs</span>
              </div>
              <p class="editable-field">— <strong>49 règles</strong>, chacune expliquée, illustrée et pratiquée.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="box blue content-box fragment">
              <p class="editable-field">📌 <strong>Pour réviser seul :</strong> utilisez <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>K</kbd> pour retrouver une règle,
              le mode <strong>🎓 Student</strong> pour refaire les exercices, et 🖨️ pour imprimer un thème en fiche de révision.</p>
            </div>
            <p class="editable-field gloss">« La grammaire n'est pas une montagne : c'est un escalier. Une marche à la fois. »</p>
          </div>
        </section>
      </section>
    </div><!-- /.slides -->
  </div><!-- /.reveal -->
</div><!-- /.reveal-shell -->

<div class="topic-progress" id="topicProgress" style="width:0"></div>
<div class="step-hint" id="stepHint"></div>

<div class="hud">
  <span class="step-group">
    <button class="nav-btn" id="prevBtn" title="Previous step / slide (←, PgUp)">◄ Back</button>
    <button class="nav-btn" id="nextBtn" title="Reveal next step, then next slide (→, Space, PgDn)">Next ►</button>
  </span>
  <span class="slide-counter" id="slideCounter">—</span>
  <button class="nav-btn" id="projectorBtn2" title="Projector / Fullscreen mode (P)">📺 Projector</button>
  <button class="nav-btn" id="fsBtn" title="Fullscreen (F)">⛶</button>
</div>

